// New recipes written for Rose's EATS (v3). [id,title,cat,emoji,minutes,difficulty,cozy,serves,desc,ingredients(;),steps(|),cuisine]
const NEWR=[[3001,"Macarona Bechamel","comfort","🍝",75,"Medium",9,8,"Egypt's beloved baked pasta layered with spiced beef sauce and a creamy golden bechamel.","1 lb|penne;1 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;4 tbsp|butter;1/2 cup|flour;4 cup|milk;2|eggs|beaten;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Boil the penne 2 minutes short of the package time, drain and toss with a spoon of butter.|Brown the ground beef with the onion in a skillet over medium-high heat for 8 minutes, then add garlic, cinnamon, salt and pepper.|Stir in the tomato sauce and simmer the meat sauce 10 minutes until thick.|For the bechamel, melt the butter, whisk in the flour and cook 2 minutes, then slowly whisk in the milk and cook until thick, about 8 minutes. Season with salt, pepper and nutmeg, cool slightly, then whisk in the eggs.|Heat the oven to 375°F. Spread half the penne in a 9x13 dish, cover with the meat sauce, then top with the remaining penne.|Pour the bechamel over everything, sprinkle with parmesan and bake 30 to 35 minutes until golden. Rest 10 minutes before cutting.","Egyptian"],
[3002,"Hawawshi","lunch","🥙",50,"Easy",8,4,"Crisp baked pita stuffed with spiced minced beef, onion and herbs, a classic Egyptian street sandwich.","1 lb|ground beef;1|onion|finely grated;1|bell pepper|finely diced;1/2 cup|parsley|chopped;1|tomatoes|finely diced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;4|pita|large rounds","Heat the oven to 425°F.|Mix the beef, onion, pepper, parsley, tomato, cumin, paprika, black pepper and salt with your hands until well combined.|Cut each pita open along one edge to make a pocket and stuff with a quarter of the meat, pressing it flat to the edges.|Brush both sides of each pita with oil and place on a baking sheet.|Bake 15 minutes, flip, and bake another 8 to 10 minutes until the bread is crisp and the meat is cooked through.|Rest 3 minutes, cut into wedges and serve with tahini or a tomato salad.","Egyptian"],
[3003,"Mahshi (Egyptian Stuffed Vegetables)","comfort","🥒",120,"Medium",9,6,"Zucchini and peppers filled with herbed tomato rice and simmered in a light tomato sauce.","1 1/2 cup|rice|short grain, rinsed;6|zucchini|small, cored;3|bell pepper|halved and seeded;1 bunch|parsley|finely chopped;1 bunch|dill|finely chopped;1/2 bunch|cilantro|finely chopped;1|onion|grated;3 tbsp|tomato paste;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|tomato sauce;2 cup|chicken broth;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the rice with the herbs, onion, 1 tbsp tomato paste, oil, cumin, coriander, salt and pepper to make the filling.|Fill each zucchini and pepper about three-quarters full, because the rice will expand as it cooks.|Stir the garlic, remaining tomato paste, tomato sauce and broth together in a wide pot with a pinch of salt.|Pack the stuffed vegetables snugly in the pot, open sides up, and lay a heatproof plate on top to keep them in place.|Bring to a simmer, cover and cook on low for 45 to 55 minutes until the rice and vegetables are tender.|Rest 10 minutes and serve with the sauce spooned over.","Egyptian"],
[3004,"Warak Enab","sides","🍃",120,"Medium",7.5,8,"Grape leaves rolled around herbed rice and simmered with lemon until soft and tangy.","1 jar|grape leaves|rinsed;1 cup|rice|short grain, rinsed;1|onion|finely chopped;2|tomatoes|finely chopped;1 bunch|parsley|finely chopped;1/2 bunch|dill|finely chopped;2 tbsp|tomato paste;1/3 cup|olive oil;1/4 cup|lemon juice;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|salt;2 cup|water;|black pepper|to taste","Combine the rice, onion, tomatoes, herbs, tomato paste, half the oil, cumin, salt and pepper for the filling.|Lay a grape leaf shiny side down, put a heaping teaspoon of filling near the stem end, fold in the sides and roll up tightly like a thin cigar.|Line the bottom of a heavy pot with a few torn leaves and pack the rolls in tight layers.|Pour over the remaining oil, the lemon juice and the water, and set a plate on top to weigh the rolls down.|Bring to a simmer, cover and cook on low for 50 to 60 minutes until the rice is tender and most of the liquid is absorbed.|Cool slightly and serve warm or at room temperature with lemon wedges.","Egyptian"],
[3005,"Om Ali","treats","🍮",50,"Easy",9,8,"Egypt's famous warm bread pudding made with flaky pastry, nuts, raisins and sweet creamy milk.","1 lb|puff pastry|baked and broken in pieces;3 cup|milk;1 cup|heavy cream;1/2 cup|sugar;1 tsp|vanilla;1/2 cup|almonds|chopped;1/2 cup|pistachios|chopped;1/2 cup|raisins;1/2 cup|coconut|shredded, unsweetened;1/2 tsp|cinnamon","Heat the oven to 400°F. Bake the puff pastry on a sheet for 20 minutes until deeply golden, then cool and break into bite-size pieces.|Warm the milk, 1/2 cup of the cream, sugar and vanilla in a pot until the sugar dissolves.|Scatter half the pastry in a baking dish, then half the nuts, raisins and coconut. Repeat with the remaining pastry and toppings.|Pour the hot milk mixture evenly over the top so the pastry soaks it up.|Whip the remaining cream to soft peaks and dollop on top, then dust with cinnamon.|Bake 15 to 20 minutes until bubbling and browned on top. Serve hot.","Egyptian"],
[3006,"Basbousa","treats","🍰",55,"Easy",9,16,"Moist semolina cake soaked in lemony syrup and topped with an almond.","2 cup|semolina|fine;1 cup|sugar;1 cup|coconut|shredded, unsweetened;1 cup|greek yogurt|plain;1/2 cup|butter|melted;2 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|vanilla;16|almonds|blanched, whole;1 1/2 cup|sugar|for syrup;1 cup|water|for syrup;1 tbsp|lemon juice|for syrup","Heat the oven to 350°F and grease a 9x13 pan.|Mix the semolina, 1 cup sugar, coconut, baking powder, yogurt, melted butter and vanilla into a thick batter and let it rest 10 minutes.|Spread the batter in the pan, score into diamonds and press an almond into the center of each.|Bake 30 to 35 minutes until golden brown.|Meanwhile simmer the syrup sugar and water for 8 minutes, stir in the lemon juice and let cool.|Pour the cool syrup over the hot cake and let it soak at least 30 minutes before serving.","Egyptian"],
[3007,"Egyptian Kofta","comfort","🍢",40,"Easy",9,6,"Juicy grilled skewers of spiced ground beef with onion and parsley, served with tahini and bread.","2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|grated and squeezed dry;1 bunch|parsley|finely chopped;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|allspice;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|olive oil;6|pita|for serving","Combine the beef, onion, parsley, garlic, cumin, coriander, cinnamon, allspice, salt and pepper and knead well for 2 minutes.|Chill the mixture 20 minutes so it holds together on skewers.|Shape into long, thin sausages around flat metal skewers or into 12 oval patties.|Heat a grill or grill pan to medium-high and brush lightly with oil.|Grill 8 to 10 minutes, turning, until browned and cooked to 160°F inside.|Serve in warm pita with tomatoes, onions and tahini.","Egyptian"],
[3008,"Roz Bel Laban","treats","🍚",50,"Easy",9,6,"Silky Egyptian rice pudding scented with vanilla and topped with cinnamon and nuts.","1/2 cup|rice|short grain, rinsed;1/2 cup|water;4 cup|milk;1/2 cup|sugar;1 tbsp|cornstarch|mixed with 2 tbsp milk;1 tsp|vanilla;1 tbsp|rose water|optional;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/4 cup|pistachios|chopped;|cinnamon|for dusting","Simmer the rice with the water in a pot for 10 minutes until the water is absorbed.|Add the milk and bring to a gentle boil, then reduce the heat and cook 25 minutes, stirring often, until the rice is very soft.|Stir in the sugar and cornstarch mixture and cook 5 more minutes until thick and creamy.|Add the cream, vanilla and rose water and warm through 2 minutes.|Spoon into bowls and chill at least 1 hour, as it thickens when cold.|Top with pistachios and cinnamon before serving.","Egyptian"],
[3009,"Bamia (Egyptian Okra Stew)","comfort","🥘",90,"Easy",9,6,"Tender beef and okra simmered in a garlicky tomato sauce, served over rice.","1 1/2 lb|beef stew meat|cubed;1|onion|chopped;1 lb|okra|frozen whole, thawed;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|tomato sauce|15 oz;2 tbsp|tomato paste;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tbsp|coriander;1 tsp|cumin;2 cup|beef broth;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;3 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Brown the beef in the oil in a heavy pot over medium-high heat for 6 minutes and add the onion, cooking 4 minutes more.|Add half the garlic, the tomato paste, cumin, salt and pepper and stir 1 minute.|Pour in the broth, cover and simmer on low for 50 minutes until the beef is nearly tender.|In a skillet, saute the okra in a little oil for 5 minutes to reduce sliminess.|Add the okra and tomato sauce to the pot and simmer 20 minutes.|Fry the remaining garlic with the coriander in a spoon of oil until fragrant and stir it in. Serve over rice.","Egyptian"],
[3010,"Shorbet Ads (Egyptian Lentil Soup)","soup","🍲",45,"Very easy",9.5,6,"Smooth, golden lentil soup with cumin and a squeeze of lemon, a staple on Egyptian tables.","1 1/2 cup|lentils|red, rinsed;1|onion|chopped;1|carrots|chopped;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|olive oil;1 1/2 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|turmeric;6 cup|chicken broth;|lemon|wedges, for serving;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Saute the onion and carrot in the oil in a large pot for 6 minutes until soft.|Stir in the garlic, cumin and turmeric for 1 minute.|Add the lentils and broth, bring to a boil, then simmer 25 minutes until the lentils fall apart.|Blend the soup until completely smooth with an immersion blender.|Season with salt and pepper and thin with hot water if too thick.|Serve with lemon wedges and toasted bread.","Egyptian"],
[3011,"Kebda Eskandarani","quick","🍽️",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Alexandrian-style liver seared with garlic, cumin and hot peppers and eaten in pita.","1 lb|beef liver|thinly sliced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1|bell pepper|sliced;1|green chili|sliced, optional;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1/2 tsp|paprika;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;4|pita|for serving","Pat the liver dry and cut into thin strips, removing any membrane.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over high heat until very hot.|Sear the liver in a single layer for 2 minutes without moving, then flip.|Add the garlic, bell pepper, chili, cumin, coriander, paprika, salt and pepper and cook 3 minutes.|Squeeze in the lemon juice and cook 1 minute more. Do not overcook or the liver turns tough.|Stuff into warm pita and serve right away.","Egyptian"],
[3012,"Sayadeya (Egyptian Fish and Rice)","light","🐟",60,"Medium",7.5,6,"Cumin-spiced white fish over deep golden caramelized onion rice, a coastal Egyptian classic.","2 lb|cod|fillets, cut in large pieces;4|onion|thinly sliced;2 cup|rice;3 cup|water;1/3 cup|vegetable oil;2 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|flour|for dusting;2 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Season the fish with half the cumin, salt, pepper and lemon juice and let sit 15 minutes.|Fry the onions in the oil over medium heat for 20 to 25 minutes, stirring often, until deep brown. Remove half for topping.|To the onions in the pot add the garlic, coriander and remaining cumin and cook 1 minute.|Add the rice and water with salt, bring to a boil, cover and cook on low for 18 minutes.|Meanwhile dust the fish in flour and pan-fry in oil 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden.|Serve the fish on the rice topped with the reserved fried onions.","Egyptian"],
[3013,"Roz Bel Shareya","sides","🍚",35,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Fluffy Egyptian rice cooked with toasted vermicelli noodles in butter.","2 cup|rice|short or medium grain;1/2 cup|vermicelli|broken;3 tbsp|butter;3 cup|chicken broth;|salt|to taste","Rinse the rice until the water runs clear and drain well.|Melt the butter in a pot and toast the vermicelli over medium heat for 2 to 3 minutes until deep golden brown.|Stir in the rice for 1 minute to coat in the butter.|Pour in the hot broth, add salt, and bring to a boil.|Reduce to the lowest heat, cover tightly and cook 18 minutes.|Rest, covered, 10 minutes, then fluff with a fork.","Egyptian"],
[3014,"Mesaka'a (Egyptian Moussaka)","comfort","🍆",70,"Easy",9,6,"Fried eggplant slow-cooked in a garlicky tomato and pepper sauce, nothing like Greek moussaka.","3 lb|eggplant|sliced 1/2 inch thick;2|bell pepper|sliced;1|onion|sliced;5 clove|garlic|sliced;1 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz;2 tbsp|tomato paste;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 cup|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|vinegar;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Salt the eggplant slices, rest 20 minutes, then pat dry.|Heat the oven to 425°F, brush the slices with oil and roast on sheets 25 minutes, flipping once, until golden.|Saute the onion and peppers in a little oil for 6 minutes, then add the garlic, cumin and paprika for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, tomato paste and vinegar, season, and simmer 15 minutes.|Layer the eggplant in a deep pan and pour the sauce over the top.|Simmer gently, covered, for 20 minutes. Serve warm or at room temperature with rice or bread.","Egyptian"],
[3015,"Egyptian Goulash","comfort","🥧",80,"Medium",9,8,"A baked phyllo pie of spiced ground beef, tomato and creamy milk, an Egyptian home favorite.","1 lb|phyllo dough|thawed;1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 cup|tomato sauce;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 cup|butter|melted;2 cup|milk;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 cup|mozzarella|shredded;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the beef with the onion for 8 minutes, add garlic, cumin, cinnamon, salt and pepper, then stir in the tomato sauce and simmer 10 minutes.|Heat the oven to 375°F and butter a 9x13 dish.|Layer half the phyllo sheets in the dish, brushing each with butter.|Spread the meat filling over the phyllo and sprinkle with the mozzarella.|Cover with the remaining buttered phyllo sheets and cut through into squares.|Bake 30 minutes until golden, then pour the milk and cream mixed with a pinch of salt over the top and bake 15 more minutes until absorbed.","Egyptian"],
[3016,"Batates Bel Lahma (Egyptian Beef and Potato Stew)","comfort","🥔",100,"Easy",9,6,"Fall-apart beef and potatoes in a simple tomato gravy.","1 1/2 lb|beef stew meat|cubed;1|onion|chopped;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|tomato paste;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;3 cup|beef broth;2 lb|potatoes|peeled, cut in chunks;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the beef in the oil in a heavy pot over medium-high heat for 7 minutes.|Add the onion and cook 4 minutes, then the garlic, tomato paste, cumin, cinnamon, salt and pepper for 1 minute.|Add the broth, cover and simmer on low for 50 minutes until the beef is almost tender.|Fry the potato chunks in a skillet until lightly golden, about 8 minutes, if you like a crisper edge.|Add the potatoes to the pot and simmer 25 minutes until tender and the sauce thickens.|Adjust the seasoning and serve with rice.","Egyptian"],
[3017,"Fasolia (Egyptian Green Bean Stew)","comfort","🫘",60,"Easy",9,4,"Green beans simmered with beef and tomatoes until tender, served over rice.","1 lb|green beans|trimmed;1 lb|beef stew meat|small cubes;1|onion|chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|cumin;2 cup|water;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;3 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Brown the beef in the oil in a pot for 6 minutes, then add the onion and cook 4 minutes.|Add the garlic, coriander, cumin, salt and pepper and stir 1 minute.|Pour in the water, cover and simmer 35 minutes until the beef is tender.|Add the green beans and tomato sauce and simmer, partly covered, 20 minutes until the beans are very soft.|Reduce uncovered 5 minutes if the sauce is thin.|Serve over rice.","Egyptian"],
[3018,"Torly (Egyptian Baked Vegetable Casserole)","comfort","🥕",90,"Easy",9,6,"Layers of potatoes, zucchini, eggplant and peppers baked in tomato sauce until tender.","1 lb|potatoes|sliced;2|zucchini|sliced;1|eggplant|cubed;2|bell pepper|sliced;2|carrots|sliced;1|onion|sliced;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|tomato sauce;1 lb|beef stew meat|small cubes, optional;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;1 cup|water;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 375°F.|If using beef, brown it in oil for 6 minutes and add the onion and garlic for 3 minutes.|Mix the tomato sauce with the water, cumin, coriander, salt and pepper.|Toss all the vegetables with oil and salt and spread in a deep baking dish with the meat.|Pour the sauce over, cover tightly with foil and bake 45 minutes.|Uncover and bake 20 to 25 minutes more until the vegetables are tender and the sauce thick. Serve with rice.","Egyptian"],
[3019,"Qatayef","treats","🥞",60,"Medium",9,12,"Ramadan pancakes folded around nuts or cream and dunked in sweet syrup.","1 1/2 cup|flour;1/2 cup|semolina;1 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|yeast;1 tbsp|sugar;2 cup|warm water;1 cup|walnuts|chopped;1/2 cup|raisins;1 tsp|cinnamon;1 cup|sugar|for syrup;1/2 cup|water|for syrup;1 tbsp|lemon juice|for syrup;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Blend the flour, semolina, baking powder, yeast, sugar and warm water into a thin batter and rest 30 minutes.|Boil the syrup sugar and water for 8 minutes, stir in the lemon juice and cool.|Mix the walnuts, raisins and cinnamon for the filling.|Pour small 3-inch rounds of batter onto a medium-hot nonstick pan and cook on one side only until the surface is covered in bubbles and set, about 1 to 2 minutes.|Put a spoon of filling in the center of each pancake, fold into a half moon and pinch the edges tightly closed.|Fry in 350°F oil for 2 to 3 minutes until golden, drain, and dip in the cool syrup.","Egyptian"],
[3020,"Kahk","treats","🍪",75,"Medium",9,30,"Buttery Eid cookies stuffed with dates or nuts and dusted with powdered sugar.","3 cup|flour;1 cup|butter|melted;1/4 cup|sesame oil;1/2 cup|milk|warm;1 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|yeast;1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|sugar;1 cup|walnuts|chopped;1 tsp|cinnamon;1 cup|powdered sugar|for dusting","Rub the flour, salt, butter and sesame oil together until the flour feels like wet sand, then rest 30 minutes.|Dissolve the yeast and sugar in the warm milk and knead into the flour to a soft, smooth dough.|Mix the walnuts with the cinnamon for the filling.|Roll the dough into walnut-size balls, flatten, fill, and close, then flatten slightly into rounds and mark the tops with a fork or tongs.|Place on a lined sheet and bake at 350°F for 20 to 25 minutes until just barely golden on the bottom.|Cool completely and dust heavily with powdered sugar.","Egyptian"],
[3021,"Egyptian Eggah","breakfast","🍳",35,"Easy",8.5,6,"A thick baked herb omelet, like a spiced Egyptian frittata cut in squares.","6|eggs;1 bunch|parsley|finely chopped;1/2 bunch|dill|finely chopped;1|onion|finely chopped;2 tbsp|flour;1 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|coriander;3 tbsp|butter;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 375°F.|Saute the onion in 1 tbsp butter for 5 minutes until soft and let cool.|Whisk the eggs with the flour, baking powder, cumin, coriander, salt and pepper until smooth.|Stir in the herbs and cooled onion.|Melt the remaining butter in an 8-inch oven-safe pan, pour in the egg mixture and cook 2 minutes on the stove.|Bake 20 to 25 minutes until puffed and set, then cut into squares.","Egyptian"],
[3022,"Sahlab","treats","🥛",15,"Very easy",9,4,"A warm, creamy milk pudding drink topped with nuts, coconut and cinnamon.","4 cup|milk;1/4 cup|cornstarch;1/3 cup|sugar;1 tsp|vanilla;1 tbsp|rose water;1/4 cup|pistachios|chopped;1/4 cup|coconut|shredded, unsweetened;|cinnamon|for dusting","Whisk the cornstarch into 1 cup of the cold milk until smooth.|Heat the remaining milk with the sugar in a pot over medium heat until steaming.|Slowly whisk in the cornstarch mixture.|Cook, whisking constantly, for 5 to 6 minutes until thickened to a pudding-like drink.|Stir in the vanilla and rose water.|Pour into cups and top with pistachios, coconut and cinnamon.","Egyptian"],
[3023,"Bessara (Egyptian Fava Bean Soup)","soup","🌿",75,"Easy",9.5,6,"A thick, green, herb-packed puree of dried fava beans and greens.","2 cup|dried fava beans|peeled, split, soaked overnight;1|onion|chopped;1 bunch|parsley;1 bunch|dill;1 bunch|cilantro;1 head|lettuce|chopped;4 clove|garlic|chopped;1 tsp|cumin;3 tbsp|olive oil;6 cup|water;|salt|to taste;|lemon|wedges, for serving","Drain the soaked fava beans and place in a pot with the water and half the onion.|Bring to a boil, skim, then simmer 40 minutes until very soft.|Add the lettuce, parsley, dill and cilantro and simmer 10 more minutes.|Blend until completely smooth and season with salt, adding hot water if too thick.|Fry the remaining onion and garlic in the oil with the cumin until golden, about 6 minutes.|Serve the soup topped with the garlicky onions, olive oil and lemon.","Egyptian"],
[3024,"Egyptian Sambousek","sides","🥟",60,"Medium",7.5,8,"Crisp fried half-moon pastries filled with spiced beef or cheese.","2 cup|flour;1/4 cup|vegetable oil;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|warm water;1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|finely chopped;1/2 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/4 cup|pine nuts;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;|black pepper|to taste","Knead the flour, oil, salt and water into a smooth dough and rest 20 minutes.|Brown the beef with the onion for 7 minutes, then stir in the cumin, cinnamon, pine nuts, salt and pepper and cool.|Roll the dough thin and cut 4-inch rounds.|Place a spoonful of filling in each, fold over and press the edges firmly with a fork to seal.|Fry in 350°F oil for 2 to 3 minutes per side until deep golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve hot.","Egyptian"],
[3025,"Betingan Makli (Fried Eggplant with Garlic Vinegar)","sides","🍆",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Golden fried eggplant slices tossed in a punchy garlic, vinegar and cumin dressing.","2 lb|eggplant|sliced 1/2 inch thick;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|white vinegar;1 tsp|cumin;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/2 tsp|salt;|black pepper|to taste","Salt the eggplant slices, rest 15 minutes and pat dry.|Heat 1/2 inch of oil in a skillet over medium-high heat.|Fry the slices 3 minutes per side until golden and tender, in batches, and drain on paper towels.|Stir the garlic, vinegar, cumin, salt and pepper together.|Arrange the eggplant on a platter and spoon the dressing over it.|Sprinkle with parsley and serve warm or at room temperature with bread.","Egyptian"],
[3026,"Roz Mu'ammar","comfort","🥣",60,"Easy",9,6,"Rich, creamy baked rice cooked in milk, butter and broth, the Egyptian comfort side.","1 cup|rice|short grain, rinsed;1 cup|milk;1 cup|chicken broth;1/2 cup|heavy cream;4 tbsp|butter;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 400°F.|Put the rice in an oven-safe pot or clay dish with the salt and pepper.|Heat the milk, broth and cream until steaming and pour over the rice.|Dot the top with the butter and cover tightly with foil or a lid.|Bake 35 to 40 minutes until the rice is soft and creamy.|Stir and serve hot, optionally under the broiler 3 minutes for a golden top.","Egyptian"],
[3027,"Shish Tawook","lunch","🍢",50,"Easy",8,4,"Lemony yogurt-marinated chicken skewers grilled until juicy, served with garlic sauce.","2 lb|chicken breast|cut in 1 1/2 inch cubes;3/4 cup|greek yogurt;3 tbsp|lemon juice;3 tbsp|olive oil;1 tbsp|tomato paste;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 tsp|cumin","Whisk the yogurt, lemon juice, oil, tomato paste, garlic, paprika, cumin, salt and pepper.|Add the chicken, toss well, cover and marinate in the fridge at least 2 hours or overnight.|Thread the chicken onto skewers.|Heat a grill or grill pan to medium-high.|Grill 10 to 12 minutes, turning every few minutes, until charred and 165°F inside.|Serve with pita, toum and pickles.","Lebanese"],
[3028,"Tabbouleh","light","🥗",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"A bright parsley salad with tomato, mint, bulgur and lemon.","4 bunch|parsley|flat leaf, finely chopped;1/2 bunch|mint|finely chopped;4|tomatoes|small dice;4|green onion|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|bulgur|fine, soaked in lemon juice;1/4 cup|lemon juice;1/3 cup|olive oil;1/2 tsp|salt;|black pepper|to taste;1 head|lettuce|romaine leaves, for serving","Soak the bulgur in the lemon juice for 15 minutes.|Wash the parsley and dry it thoroughly so the salad is not soggy, then chop very fine.|Combine the parsley, mint, tomatoes and green onion.|Add the soaked bulgur, olive oil, salt and pepper and toss gently.|Taste and add more lemon or salt as needed.|Serve in lettuce leaves.","Lebanese"],
[3029,"Fattoush","light","🥗",25,"Easy",7.5,6,"Crunchy Lebanese chopped salad with fried pita chips and tangy sumac dressing.","2|pita|torn;1 head|lettuce|romaine, chopped;2|cucumber|diced;4|tomatoes|diced;5|radish|sliced;4|green onion|sliced;1/2 cup|parsley|chopped;1/4 cup|mint|chopped;1/3 cup|olive oil;1/4 cup|lemon juice;1 tbsp|sumac;1 tbsp|pomegranate molasses;1 clove|garlic|minced;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 400°F and toss the torn pita with 2 tbsp olive oil and a pinch of salt.|Bake 8 to 10 minutes until crisp and golden and let cool.|Whisk the remaining oil, lemon juice, sumac, pomegranate molasses, garlic and salt.|Toss the lettuce, cucumbers, tomatoes, radishes, green onion and herbs in a large bowl.|Pour the dressing over and toss.|Add the pita chips just before serving so they stay crunchy.","Lebanese"],
[3030,"Mujadara","comfort","🧅",60,"Easy",9,6,"Lentils and rice crowned with deeply caramelized onions, the ultimate Levantine comfort dish.","1 cup|lentils|brown or green, rinsed;1 cup|rice;4|onion|thinly sliced;1/2 cup|olive oil;2 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|salt;4 cup|water;|black pepper|to taste;1 cup|greek yogurt|for serving","Simmer the lentils in 3 cups of the water for 15 minutes until just starting to soften, then drain, saving the water.|Fry the onions in the oil over medium heat, stirring often, for 25 to 30 minutes until dark golden and crisp at the edges.|Remove half the onions for topping.|To the pot add the lentils, rice, cumin, salt, pepper and 2 cups of the reserved cooking water topped up with water.|Bring to a boil, cover and cook on low for 20 minutes.|Rest 10 minutes, fluff, top with the reserved onions and serve with yogurt.","Lebanese"],
[3031,"Manakish Za'atar","breakfast","🫓",90,"Medium",8.5,6,"Soft flatbreads brushed with olive oil and za'atar, the classic Lebanese breakfast.","3 cup|flour;1 packet|yeast|2 1/4 tsp;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|warm water;2 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 cup|za'atar;1/2 cup|olive oil|for topping","Mix the yeast, sugar and warm water and wait 5 minutes until foamy.|Combine the flour and salt, add the yeast mixture and 2 tbsp oil and knead 8 minutes into a soft dough.|Cover and let rise 1 hour until doubled.|Heat the oven to 475°F with a baking sheet inside.|Divide the dough into 6 balls, flatten into 6-inch rounds and press dimples into them.|Mix the za'atar with the topping oil, spread over the dough and bake 8 to 10 minutes until golden.","Lebanese"],
[3032,"Baked Kibbeh (Kibbeh bil Sanieh)","comfort","🥘",90,"Medium",9,8,"Layers of spiced bulgur and lamb with a pine nut and onion filling, baked until golden.","1 1/2 cup|bulgur|fine;1 1/2 lb|ground lamb|divided;2|onion|divided, one grated and one chopped;1 tsp|allspice;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 cup|pine nuts;3 tbsp|olive oil;1/4 cup|butter|melted;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Soak the bulgur in cold water 15 minutes, drain and squeeze dry.|Process 1 lb of the lamb with the grated onion, bulgur, half the allspice, cinnamon, salt and pepper into a smooth paste.|For the filling, brown the remaining lamb with the chopped onion in the oil for 8 minutes, then add the pine nuts, remaining allspice, salt and pepper.|Heat the oven to 375°F. Press half the kibbeh paste into a greased 9x13 dish.|Spread the filling on top and cover with the remaining paste, smoothing the top.|Score into diamonds, pour over the butter and bake 40 to 45 minutes until browned.","Lebanese"],
[3033,"Iskender Kebab","comfort","🥩",50,"Medium",9,4,"Thin-sliced spiced beef on bread with hot tomato sauce, yogurt and sizzling butter.","1 1/2 lb|sirloin steak|very thinly sliced;2 tbsp|olive oil;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|salt;4|pita|cut in squares;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;1 tbsp|tomato paste;4 tbsp|butter;1 cup|greek yogurt;1 clove|garlic|minced;1|tomatoes|halved, grilled, optional","Toss the steak with the oil, cumin, paprika and salt.|Warm the pita squares in a 350°F oven for 5 minutes and spread on a platter.|Simmer the tomato sauce and tomato paste with a pinch of salt for 8 minutes.|Sear the meat in a very hot skillet in small batches for 2 minutes per batch until browned.|Pile the meat over the bread, ladle the hot tomato sauce on top and add a bed of yogurt mixed with garlic on the side.|Brown the butter in a small pan until nutty and pour sizzling over everything right before serving.","Turkish"],
[3034,"Menemen","breakfast","🍳",25,"Easy",8.5,3,"Soft-scrambled eggs cooked with tomatoes and peppers, a Turkish breakfast staple.","4|eggs;3|tomatoes|chopped;2|bell pepper|green, diced;1|onion|diced, optional;2 tbsp|butter;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;|bread|for serving","Melt the butter in a skillet and saute the peppers and onion 5 minutes until soft.|Add the tomatoes and cook 8 to 10 minutes until the juices reduce and thicken.|Season with salt, pepper and pepper flakes.|Crack the eggs over the top and stir gently or leave whole.|Cook 2 to 3 minutes until just set but still soft.|Serve in the pan with crusty bread.","Turkish"],
[3035,"Karniyarik","comfort","🍆",75,"Medium",9,4,"Split eggplants stuffed with spiced beef and baked in tomato sauce.","4|eggplant|small;1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2|tomatoes|diced;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 cup|water;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Peel the eggplants in stripes, slit lengthwise leaving the ends intact and soak in salted water 15 minutes, then pat dry.|Fry the eggplants in oil until golden on all sides, about 8 minutes, and drain.|Brown the beef with the onion for 7 minutes, add the garlic, half the tomato, parsley, salt and pepper and cook 5 minutes.|Heat the oven to 375°F and arrange the eggplants in a baking dish.|Press the beef into the slits and top with the remaining tomato.|Mix the tomato paste with the water, pour around, and bake 30 minutes.","Turkish"],
[3036,"Kiymali Pide","lunch","🥖",100,"Medium",8,4,"Boat-shaped Turkish flatbread filled with spiced minced beef and baked until blistered.","3 cup|flour;1 packet|yeast;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|warm water;1 tbsp|olive oil;3/4 lb|ground beef;1|onion|finely diced;1|bell pepper|finely diced;1|tomatoes|finely diced;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1 tsp|paprika;1|eggs|beaten, for brushing","Mix the yeast, sugar and water, wait 5 minutes, then knead with the flour, salt and oil for 8 minutes. Let rise 1 hour.|Combine the beef, onion, pepper, tomato, tomato paste, paprika and salt for the filling.|Heat the oven to 475°F with a baking sheet inside.|Divide the dough into 4, roll each into an oval and spread the filling down the center, leaving a border.|Fold the long edges over the filling and pinch the ends into a boat shape. Brush the crust with egg.|Bake 12 to 15 minutes until golden and the meat is cooked.","Turkish"],
[3037,"Gozleme","lunch","🫓",50,"Easy",8,4,"Thin hand-rolled Turkish flatbreads filled with spinach and feta and griddled until crisp.","3 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|warm water;2 tbsp|olive oil;1 lb|spinach|fresh, wilted and squeezed dry;1 cup|feta|crumbled;1|onion|small, finely diced;3 tbsp|butter|melted;|black pepper|to taste","Knead the flour, salt, water and oil into a smooth dough, cover and rest 30 minutes.|Mix the spinach, feta, onion and pepper for the filling.|Divide the dough into 4 balls and roll each into a very thin round.|Spread the filling over half of each round, fold over and seal the edges.|Cook on a dry hot skillet 2 to 3 minutes per side until blistered and golden.|Brush with butter and serve with lemon.","Turkish"],
[3038,"Manti","comfort","🥟",120,"Medium",9,6,"Tiny Turkish beef dumplings under garlicky yogurt and paprika butter.","2 1/2 cup|flour;1|eggs;1/2 cup|water;1 tsp|salt;1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|grated;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2 cup|greek yogurt;2 clove|garlic|minced;4 tbsp|butter;1 tbsp|paprika;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;6 cup|beef broth","Knead the flour, egg, water and salt into a stiff dough and rest 30 minutes.|Mix the beef, onion, pepper and a pinch of salt.|Roll the dough very thin, cut into 1-inch squares, and place a pea-size bit of filling in each center. Pinch the corners together.|Mix the yogurt with the garlic and a pinch of salt.|Simmer the manti in the broth for 10 to 12 minutes until they float and are tender.|Melt the butter with the paprika and flakes. Spoon the manti with a little broth onto plates, top with yogurt and the sizzling butter.","Turkish"],
[3039,"Muhammara","sides","🌶️",15,"Very easy",7.5,8,"A smoky roasted red pepper and walnut dip with a tangy-sweet pomegranate kick.","1 jar|roasted red peppers|12 oz, drained;1 cup|walnuts|toasted;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs;2 tbsp|pomegranate molasses;1 clove|garlic;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes;1/4 cup|olive oil;1 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste","Toast the walnuts in a dry skillet for 4 minutes until fragrant and cool.|Add the peppers, walnuts, breadcrumbs, garlic, cumin and pepper flakes to a food processor.|Pulse until chunky.|Add the pomegranate molasses and lemon juice and blend while streaming in the olive oil.|Season with salt and chill 30 minutes.|Serve with a swirl of oil and warm pita.","Middle Eastern"],
[3040,"Toum (Lebanese Garlic Sauce)","sides","🧄",15,"Medium",7.5,12,"Fluffy, intensely garlicky white sauce for chicken and kebabs.","1 head|garlic|peeled;1 tsp|salt;1 1/2 cup|vegetable oil;1/4 cup|lemon juice;2 tbsp|ice water","Process the garlic and salt in a food processor to a fine paste, scraping the sides.|With the machine running, add the oil a few drops at a time at first, then in a thin stream.|Add the lemon juice in small portions, alternating with the oil.|Blend in the ice water to lighten the sauce.|Taste and adjust salt and lemon.|Refrigerate in a jar, where it will keep about 2 weeks.","Lebanese"],
[3041,"Batata Harra","sides","🥔",45,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crispy Lebanese potatoes tossed with garlic, cilantro, lemon and chili.","2 lb|baby potatoes|halved;1/4 cup|olive oil;6 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;1 tsp|coriander;2 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste","Boil the potatoes in salted water 10 minutes until barely tender and drain well.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.|Fry the potatoes 15 minutes, turning, until crisp and golden.|Add the garlic, coriander and chili and cook 1 minute.|Remove from the heat and toss with the cilantro and lemon juice.|Season with salt and serve hot.","Lebanese"],
[3042,"Fatayer bi Sabanekh","sides","🥟",100,"Medium",7.5,12,"Soft triangle pies stuffed with lemony spinach and onion.","3 cup|flour;1 packet|yeast;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|warm water;1/4 cup|olive oil;1 lb|spinach|fresh, chopped;1|onion|finely diced;3 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tbsp|sumac;3 tbsp|olive oil|for the filling;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the yeast, sugar and water, wait 5 minutes, then knead with the flour, salt and oil. Rise 1 hour.|Toss the spinach with 1 tsp salt, rest 10 minutes and squeeze out all the liquid.|Mix with the onion, lemon juice, sumac, oil and pepper.|Heat the oven to 400°F. Roll the dough thin and cut 4-inch rounds.|Place filling in the center and pinch the edges in three sides to form triangles, sealing completely.|Bake 15 to 18 minutes until golden and brush with oil.","Lebanese"],
[3043,"Birria Tacos","comfort","🌮",240,"Medium",9,8,"Chile-braised beef in corn tortillas crisped in the red fat, served with a cup of rich consomme for dipping.","6|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;3|dried ancho chiles|stemmed and seeded;2|tomatoes|quartered;1|onion|quartered;4 clove|garlic;3 lb|chuck roast|cut in large chunks;2 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|oregano;2|bay leaves;4 cup|beef broth;16|corn tortillas;2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;1/2 cup|onion|finely diced, for serving;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;2|lime|cut in wedges;|salt|to taste","Toast the dried chiles in a dry skillet over medium heat for 30 seconds per side, then soak in hot water for 15 minutes until soft.|Blend the soaked chiles with the tomatoes, onion, garlic, vinegar, cumin, oregano and 1 cup of the broth until smooth, then strain.|Season the beef generously with salt and toss with the chile sauce in a Dutch oven. Add the bay leaves and the remaining broth.|Cover and braise in a 325°F oven for 3 hours until the beef shreds easily.|Skim the red fat from the top into a bowl, discard the bay leaves, and shred the meat, moistening it with some of the consomme.|Dip each tortilla in the reserved fat, fry on a hot skillet, add cheese and beef, fold, and crisp 1 to 2 minutes per side.|Serve with diced onion, cilantro, lime and a cup of warm consomme for dipping.","Mexican"],
[3044,"Carne Asada","comfort","🥩",50,"Easy",9,6,"Citrus-marinated skirt or flank steak grilled hot and sliced thin for tacos, tortas or plates.","2 lb|flank steak;1/2 cup|lime juice;1/2 cup|orange juice;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|olive oil;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;1|jalapeno|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|chili powder;1 tsp|oregano;2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;12|corn tortillas|warmed, for serving","Whisk together the lime juice, orange juice, garlic, oil, cilantro, jalapeno, cumin, chili powder, oregano, salt and pepper.|Place the steak in a zip bag with the marinade and refrigerate for at least 2 hours and up to 8.|Heat a grill or cast iron pan to high heat, around 500°F.|Grill the steak 4 to 5 minutes per side for medium-rare, until it reaches 130°F inside.|Rest the meat 10 minutes, then slice thinly against the grain.|Serve in warm tortillas with salsa, onion and lime.","Mexican"],
[3045,"Tacos al Pastor","comfort","🌮",90,"Medium",9,6,"Thin pork marinated in chiles and pineapple, seared until charred and tucked into tortillas with fresh pineapple.","3|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;2 tbsp|chipotle in adobo|with sauce;1/2 cup|pineapple juice;1/4 cup|white vinegar;4 clove|garlic;2 tbsp|achiote paste;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|oregano;2 tsp|salt;2 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;1 cup|pineapple|diced fresh;12|corn tortillas;1/2|onion|finely diced;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;1|lime|cut in wedges","Soak the guajillos in hot water for 15 minutes until soft.|Blend the chiles with the chipotle, pineapple juice, vinegar, garlic, achiote, cumin, oregano and salt until smooth.|Coat the sliced pork in the marinade and refrigerate at least 4 hours or overnight.|Heat a large cast iron skillet over high heat and sear the pork in batches, 3 to 4 minutes per side, until charred at the edges and cooked through.|Sear the pineapple in the same pan for 2 minutes until caramelized.|Chop the pork, warm the tortillas, and fill with pork, pineapple, onion and cilantro.|Serve with lime wedges.","Mexican"],
[3046,"Carnitas","prep","🐖",200,"Easy",9,8,"Pork simmered until tender in its own fat and orange, then crisped under the broiler for juicy, crackly edges.","4 lb|pork shoulder|cut in 3 inch chunks;2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|oregano;1|onion|quartered;6 clove|garlic|smashed;2|bay leaves;2|oranges|juiced;1|lime|juiced;1/2 cup|water;12|corn tortillas;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped","Season the pork with salt, pepper, cumin and oregano and let it sit 30 minutes.|Place the pork in a Dutch oven with the onion, garlic, bay leaves, orange juice, lime juice and water.|Bring to a simmer, cover, and cook in a 300°F oven for 2 1/2 to 3 hours until the meat is fork tender.|Shred the pork and discard the bay leaves, onion and skin.|Spread on a sheet pan, spoon over some pan juices, and broil 5 to 7 minutes until the edges are browned and crisp.|Serve in warm tortillas with cilantro, onion and salsa.","Mexican"],
[3047,"Chicken Tinga","comfort","🌶️",45,"Easy",9,6,"Shredded chicken in a smoky chipotle and tomato sauce, perfect for tostadas, tacos or tortas.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast;4 cup|chicken broth;1|onion|half quartered, half sliced;3 clove|garlic;4|tomatoes|roma, quartered;2 tbsp|chipotle in adobo|with sauce;1 tsp|oregano;1/2 tsp|cumin;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;|salt|to taste;12|corn tortillas;1/2 cup|sour cream|for serving","Simmer the chicken in the broth with the quartered onion half and 1 clove garlic for 20 minutes until cooked through.|Shred the chicken and reserve 1/2 cup of the broth.|Blend the tomatoes, remaining garlic, chipotle, oregano, cumin and the reserved broth until smooth.|Saute the sliced onion in the oil for 5 minutes until soft, then pour in the sauce and simmer 8 minutes.|Stir in the shredded chicken and cook 5 more minutes, seasoning with salt.|Serve on warm tortillas or crisp tostadas topped with sour cream.","Mexican"],
[3048,"Pozole Rojo","soup","🍲",150,"Medium",9.5,8,"Hearty pork and hominy soup in a deep red guajillo broth, served with crunchy cabbage, radish and lime.","2 lb|pork shoulder|cut in chunks;8 cup|water;1|onion|halved;6 clove|garlic;2|bay leaves;6|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;2|dried ancho chiles|stemmed and seeded;2 can|hominy|25 oz each, drained;1 tsp|oregano;1 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|salt;2 cup|cabbage|shredded, for serving;6|radishes|sliced, for serving;2|lime|cut in wedges","Place the pork, water, half the onion, 3 cloves garlic, bay leaves and salt in a large pot and bring to a boil. Skim the foam.|Simmer covered for 1 hour 15 minutes until the pork is tender.|Soak the chiles in hot water for 15 minutes, then blend with the remaining onion and garlic, oregano, cumin and 1 cup of the broth until smooth. Strain.|Stir the chile sauce and hominy into the pot and simmer uncovered for 30 minutes.|Adjust the salt and shred some of the pork if you like.|Ladle into bowls and top with cabbage, radish, onion and a squeeze of lime.","Mexican"],
[3049,"Chicken Tortilla Soup","soup","🥣",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"A smoky tomato and chile broth with shredded chicken, topped with crisp tortilla strips and avocado.","1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1|jalapeno|diced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14.5 oz, fire roasted;1 tbsp|chili powder;1 tsp|cumin;6 cup|chicken broth;1 lb|chicken breast;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;1 cup|frozen corn;8|corn tortillas|cut in strips;1|avocado|diced;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;2|lime|juiced;|salt|to taste;1/2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded","Toss the tortilla strips with a little oil and salt and bake at 400°F for 8 to 10 minutes until crisp.|Saute the onion and jalapeno in the oil for 5 minutes, then add the garlic, chili powder and cumin for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes and broth, then the chicken breasts, and simmer 18 to 20 minutes until the chicken is cooked.|Remove the chicken, shred it, and return to the pot with the beans and corn.|Simmer 5 more minutes, then stir in the lime juice and cilantro and season with salt.|Ladle into bowls and top with tortilla strips, avocado and cheese.","Mexican"],
[3050,"Chiles Rellenos","comfort","🫑",60,"Medium",9,4,"Roasted poblano peppers stuffed with cheese, dipped in fluffy egg batter, fried and served in tomato sauce.","4|poblano peppers;8 oz|mexican cheese blend|cut in strips;3|eggs|separated;1/4 cup|flour|plus more for dredging;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 can|tomato sauce|15 oz;1/4 cup|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 tsp|cumin;|salt|to taste","Char the poblanos over a flame or under the broiler until blackened all over, then steam in a covered bowl for 10 minutes and peel.|Make a slit in each pepper, remove the seeds, and stuff with cheese strips.|Simmer the tomato sauce with the onion, garlic, cumin and salt for 10 minutes.|Beat the egg whites to stiff peaks, fold in the yolks and 1/4 cup flour with a pinch of salt.|Dust the peppers in flour, dip into the batter, and fry in 350°F oil for 2 to 3 minutes per side until golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve in the warm tomato sauce.","Mexican"],
[3051,"Pork Tamales","prep","🌽",240,"Medium",9,12,"Fluffy masa wrapped around red chile pork in corn husks and steamed, a holiday tradition.","30|dried corn husks;2 lb|pork shoulder|cut in chunks;6|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;3 clove|garlic;1 tsp|cumin;4 cup|masa harina;1 1/2 cup|lard|or vegetable shortening;1 tbsp|baking powder;4 cup|chicken broth|warm;2 tsp|salt","Soak the husks in hot water for 30 minutes until pliable.|Simmer the pork in water with a little salt for 1 1/2 hours until tender, then shred, saving 2 cups of the broth.|Soak the chiles in hot water 15 minutes, blend with garlic, cumin and 1 cup pork broth, strain, and toss with the shredded pork.|Whip the lard for 3 minutes until fluffy. Mix the masa harina, baking powder and salt, then beat into the lard alternately with the warm broth until it resembles thick frosting.|Spread 2 tbsp masa on each husk, add a spoonful of pork, fold and roll.|Stand the tamales upright in a steamer and steam covered for 1 hour 15 minutes, until the masa pulls cleanly from the husk.|Rest 15 minutes before serving.","Mexican"],
[3052,"Chilaquiles Rojos","breakfast","🍳",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Crisp tortilla chips simmered briefly in red salsa and topped with eggs, cheese and cream.","1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/2|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|salsa|red, blended smooth;1/2 cup|chicken broth;8 oz|tortilla chips;4|eggs|fried;1/2 cup|mexican cheese blend|crumbled;1/4 cup|sour cream;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/4|red onion|thinly sliced","Heat the oil and soften the onion and garlic for 3 minutes.|Add the salsa and broth and simmer 5 minutes until slightly thickened.|Fold in the tortilla chips and toss for 1 to 2 minutes until coated but still a little crisp.|Divide among plates right away.|Top with fried eggs, cheese, drizzles of sour cream, cilantro and red onion.","Mexican"],
[3053,"Elote (Mexican Street Corn)","sides","🌽",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Charred corn on the cob slathered with mayo, cotija cheese, chili powder and lime.","4|ears corn|husked;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;1/4 cup|sour cream;1/2 cup|cotija cheese|crumbled;1 tsp|chili powder;1|lime|cut in wedges;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped;|salt|to taste","Heat a grill to medium-high.|Grill the corn 10 to 12 minutes, turning, until charred in spots.|Mix the mayonnaise and sour cream and brush onto each hot ear.|Roll the corn in the cotija cheese.|Dust with chili powder and salt, sprinkle with cilantro and serve with lime.","Mexican"],
[3054,"Mexican Rice","sides","🍚",35,"Easy",7.5,6,"Fluffy long grain rice toasted golden and simmered in a light tomato broth.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 1/2 cup|rice|long grain, rinsed;1/2|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|tomato sauce;2 1/2 cup|chicken broth;1/2 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|frozen peas|optional","Heat the oil in a saucepan over medium heat and toast the rice 5 to 6 minutes, stirring, until golden.|Add the onion and garlic and cook 2 minutes.|Stir in the tomato sauce, broth, cumin and salt and bring to a boil.|Cover, reduce to low, and cook 18 minutes without lifting the lid.|Rest 5 minutes off the heat, fold in the peas if using, and fluff with a fork.","Mexican"],
[3055,"Refried Beans","sides","🫘",30,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Creamy, garlicky pinto beans mashed in a hot skillet, the classic side for tacos and enchiladas.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/2|onion|finely diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 can|pinto beans|15 oz, with their liquid;1/2 tsp|cumin;1/2 cup|chicken broth;|salt|to taste;1/2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded","Heat the oil in a skillet and cook the onion 4 minutes until soft.|Add the garlic and cumin and cook 30 seconds.|Add the beans with their liquid and the broth.|Mash with a potato masher while simmering 10 to 12 minutes until thick and creamy.|Season with salt and top with cheese.","Mexican"],
[3056,"Guacamole","sides","🥑",10,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Chunky ripe avocado mashed with onion, cilantro, jalapeno and lime.","3|avocado|ripe;1/4 cup|red onion|finely diced;1|jalapeno|seeded and minced;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped;2 tbsp|lime juice;1/2 tsp|salt;1|tomatoes|seeded and diced","Halve and pit the avocados and scoop into a bowl.|Mash roughly with a fork, leaving some chunks.|Fold in the onion, jalapeno, cilantro, lime juice and salt.|Stir in the diced tomato.|Taste, adjust the salt and lime, and serve right away with tortilla chips.","Mexican"],
[3057,"Pico de Gallo","sides","🍅",10,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Fresh chopped tomato, onion, jalapeno and cilantro with lime, the brightest salsa on the table.","4|tomatoes|roma, diced;1/2|onion|finely diced;1|jalapeno|seeded and minced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;2 tbsp|lime juice;1/2 tsp|salt","Dice the tomatoes and drain off excess juice in a sieve for 5 minutes.|Combine the tomatoes with the onion, jalapeno and cilantro.|Stir in the lime juice and salt.|Rest 10 minutes so the flavors blend, then serve.","Mexican"],
[3058,"Chile con Queso","sides","🧀",20,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Smooth, melty Tex-Mex cheese dip with green chiles and tomato, made for tortilla chips.","2 tbsp|butter;1/2|onion|finely diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes with green chiles|10 oz, drained;1/2 cup|milk;8 oz|american cheese|cubed;4 oz|cream cheese|cubed;1 tsp|cumin;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;|tortilla chips|for serving","Melt the butter in a saucepan and cook the onion for 4 minutes until soft.|Add the garlic and cumin and cook 30 seconds.|Add the tomatoes with green chiles and the milk and warm over low heat.|Stir in the american cheese and cream cheese a handful at a time until smooth.|Stir in the cilantro and serve warm with chips.","Tex-Mex"],
[3059,"Tres Leches Cake","treats","🍰",120,"Medium",9,12,"Airy sponge cake soaked in three milks and topped with whipped cream.","1 cup|flour;1 1/2 tsp|baking powder;5|eggs|separated;1 cup|sugar;1/3 cup|milk;1 tsp|vanilla;1 can|evaporated milk|12 oz;1 can|sweetened condensed milk|14 oz;1/2 cup|heavy cream;2 cup|heavy cream|whipped, for topping;2 tbsp|powdered sugar;1/2 tsp|cinnamon","Heat the oven to 350°F and grease a 9x13 inch pan.|Beat the yolks with 3/4 cup sugar until pale, then mix in the milk and vanilla and fold in the flour and baking powder.|Whip the whites with the remaining sugar to stiff peaks and fold into the batter.|Bake 25 to 30 minutes until golden, then cool completely.|Whisk the evaporated milk, condensed milk and 1/2 cup cream and pierce the cake all over with a fork.|Pour the milk mixture slowly over the cake and chill at least 4 hours.|Whip the 2 cups cream with the powdered sugar, spread over the cake and dust with cinnamon.","Mexican"],
[3060,"Enchiladas Suizas","comfort","🌯",50,"Medium",9,6,"Chicken enchiladas smothered in creamy tomatillo sauce and melted cheese.","1 lb|tomatillos|husked;2|poblano peppers|roasted, seeded;1/2|onion;3 clove|garlic;1/2 cup|cilantro;1 cup|heavy cream;1/2 cup|chicken broth;3 cup|rotisserie chicken|shredded;12|corn tortillas;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;|salt|to taste","Simmer the tomatillos in water for 8 minutes until soft and drain.|Blend them with the poblanos, onion, garlic, cilantro, cream, broth and salt until smooth.|Warm the tortillas briefly in the oil so they stay pliable.|Fill each tortilla with chicken and a little cheese, roll, and place seam side down in a baking dish.|Pour the sauce over and top with the remaining cheese.|Bake at 375°F for 20 minutes until bubbling and golden.","Mexican"],
[3061,"Chicken Fajitas","quick","🌮",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Sizzling marinated chicken with peppers and onions, wrapped in warm flour tortillas.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|sliced in strips;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|lime juice;2 tsp|chili powder;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|salt;2|bell pepper|sliced;1|onion|sliced;8|flour tortillas|warmed;1/2 cup|sour cream;1|avocado|sliced","Toss the chicken with 1 tbsp oil, lime juice, chili powder, cumin, paprika, garlic powder and salt and marinate 15 minutes.|Heat a large cast iron skillet over high heat with 1 tbsp oil.|Cook the chicken 5 to 6 minutes until browned and 165°F inside, then remove.|Add the remaining oil and cook the peppers and onion 5 minutes until charred at the edges.|Return the chicken to the pan and toss.|Serve in warm tortillas with sour cream and avocado.","Tex-Mex"],
[3062,"Beef Burrito Bowl","quick","🥗",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Seasoned ground beef over rice with black beans, corn, salsa and all the toppings.","1 lb|ground beef;2 tbsp|taco seasoning;1/4 cup|water;2 cup|rice|cooked;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;1 cup|frozen corn|thawed;1 cup|salsa;1|avocado|diced;1 cup|lettuce|shredded;1/2 cup|cheddar|shredded;1/4 cup|sour cream;1|lime|cut in wedges","Brown the beef in a skillet over medium-high heat for 6 to 7 minutes and drain the fat.|Stir in the taco seasoning and water and simmer 3 minutes until thick.|Warm the black beans and corn separately in a small pan.|Divide the rice among bowls.|Top with beef, beans, corn, salsa, avocado, lettuce, cheese and sour cream.|Serve with lime wedges.","Tex-Mex"],
[3063,"Sopes","lunch","🫓",45,"Medium",8,6,"Thick masa cups with a pinched rim, crisped and topped with beans, meat, lettuce and crumbly cheese.","2 cup|masa harina;1 1/2 cup|warm water;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 cup|vegetable oil;1 cup|refried beans;1 cup|chicken breast|cooked and shredded;1 cup|lettuce|shredded;1/2 cup|salsa;1/2 cup|cotija cheese|crumbled;1/4 cup|sour cream","Mix the masa harina, warm water and salt into a soft dough and rest 10 minutes.|Form 12 balls and press each into a 3 inch disc about 1/4 inch thick.|Cook on a dry hot skillet 2 minutes per side until lightly set.|Pinch a raised rim around each disc while still warm.|Fry the sopes in the oil 1 to 2 minutes per side until crisp and golden.|Spread with beans, then top with chicken, lettuce, salsa, cotija and sour cream.","Mexican"],
[3064,"Flautas","lunch","🌯",40,"Easy",8,4,"Tightly rolled corn tortillas stuffed with chicken and fried until shatteringly crisp.","2 cup|rotisserie chicken|shredded;1/2 cup|salsa;1 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;12|corn tortillas;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 cup|lettuce|shredded;1/2 cup|sour cream;1|avocado|diced","Mix the chicken with the salsa and cheese.|Warm the tortillas wrapped in a damp towel in the microwave for 30 seconds so they bend without cracking.|Spoon filling along one edge, roll tightly, and secure with a toothpick.|Heat the oil in a skillet to 350°F.|Fry the flautas seam side down 2 to 3 minutes per side until golden and crisp.|Drain on paper towels and serve over lettuce with sour cream and avocado.","Mexican"],
[3065,"Menudo","soup","🍲",240,"Medium",9.5,8,"Traditional red chile tripe and hominy soup, long simmered and eaten with oregano, onion and lime.","2 lb|beef tripe|cleaned and cut in pieces;1 lb|beef stew meat|cut in chunks;1|onion|halved;1 head|garlic|halved;10 cup|water;6|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;2|dried ancho chiles|stemmed and seeded;1 can|hominy|25 oz, drained;1 tbsp|oregano;2 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|onion|diced, for serving;2|lime|cut in wedges","Simmer the tripe, beef, halved onion, garlic and salt in the water for 2 1/2 to 3 hours until the tripe is tender, skimming the foam.|Soak the chiles in hot water for 15 minutes, then blend with 1 cup of broth until smooth and strain.|Stir the chile sauce and hominy into the pot.|Simmer 30 minutes more and adjust the salt.|Serve hot topped with diced onion, oregano and lime.","Mexican"],
[3066,"Huevos Rancheros","breakfast","🍳",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Fried eggs on crisp corn tortillas smothered in warm ranchero sauce with refried beans.","1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/2|onion|diced;1|jalapeno|minced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14.5 oz, fire roasted;1/2 tsp|cumin;8|corn tortillas;8|eggs;1 cup|refried beans|warmed;1/2 cup|cotija cheese|crumbled;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;|salt|to taste","Saute the onion and jalapeno in the oil for 4 minutes, then add the garlic and cumin for 30 seconds.|Add the tomatoes and simmer 8 minutes, then blend partly and season with salt.|Fry the tortillas in a little oil for 30 seconds per side until crisp but flexible.|Fry the eggs sunny side up.|Spread beans on two tortillas per plate, top with eggs, spoon over the sauce and finish with cotija and cilantro.","Mexican"],
[3067,"Beef Barbacoa","prep","🥩",240,"Easy",9,8,"Chipotle and adobo braised chuck, falling-apart tender, for tacos and burrito bowls.","3 lb|chuck roast|cut in large chunks;2|chipotle in adobo|chiles plus 2 tbsp sauce;1/4 cup|apple cider vinegar;1/4 cup|lime juice;5 clove|garlic;1 tbsp|cumin;1 tbsp|oregano;1/2 tsp|cloves|ground;2|bay leaves;1 cup|beef broth;2 tsp|salt;12|corn tortillas","Blend the chipotles, adobo, vinegar, lime juice, garlic, cumin, oregano, cloves and salt into a paste.|Place the beef in a slow cooker or Dutch oven with the sauce, bay leaves and broth.|Cook on low for 8 hours in the slow cooker, or covered at 300°F for 3 1/2 hours in the oven, until very tender.|Shred the beef and moisten with the cooking juices.|Serve in warm tortillas with onion, cilantro and lime.","Mexican"],
[3068,"Chicken Mole Poblano","comfort","🍗",120,"Medium",9,6,"Chicken simmered in Mexico's famed dark chile, nut and chocolate sauce, finished with sesame seeds.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;4|dried ancho chiles|stemmed and seeded;3|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;2|dried pasilla chiles|stemmed and seeded;2 tbsp|sesame seeds|plus more for garnish;1/4 cup|almonds;1/4 cup|raisins;1|tomatoes|roasted;1/2|onion;3 clove|garlic;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 slice|bread|toasted;2 oz|chocolate chips|dark;4 cup|chicken broth;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;|salt|to taste","Simmer the chicken in the broth with a little salt for 25 minutes until cooked, then set aside, saving the broth.|Toast the chiles in a dry pan for 30 seconds, then soak in hot water 20 minutes.|Fry the sesame, almonds, raisins, onion, garlic and bread in a little oil until browned.|Blend the chiles, fried ingredients, tomato, cinnamon and pepper with 2 cups of the broth until very smooth.|Fry the sauce in the oil in a large pot for 10 minutes, stirring, until it darkens.|Add the chocolate and 2 more cups of broth and simmer 30 minutes, seasoning with salt.|Add the chicken and simmer 10 minutes, then garnish with sesame seeds and serve with rice.","Mexican"],
[3069,"Loaded Beef Nachos","sides","🧀",25,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Sheet pan nachos layered with seasoned beef, beans and melted cheese, finished with fresh toppings.","1 lb|ground beef;2 tbsp|taco seasoning;10 oz|tortilla chips;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;1/2 cup|pickled jalapenos|sliced;1 cup|pico de gallo;1/2 cup|sour cream;1|avocado|diced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Brown the beef in a skillet 6 minutes, drain, and stir in the taco seasoning with 1/4 cup water.|Spread the chips over a sheet pan.|Scatter the beef, beans and cheese over the chips.|Bake at 400°F for 7 to 8 minutes until the cheese melts.|Top with jalapenos, pico, sour cream, avocado and cilantro and serve immediately.","Tex-Mex"],
[3070,"Carne Guisada","comfort","🍲",120,"Easy",9,6,"Tex-Mex stewed beef in a rich cumin-spiced gravy, spooned into flour tortillas.","2 lb|beef stew meat|cut in small cubes;2 tbsp|flour;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes with green chiles|10 oz;1 tbsp|chili powder;2 tsp|cumin;2 cup|beef broth;1 tsp|salt;8|flour tortillas|warmed","Toss the beef with the flour, salt and half the cumin.|Brown the beef in the oil in batches in a Dutch oven and set aside.|Cook the onion and bell pepper 5 minutes, then add the garlic, chili powder and remaining cumin for 1 minute.|Return the beef and add the tomatoes and broth.|Cover and simmer on low for 1 1/2 hours until tender and the gravy thickens.|Serve in flour tortillas or over rice.","Tex-Mex"],
[3071,"Cuban Picadillo","quick","🍛",35,"Easy",8.5,6,"Savory-sweet ground beef with tomato, olives and raisins, served over rice.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|oregano;1/2 cup|olives|green, sliced;1/3 cup|raisins;2 tbsp|white wine|dry;2|bay leaves;|salt|to taste;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Saute the onion and bell pepper in the oil for 5 minutes, then add the garlic for 1 minute.|Add the beef and cook 7 to 8 minutes until browned, breaking it up.|Stir in the cumin, oregano, tomato sauce, wine and bay leaves.|Simmer 15 minutes until thick.|Stir in the olives and raisins and cook 5 minutes more, seasoning with salt.|Serve over white rice.","Cuban"],
[3072,"Lechon Asado","comfort","🐖",300,"Easy",9,10,"Cuban roast pork marinated in garlicky sour orange mojo until fork tender.","5 lb|pork shoulder|bone-in;1 head|garlic|peeled;1 cup|orange juice;1/2 cup|lime juice;2 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|oregano;1 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|salt;1/4 cup|olive oil;1|onion|sliced","Blend the garlic with the orange juice, lime juice, cumin, oregano, pepper, salt and oil to make the mojo.|Poke the pork all over with a knife and pour the mojo over it in a pan or bag.|Marinate in the refrigerator for 12 to 24 hours.|Lay the onion slices in a roasting pan, set the pork on top, and pour in the marinade.|Cover with foil and roast at 325°F for 4 hours, then uncover and roast 30 minutes more until browned and 195°F inside.|Rest 20 minutes and shred, spooning pan juices over the top.","Cuban"],
[3073,"Moros y Cristianos","sides","🍚",50,"Easy",7.5,6,"Cuban black beans and white rice cooked together with garlic, cumin and green pepper.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|oregano;1 1/2 cup|rice|long grain;2 can|black beans|15 oz each, with liquid;1 cup|chicken broth;2|bay leaves;1 tbsp|white vinegar;1 tsp|salt","Saute the onion and bell pepper in the oil for 5 minutes, then add the garlic, cumin and oregano for 1 minute.|Drain the beans, saving the liquid, and add enough broth to the liquid to make 3 cups.|Add the rice and bay leaves to the pot and stir for 1 minute.|Pour in the bean liquid mixture, salt and vinegar and bring to a boil.|Cover and cook on low 18 minutes, then stir in the beans.|Cover 5 minutes more, discard the bay leaves and fluff.","Cuban"],
[3074,"Tostones","sides","🍌",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Twice-fried green plantain discs, crisp outside and starchy inside, with a garlic dip.","3|green plantains;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;|coarse salt|to taste;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|olive oil;1 tbsp|lime juice","Peel the plantains and cut into 1 inch rounds.|Fry in 325°F oil for 3 minutes per side until pale golden.|Remove and smash each piece flat to 1/3 inch with the bottom of a glass.|Fry again at 375°F for 2 minutes per side until crisp and golden.|Drain, sprinkle with salt, and serve with a quick mojo made from the garlic, olive oil and lime juice.","Cuban"],
[3075,"Maduros (Fried Sweet Plantains)","sides","🍌",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Ripe plantains fried until caramelized, soft and sweet.","3|plantains|very ripe, black skins;1/2 cup|vegetable oil;|salt|pinch","Peel the plantains and slice on the diagonal 1/2 inch thick.|Heat the oil in a skillet over medium heat.|Fry the slices 2 to 3 minutes per side until deep golden and caramelized at the edges.|Drain on paper towels and sprinkle with a pinch of salt.","Cuban"],
[3076,"Arroz con Pollo","comfort","🍗",60,"Medium",9,6,"One-pot chicken and yellow rice with peppers, peas and a splash of beer.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;2 cup|rice|long grain;3 cup|chicken broth;1 cup|frozen peas;1/2 cup|olives|green","Season the chicken with salt and brown in the oil in a wide Dutch oven for 4 minutes per side, then set aside.|Cook the onion and bell pepper in the drippings for 5 minutes, then add the garlic, cumin, paprika and turmeric for 1 minute.|Stir in the tomato sauce and rice and toast 2 minutes.|Add the broth and bring to a boil, then nestle the chicken in the rice.|Cover and cook on low for 25 minutes until the rice is tender.|Scatter over the peas and olives, cover 5 minutes, and serve.","Cuban"],
[3077,"Vaca Frita","comfort","🥩",150,"Medium",9,6,"Cuban shredded flank steak seared crisp and tossed with lime, garlic and onions.","2 lb|flank steak;1|onion|half quartered, half sliced;6 clove|garlic;2|bay leaves;4 cup|water;1/3 cup|lime juice;2 tbsp|olive oil;2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|oregano;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Simmer the steak with the quartered onion, 2 cloves garlic, bay leaves and 1 tsp salt in the water for 1 1/2 hours until tender.|Cool slightly and shred the beef finely.|Mince the remaining garlic and toss the beef with the lime juice, garlic, cumin, oregano, pepper and remaining salt and marinate 30 minutes.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over high heat and sear the beef in batches 4 to 5 minutes, undisturbed, until crisp and browned.|Cook the sliced onion in the same pan until golden, then toss with the beef and serve with rice and beans.","Cuban"],
[3078,"Coxinha","treats","🍗",90,"Medium",9,24,"Teardrop-shaped Brazilian snacks of creamy shredded chicken in dough, breaded and fried.","2 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|butter;1 1/2 cup|flour;1 1/2 cup|rotisserie chicken|finely shredded;1/2|onion|finely diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;4 oz|cream cheese;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;2|eggs|beaten;1 1/2 cup|breadcrumbs;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;|salt|to taste","Cook the onion and garlic in 1 tbsp oil for 4 minutes, then mix in the chicken, cream cheese, parsley and salt for the filling and chill.|Bring the broth and butter to a boil, add all the flour at once, and stir over low heat 3 to 4 minutes until a smooth dough pulls from the pan.|Knead the dough on a counter until smooth and cool enough to handle.|Take a golf ball of dough, flatten in your palm, add a spoonful of filling, and shape into a teardrop sealing the edges.|Dip in the beaten eggs and roll in breadcrumbs.|Fry in 350°F oil for 3 to 4 minutes per batch until deep golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve warm.","Brazilian"],
[3079,"Farofa","sides","🍚",15,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Toasted cassava flour with bacon and onion, sprinkled over rice, beans and grilled meats.","4 slice|bacon|diced;2 tbsp|butter;1/2|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|cassava flour|farinha de mandioca, toasted;2|eggs|beaten;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste","Cook the bacon in a large skillet over medium heat for 6 minutes until crisp and remove with a slotted spoon.|Add the butter, onion and garlic to the bacon fat and cook 4 minutes.|Push the onion aside, pour in the eggs and scramble until set.|Add the cassava flour a little at a time, stirring 3 to 4 minutes until golden and toasty.|Fold in the bacon and parsley and season with salt.","Brazilian"],
[3080,"Lomo Saltado","quick","🥩",35,"Easy",8.5,4,"Peruvian beef stir-fry with onion, tomato and fries in a soy and vinegar sauce, served with rice.","1 1/2 lb|sirloin steak|cut in strips;3 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|red onion|cut in thick wedges;2|tomatoes|cut in wedges;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|minced;2 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1|jalapeno|sliced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1 lb|potatoes|cut in fries and fried;2 cup|rice|cooked;|salt|to taste","Toss the steak with 1 tbsp soy sauce, salt and pepper.|Heat a wok or large skillet until smoking and sear the beef in batches in the oil for 1 to 2 minutes until browned.|Add the onion, garlic, ginger and jalapeno and stir-fry 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, remaining soy sauce and the vinegar and toss 1 minute.|Return the beef, fold in the cilantro and the hot fried potatoes.|Serve immediately over white rice.","Peruvian"],
[3081,"Pollo a la Brasa","comfort","🍗",120,"Easy",9,4,"Peruvian rotisserie-style chicken marinated in garlic, cumin and soy, roasted until crisp and golden.","1|whole chicken|about 4 lb;6 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|lime juice;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tbsp|cumin;1 tbsp|paprika;1 tsp|oregano;1 tsp|black pepper;2 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|apple cider vinegar","Mix the garlic, soy sauce, lime juice, oil, cumin, paprika, oregano, pepper, salt and vinegar into a paste.|Rub the paste all over and under the skin of the chicken.|Marinate in the refrigerator at least 4 hours or overnight.|Roast on a rack at 450°F for 20 minutes, then reduce to 375°F.|Roast another 50 to 60 minutes until the thigh reaches 165°F and the skin is crisp.|Rest 10 minutes, carve, and serve with fries and a green sauce.","Peruvian"],
[3082,"Peruvian Ceviche","light","🐟",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Raw white fish cured in sharp lime juice with red onion, chile and cilantro, served cold.","1 1/2 lb|cod|very fresh, cut in 1/2 inch cubes;3/4 cup|lime juice|fresh;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1|jalapeno|minced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|salt;1|sweet potatoes|boiled and sliced;1 cup|corn|boiled, or cooked kernels","Rinse the sliced onion in cold water for 5 minutes and drain.|Combine the fish with the salt, garlic and jalapeno in a bowl.|Pour in the lime juice and stir.|Refrigerate for 10 to 15 minutes until the fish turns opaque on the outside.|Fold in the onion and cilantro and serve right away with sweet potato and corn.","Peruvian"],
[3083,"Aji de Gallina","comfort","🍛",60,"Medium",9,6,"Shredded chicken in a creamy yellow chile and walnut sauce over rice and potatoes.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast;4 cup|chicken broth;4 slice|bread|crusts removed;1 cup|milk;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|finely diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|aji amarillo paste;1/2 cup|walnuts;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;4|potatoes|boiled and sliced;2 cup|rice|cooked;4|eggs|hard boiled;1/2 cup|olives|black;|salt|to taste","Poach the chicken in the broth for 20 minutes until cooked, then shred and reserve the broth.|Soak the bread in the milk, then blend with the walnuts and 1 cup of the broth until smooth.|Cook the onion in the oil for 6 minutes, then add the garlic and aji amarillo paste for 3 minutes.|Stir in the blended mixture and another cup of broth and simmer 10 minutes.|Add the shredded chicken and parmesan and simmer until thick and creamy, seasoning with salt.|Serve over potato slices with rice, halved eggs and olives.","Peruvian"],
[3084,"Papa a la Huancaina","sides","🥔",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"Boiled potatoes in a creamy, spicy yellow cheese sauce, a Peruvian starter.","2 lb|potatoes|boiled and sliced;1/2 cup|aji amarillo paste;8 oz|feta;1/2 cup|evaporated milk;4|crackers|saltines;1 clove|garlic;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;4|eggs|hard boiled;1/2 cup|olives|black;|lettuce|leaves, for serving","Blend the aji amarillo, feta, evaporated milk, crackers, garlic and oil until smooth and creamy.|Taste and adjust with a little salt or milk to reach a pourable thickness.|Line a platter with lettuce leaves.|Arrange the sliced potatoes on top.|Spoon the sauce generously over the potatoes and garnish with halved eggs and olives.","Peruvian"],
[3085,"Sesame Chicken","comfort","🍗",40,"Medium",9,4,"Crispy fried chicken pieces tossed in a glossy sweet-savory sauce and finished with toasted sesame seeds.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in 1 inch pieces;1|eggs|beaten;1/2 cup|cornstarch;1/4 cup|flour;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/4 cup|soy sauce;1/4 cup|honey;3 tbsp|brown sugar;2 tbsp|rice vinegar;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1/2 cup|chicken broth;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1 tbsp|cornstarch|mixed with 2 tbsp water;2 tbsp|sesame seeds|toasted;2|green onion|sliced","Toss the chicken with the egg and salt, then dredge in the cornstarch and flour mixed together, pressing to coat.|Heat the oil in a large skillet to 350°F.|Fry the chicken in batches for 4 to 5 minutes until golden and cooked through, then drain on a rack.|In a saucepan combine soy sauce, honey, brown sugar, vinegar, sesame oil, broth, garlic and ginger and simmer 3 minutes.|Stir in the cornstarch slurry and simmer 1 to 2 minutes until the sauce is thick and glossy.|Toss the chicken in the sauce, sprinkle with sesame seeds and green onion, and serve over rice.","Chinese"],
[3086,"Honey Walnut Shrimp","comfort","🍤",35,"Medium",9,4,"Crispy battered shrimp in a creamy honey-mayo sauce, topped with candied walnuts.","1 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined, large;1/2 cup|cornstarch;1|eggs|beaten;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/3 cup|mayonnaise;2 tbsp|honey;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tbsp|sweetened condensed milk|optional;1 cup|walnuts|halves;1/4 cup|sugar;2 cup|water|for boiling walnuts;|salt|to taste;1 cup|broccoli|steamed florets, for serving","Boil the walnuts in water for 5 minutes, drain well, and toss with the sugar until coated.|Fry the sugared walnuts in 350°F oil for 2 to 3 minutes until deep golden, then spread on parchment to cool.|Whisk the mayonnaise, honey, lemon juice and condensed milk in a large bowl.|Toss the shrimp with a pinch of salt and the egg, then coat well in cornstarch.|Fry the shrimp in batches for 2 to 3 minutes until crisp and golden, and drain.|Toss the hot shrimp in the sauce, top with the walnuts, and serve with steamed broccoli and rice.","Chinese"],
[3087,"Mongolian Beef","quick","🥩",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Tender sliced flank steak seared crisp and coated in a sweet, garlicky soy-brown sugar sauce with green onions.","1 1/2 lb|flank steak|sliced thin against the grain;1/4 cup|cornstarch;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 tbsp|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1/2 cup|soy sauce;1/2 cup|water;3/4 cup|brown sugar;1 tbsp|hoisin sauce;6|green onion|cut in 2 inch pieces","Toss the steak with the cornstarch until evenly coated.|Heat the oil in a large skillet or wok over medium-high heat and sear the beef in batches for 1 to 2 minutes until browned, then remove.|Pour off all but 1 tablespoon of oil and cook the garlic and ginger for 30 seconds.|Add the soy sauce, water, brown sugar and hoisin and simmer 3 to 4 minutes until slightly thickened.|Return the beef to the pan with the green onions and toss for 1 minute.|Serve over steamed rice.","Chinese"],
[3088,"Pepper Steak","quick","🫑",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Tender strips of steak stir-fried with bell peppers and onion in a savory soy-ginger sauce.","1 1/2 lb|flank steak|sliced thin against the grain;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|cornstarch;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2|bell pepper|sliced in strips;1|onion|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1/2 cup|beef broth;2 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|cornstarch|mixed with 1 tbsp water;|black pepper|to taste","Toss the steak with 2 tablespoons soy sauce and 1 tablespoon cornstarch and let sit 10 minutes.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok or large skillet over high heat and sear the steak 2 minutes, then remove.|Add the remaining oil and stir-fry the peppers and onion for 3 minutes until crisp-tender.|Add the garlic and ginger and cook 30 seconds.|Stir in the broth, oyster sauce, sugar and black pepper, return the beef, and bring to a simmer.|Stir in the cornstarch slurry and cook 1 minute until glossy, then serve over rice.","Chinese"],
[3089,"Crab Rangoon","sides","🥟",35,"Easy",7.5,6,"Crispy fried wonton wrappers filled with a creamy, lightly sweet crab and cream cheese mixture.","8 oz|cream cheese|softened;6 oz|crab meat|canned or imitation, drained;2|green onion|minced;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|worcestershire;1 tsp|soy sauce;24|wonton wrappers;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/4 cup|sweet chili sauce|for dipping","Mix the cream cheese, crab, green onion, garlic, worcestershire and soy sauce until combined.|Place about 2 teaspoons of filling in the center of each wrapper.|Wet the edges with water, then fold corners up to the center and pinch to seal into a four-pointed star or fold into a triangle.|Heat 1 inch of oil in a skillet to 350°F.|Fry in batches for 1 to 2 minutes per side until golden, then drain on paper towels.|Serve warm with sweet chili sauce.","Chinese"],
[3090,"Pork Fried Rice","quick","🍚",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Day-old rice stir-fried with diced pork, scrambled egg, peas and carrots.","4 cup|rice|cooked and chilled, day-old;1/2 lb|pork shoulder|diced small;2 tbsp|soy sauce;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;2|eggs|beaten;1/2 cup|frozen peas;1/2 cup|carrots|diced small;1/2|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sesame oil;3|green onion|sliced;|black pepper|to taste","Toss the pork with 1 tablespoon soy sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok over high heat and cook the pork 3 to 4 minutes until browned and cooked through, then remove.|Scramble the eggs in the same wok for 30 seconds, break into pieces, and remove.|Heat the remaining oil and stir-fry the onion, carrots and peas for 2 minutes, adding the garlic for the last 30 seconds.|Add the rice, breaking up clumps, and stir-fry 3 minutes until hot and slightly toasted.|Add the remaining soy sauce, oyster sauce, sesame oil and pepper, return the pork and egg, and toss with the green onions.","Chinese"],
[3091,"Chicken Chow Mein","quick","🍜",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Stir-fried noodles with chicken, cabbage, carrots and celery in a savory soy-oyster sauce.","8 oz|lo mein noodles;1 lb|chicken breast|sliced thin;1 tbsp|cornstarch;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 cup|cabbage|shredded;1|carrots|julienned;2 stalk|celery|sliced thin;1|onion|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|sesame oil;1 cup|bean sprouts;|black pepper|to taste","Cook the noodles according to the package, drain, rinse and toss with a little oil.|Toss the chicken with the cornstarch and a splash of soy sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok over high heat and cook the chicken 3 to 4 minutes until done, then remove.|Add 1 tablespoon oil and stir-fry the onion, celery, carrot and cabbage for 3 minutes.|Add the garlic, noodles, remaining soy sauce, oyster sauce, sugar and pepper and toss for 2 to 3 minutes.|Return the chicken, add the bean sprouts and sesame oil, and toss 1 minute before serving.","Chinese"],
[3092,"Dan Dan Noodles","quick","🍜",30,"Medium",8.5,4,"Sichuan noodles topped with spicy minced pork in a sesame, chili oil and soy sauce.","12 oz|lo mein noodles|or fresh wheat noodles;1/2 lb|ground pork;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;2 tbsp|sesame paste|or tahini or peanut butter;3 tbsp|chili oil;1 tsp|sichuan peppercorns|toasted and ground;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|sugar;1/2 cup|chicken broth;2 cup|spinach|or bok choy, blanched;3|green onion|sliced;2 tbsp|peanuts|crushed","Brown the pork in the oil over medium-high heat for 5 minutes, breaking it up, then add 1 tablespoon soy sauce and cook 1 minute more.|Whisk the sesame paste, remaining soy sauce, vinegar, chili oil, ground peppercorns, garlic, sugar and broth to make the sauce.|Cook the noodles per package directions and blanch the greens in the same water for 30 seconds.|Divide the sauce among four bowls.|Top with the noodles, greens and pork, then sprinkle with green onion and peanuts.|Toss everything together before eating.","Chinese"],
[3093,"Char Siu","comfort","🍖",240,"Medium",9,6,"Cantonese barbecued pork with a sticky, sweet-savory red glaze, roasted until caramelized at the edges.","2 lb|pork shoulder|cut into 2 inch strips;1/4 cup|hoisin sauce;1/4 cup|honey;3 tbsp|soy sauce;3 tbsp|brown sugar;2 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|five spice powder;|red food coloring|optional;2 tbsp|honey|for basting","Whisk the hoisin, honey, soy sauce, brown sugar, oyster sauce, vinegar, garlic and five spice.|Reserve 1/4 cup of marinade, then coat the pork in the rest and refrigerate 4 hours or overnight.|Heat the oven to 425°F and set the pork on a rack over a foil-lined pan with a little water in the pan.|Roast 20 minutes, then brush with the reserved marinade and flip.|Roast another 20 to 25 minutes, brushing again, until the edges caramelize and the pork reaches 160°F.|Brush with honey, rest 10 minutes, and slice across the grain.","Chinese"],
[3094,"Cashew Chicken","quick","🥜",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Stir-fried chicken and crisp vegetables in a savory brown sauce with roasted cashews.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in 1 inch pieces;1 tbsp|cornstarch;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|bell pepper|diced;2 stalk|celery|sliced;4 oz|mushrooms|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1/2 cup|chicken broth;3 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|hoisin sauce;1 tsp|rice vinegar;1 tsp|cornstarch|mixed with 1 tbsp water;3/4 cup|cashews|roasted;2|green onion|sliced","Toss the chicken with 1 tablespoon cornstarch.|Heat 2 tablespoons oil in a wok over high heat and cook the chicken 4 to 5 minutes until browned and cooked through, then remove.|Add the remaining oil and stir-fry the pepper, celery and mushrooms for 3 minutes.|Add the garlic and ginger for 30 seconds.|Stir in the broth, soy sauce, oyster sauce, hoisin and vinegar, then the slurry, and simmer 1 minute.|Return the chicken, add the cashews and green onion, toss, and serve over rice.","Chinese"],
[3095,"Lemon Chicken","comfort","🍋",40,"Medium",9,4,"Crispy battered chicken with a bright, tangy lemon sauce, a Chinese-American takeout favorite.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in strips;1/2 cup|cornstarch;1/4 cup|flour;1|eggs;1 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;3/4 cup|chicken broth;1/3 cup|sugar;1/4 cup|lemon juice;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|cornstarch|mixed with 2 tbsp water;1|lemon|sliced thin;2|green onion|sliced","Whisk the cornstarch, flour, baking powder, salt, egg and a few tablespoons of cold water into a thin batter and coat the chicken.|Heat the oil to 350°F in a deep skillet.|Fry the chicken in batches for 4 to 5 minutes until golden and crisp, then drain.|Simmer the broth, sugar, lemon juice and soy sauce for 2 minutes.|Stir in the cornstarch slurry and cook until thickened and glossy.|Pour the sauce over the chicken, top with lemon slices and green onion, and serve with rice.","Chinese"],
[3096,"Pork Potstickers","sides","🥟",60,"Medium",7.5,6,"Pan-fried dumplings with a juicy pork and cabbage filling, crisp on the bottom and tender on top.","1 lb|ground pork;2 cup|cabbage|finely chopped, napa preferred;3|green onion|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|sugar;1 tbsp|cornstarch;40|dumpling wrappers|round;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/2 cup|water;3 tbsp|soy sauce|for dipping;1 tbsp|rice vinegar|for dipping","Toss the chopped cabbage with a pinch of salt, let sit 10 minutes, and squeeze out the liquid.|Mix the pork, cabbage, green onion, ginger, garlic, soy sauce, sesame oil, sugar and cornstarch until sticky.|Put a heaping teaspoon of filling in each wrapper, wet the edge, and fold and pleat to seal.|Heat the oil in a nonstick skillet over medium-high heat and arrange the dumplings flat side down.|Fry 2 minutes until golden, then add the water, cover, and steam 6 to 7 minutes.|Uncover and cook until the water evaporates and the bottoms re-crisp, then serve with the soy and vinegar dip.","Chinese"],
[3097,"Scallion Pancakes","sides","🥞",60,"Medium",7.5,4,"Flaky, chewy, flatbread-style pancakes layered with sesame oil and green onions and pan-fried until crisp.","2 cup|flour;3/4 cup|water|boiling hot;1/2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|sesame oil;1 cup|green onion|finely sliced;1/4 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;3 tbsp|soy sauce|for dipping;1 tbsp|rice vinegar|for dipping","Mix the flour and salt, stir in the hot water until shaggy, then knead 5 minutes until smooth and let rest covered for 30 minutes.|Divide the dough into 4 pieces and roll each into a thin 8 inch circle.|Brush with sesame oil, sprinkle with salt and green onions, and roll into a tight log.|Coil the log into a spiral, tuck the end under, and flatten with a rolling pin to about 1/4 inch.|Fry in a skillet with a few tablespoons of oil over medium heat 3 minutes per side until golden and crisp.|Cut into wedges and serve with soy-vinegar dip.","Chinese"],
[3098,"Hunan Beef","quick","🌶️",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Spicy, savory stir-fried beef and broccoli with dried chilies and garlic in a Hunan-style sauce.","1 1/2 lb|flank steak|sliced thin against the grain;1 tbsp|cornstarch;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 cup|broccoli|small florets;1|bell pepper|sliced;5|dried red chilies|whole;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;1/4 cup|soy sauce;2 tbsp|hoisin sauce;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;1 tbsp|sugar;1/2 cup|beef broth;1 tsp|cornstarch|mixed with 1 tbsp water","Toss the steak with 1 tablespoon cornstarch and a splash of soy sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok over high heat and sear the beef 2 minutes, then remove.|Add the remaining oil and stir-fry the broccoli and pepper for 3 minutes, adding a splash of water to steam.|Add the chilies, garlic and ginger and cook 30 seconds.|Stir in the soy sauce, hoisin, vinegar, sugar and broth and bring to a simmer.|Return the beef, stir in the slurry, cook 1 minute until glossy, and serve over rice.","Chinese"],
[3099,"Moo Shu Pork","comfort","🌯",35,"Medium",9,4,"Stir-fried pork, egg and shredded cabbage in hoisin sauce, wrapped in warm thin pancakes.","1 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|cornstarch;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;3|eggs|beaten;3 cup|cabbage|shredded;1|carrots|julienned;4 oz|mushrooms|sliced;4|green onion|cut in 2 inch strips;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|grated;2 tbsp|hoisin sauce|plus more for spreading;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|sesame oil;8|flour tortillas|small, or mandarin pancakes","Marinate the pork in 1 tablespoon soy sauce and the cornstarch for 10 minutes.|Scramble the eggs in 1 tablespoon oil in a wok until just set, then remove.|Stir-fry the pork in 1 tablespoon oil over high heat for 3 minutes, then remove.|Add the last tablespoon of oil and stir-fry the cabbage, carrot, mushrooms, garlic and ginger for 3 to 4 minutes.|Return the pork and eggs, add the hoisin, soy sauce, sesame oil and green onions, and toss 1 minute.|Warm the tortillas, spread each with hoisin, fill with the mixture, and roll up.","Chinese"],
[3100,"Beef Chow Fun","quick","🍜",30,"Medium",8.5,4,"Wide rice noodles wok-fried with tender beef, bean sprouts and green onions in a savory soy sauce.","1 lb|rice noodles|fresh wide, or dried and soaked;3/4 lb|flank steak|sliced thin;1 tbsp|cornstarch;4 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|dark soy sauce;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sugar;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|bean sprouts;4|green onion|cut in 2 inch pieces;1/2|onion|sliced;|black pepper|to taste","Toss the steak with the cornstarch and 1 tablespoon soy sauce and let sit 10 minutes.|Mix the remaining soy sauce, dark soy, oyster sauce and sugar.|Heat 2 tablespoons oil in a wok over very high heat and sear the beef 1 to 2 minutes, then remove.|Add 2 more tablespoons oil, stir-fry the onion and garlic 30 seconds, then add the noodles and gently toss for 2 minutes.|Pour in the sauce and toss until the noodles are evenly colored.|Return the beef and add the sprouts, green onion and pepper, toss 1 minute, and serve immediately.","Chinese"],
[3101,"Salt and Pepper Shrimp","light","🦐",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Lightly crisp shrimp wok-tossed with garlic, chilies and a peppery salt seasoning.","1 lb|shrimp|large, shell-on or peeled;1/2 cup|cornstarch;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper|freshly ground;1/2 tsp|five spice powder;4 clove|garlic|minced;2|jalapeno|sliced thin;3|green onion|sliced","Pat the shrimp very dry and toss with the cornstarch to coat.|Heat the oil in a wok to 375°F and fry the shrimp in batches for 1 to 2 minutes until crisp and pink, then drain.|Pour off all but 1 tablespoon oil from the wok.|Stir-fry the garlic, jalapeno and green onions over high heat for 30 to 60 seconds until fragrant.|Return the shrimp and sprinkle with the salt, pepper and five spice.|Toss for 30 seconds and serve hot.","Chinese"],
[3102,"Twice-Cooked Pork","comfort","🥓",60,"Medium",9,4,"Sichuan classic of simmered pork belly sliced thin and stir-fried with leeks and spicy bean paste.","1 lb|pork belly|skin off;2 slice|ginger;3|green onion|whites cut in pieces;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|doubanjiang|spicy bean paste;1 tbsp|fermented black beans|optional;3|leeks|or green onion, sliced;1|bell pepper|sliced;3 clove|garlic|sliced;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1 tbsp|rice vinegar","Simmer the pork belly with the ginger and green onion whites in water to cover for 30 minutes until just cooked through.|Remove, cool for 15 minutes, then slice thinly.|Heat the oil in a wok over medium-high heat and fry the pork slices 3 to 4 minutes until the edges curl and crisp, then push aside.|Add the doubanjiang and black beans and fry 30 seconds until the oil turns red.|Add the garlic, leeks and pepper and stir-fry 2 to 3 minutes.|Add the soy sauce, sugar and vinegar, toss everything together, and serve with rice.","Chinese"],
[3103,"Beef Bulgogi","quick","🥩",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Thinly sliced beef marinated in a sweet soy, pear and garlic sauce, then seared until caramelized.","1 1/2 lb|sirloin steak|sliced very thin;1/4 cup|soy sauce;2 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|sesame oil;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;1/2|apple|grated, or Asian pear;1/2|onion|sliced thin;3|green onion|sliced;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the soy sauce, sugar, sesame oil, garlic, ginger, grated apple and pepper in a bowl.|Add the beef, onion and half the green onions and marinate at least 20 minutes, or up to overnight.|Heat the oil in a large skillet or cast iron over high heat.|Cook the beef in two batches for 2 to 3 minutes each until browned and caramelized at the edges.|Top with the remaining green onion and sesame seeds.|Serve with rice and lettuce leaves for wrapping.","Korean"],
[3104,"Bibimbap","comfort","🍚",50,"Medium",9,4,"Korean rice bowl topped with seasoned vegetables, marinated beef, a fried egg and spicy gochujang sauce.","4 cup|rice|cooked;1/2 lb|ground beef|or sliced beef;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tbsp|sugar;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|spinach;1|carrots|julienned;1|zucchini|julienned;1 cup|bean sprouts;4 oz|mushrooms|sliced;4|eggs;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|gochujang;1 tbsp|sesame oil|for sauce;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;1 tbsp|sesame seeds","Brown the beef with 1 tablespoon soy sauce, the sugar and half the garlic for 4 to 5 minutes and set aside.|Blanch the spinach 30 seconds, squeeze dry, and season with a little sesame oil, salt and garlic.|Blanch the bean sprouts 2 minutes, drain, and season with sesame oil and salt.|Saute the carrot, zucchini and mushrooms separately in a little oil for 2 to 3 minutes each, seasoning with salt.|Mix the gochujang, sesame oil, vinegar and 1 teaspoon sugar for the sauce.|Fry the eggs sunny side up, then arrange the rice, vegetables and beef in bowls, top with an egg, sesame seeds and sauce, and mix before eating.","Korean"],
[3105,"Kimchi Jjigae","soup","🍲",40,"Easy",9.5,4,"Hearty Korean stew of aged kimchi, pork and tofu simmered in a spicy, tangy broth.","2 cup|kimchi|aged, chopped, plus 1/2 cup juice;1/2 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin, or pork belly;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1/2|onion|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|gochugaru|Korean chili flakes;1 tbsp|gochujang;4 cup|water|or anchovy stock;14 oz|tofu|firm, sliced;3|green onion|sliced;1 tsp|sugar;1 tbsp|soy sauce","Heat the sesame oil in a pot over medium-high heat and cook the pork for 3 to 4 minutes until lightly browned.|Add the kimchi, onion and garlic and stir-fry 4 to 5 minutes.|Stir in the gochugaru, gochujang, sugar and soy sauce.|Add the kimchi juice and water and bring to a boil.|Reduce to a simmer, cover, and cook 20 minutes.|Add the tofu and green onion and simmer 5 more minutes, then serve with rice.","Korean"],
[3106,"Japchae","comfort","🍜",45,"Medium",9,6,"Chewy glass noodles stir-fried with beef and colorful vegetables in a sweet sesame-soy sauce.","8 oz|sweet potato starch noodles|dangmyeon;1/2 lb|sirloin steak|sliced thin;4 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|sesame oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1|carrots|julienned;1|onion|sliced;5 oz|spinach;4 oz|mushrooms|sliced;1|bell pepper|sliced thin;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;|black pepper|to taste","Marinate the beef in 1 tablespoon soy sauce, 1 teaspoon sugar, 1 teaspoon sesame oil and half the garlic.|Boil the noodles 6 to 7 minutes until chewy, drain, rinse, cut into shorter lengths, and toss with 1 tablespoon sesame oil.|Blanch the spinach for 30 seconds, squeeze dry, and season with a little soy sauce and sesame oil.|Stir-fry the onion, carrot, pepper and mushrooms separately in a little oil for 2 to 3 minutes each.|Cook the beef 2 to 3 minutes.|Toss everything with the remaining soy sauce, sugar, sesame oil, garlic, pepper and sesame seeds, and serve warm or at room temperature.","Korean"],
[3107,"Tteokbokki","quick","🌶️",30,"Easy",8.5,3,"Chewy rice cakes simmered in a sweet, spicy gochujang sauce with fish cakes and green onion.","1 lb|rice cakes|cylinder-shaped, soaked if hard;3 cup|water|or anchovy stock;3 tbsp|gochujang;1 tbsp|gochugaru;1 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|sugar;2 clove|garlic|minced;4 oz|fish cakes|sliced;3|green onion|cut in 2 inch pieces;2|eggs|hard-boiled;1 tsp|sesame seeds","Soak the rice cakes in warm water for 10 minutes if they are hard or refrigerated.|Bring the water to a boil in a wide pan and stir in the gochujang, gochugaru, soy sauce, sugar and garlic.|Add the rice cakes and simmer over medium heat for 8 to 10 minutes, stirring often.|Add the fish cakes and cook 3 to 4 minutes more until the sauce thickens and clings.|Add the green onion and eggs and cook 1 minute.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and serve hot.","Korean"],
[3108,"Korean Fried Chicken","comfort","🍗",60,"Medium",9,4,"Extra-crunchy double-fried chicken wings glazed in a sticky, sweet and spicy gochujang sauce.","2 lb|chicken wings|split, or drumettes;1/2 cup|cornstarch;1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|garlic powder;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;3 tbsp|gochujang;3 tbsp|honey;2 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tbsp|sesame seeds","Pat the wings very dry and toss with the cornstarch, flour, salt, pepper and garlic powder.|Heat 2 inches of oil to 325°F and fry the wings in batches 8 to 10 minutes until cooked, then drain.|Simmer the gochujang, honey, soy sauce, brown sugar, vinegar, garlic and sesame oil in a pan for 3 minutes until syrupy.|Raise the oil to 375°F and fry the wings again for 3 to 4 minutes until deeply crisp.|Toss the hot wings in the sauce until coated.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and serve right away.","Korean"],
[3109,"Galbi","comfort","🍖",50,"Medium",9,4,"Grilled Korean short ribs marinated in a sweet soy, pear and garlic sauce until tender and charred.","3 lb|beef short ribs|flanken cut, 1/2 inch thick;1/2 cup|soy sauce;1/4 cup|brown sugar;2 tbsp|sesame oil;1/2|apple|grated, or Asian pear;1/2|onion|grated;6 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;2 tbsp|rice wine|mirin or similar;3|green onion|sliced;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;|black pepper|to taste","Soak the ribs in cold water for 30 minutes to draw out excess blood, then drain and pat dry.|Mix the soy sauce, brown sugar, sesame oil, apple, onion, garlic, ginger, rice wine and pepper.|Marinate the ribs in the mixture in the refrigerator at least 4 hours or overnight.|Heat a grill or cast-iron pan over high heat.|Grill the ribs 3 to 4 minutes per side until charred and caramelized.|Sprinkle with green onion and sesame seeds, and serve with rice and lettuce.","Korean"],
[3110,"Sundubu Jjigae","soup","🍲",30,"Easy",9.5,2,"Bubbling Korean soft tofu stew with a spicy broth, clams or pork, and a cracked egg on top.","1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/4 lb|ground pork|or sliced pork;1 tbsp|gochugaru;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|water|or anchovy stock;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|fish sauce;1/2|onion|sliced;12 oz|soft tofu|sundubu;1/2 lb|clams|optional, scrubbed;2|green onion|sliced;1|eggs;1 tsp|sesame oil","Heat the oil in a small pot or stone bowl over medium heat and cook the pork 2 to 3 minutes.|Add the gochugaru and garlic and stir 30 seconds so the oil turns red.|Pour in the water, soy sauce and fish sauce, add the onion, and bring to a boil.|Add the clams if using and simmer until they open, about 4 minutes.|Spoon in the tofu in large chunks and simmer 4 to 5 minutes.|Crack the egg on top, add green onion and sesame oil, and serve boiling hot with rice.","Korean"],
[3111,"Kimchi Fried Rice","quick","🍳",20,"Very easy",8.5,2,"Day-old rice fried with tangy kimchi and gochujang, topped with a runny fried egg.","3 cup|rice|cooked and cold;1 cup|kimchi|chopped;2 tbsp|kimchi juice;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/4 lb|bacon|chopped, or spam;2|green onion|sliced;1 tbsp|gochujang;1 tsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|sesame oil;2|eggs;1 tsp|sesame seeds;1 tsp|sugar","Cook the bacon in a large skillet over medium-high heat for 3 to 4 minutes until crisp.|Add the kimchi and sugar and stir-fry 3 minutes.|Add the gochujang and cook 30 seconds.|Add the rice and kimchi juice, breaking up clumps, and fry 4 to 5 minutes until hot and slightly crisp.|Stir in the soy sauce, sesame oil and green onion.|Fry the eggs sunny side up, place on top, and sprinkle with sesame seeds.","Korean"],
[3112,"Dakgalbi","comfort","🌶️",45,"Easy",9,4,"Spicy stir-fried chicken with cabbage, sweet potato and rice cakes in a sweet gochujang sauce.","2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, bite-size pieces;3 tbsp|gochujang;2 tbsp|gochugaru;2 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|honey;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 cup|cabbage|chopped;1|sweet potatoes|sliced in half moons;1|onion|sliced;8 oz|rice cakes|optional;4|perilla leaves|optional;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the gochujang, gochugaru, soy sauce, sugar, honey, garlic, ginger, sesame oil and pepper.|Coat the chicken in the sauce and marinate at least 30 minutes.|Heat the oil in a large wide skillet over medium heat and add the sweet potato with a splash of water, covered, for 5 minutes.|Add the chicken, onion and cabbage and cook, stirring, 10 minutes.|Add the rice cakes and cook another 8 to 10 minutes until the chicken is cooked through and the sauce clings.|Top with perilla leaves and serve with rice.","Korean"],
[3113,"Pajeon","sides","🥞",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crispy Korean green onion pancakes with a chewy center, served with a tangy soy dipping sauce.","1 cup|flour;1/4 cup|cornstarch;1 1/4 cup|water|ice cold;1|eggs;1/2 tsp|salt;1 bunch|green onion|cut in 3 inch lengths;1/2 cup|shrimp|optional, chopped;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|soy sauce|for dipping;1 tbsp|rice vinegar|for dipping;1 tsp|gochugaru|for dipping;1 tsp|sesame seeds|for dipping","Whisk the flour, cornstarch, salt, egg and cold water into a thin batter.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat.|Spread half the green onions in the pan in a single layer, scatter the shrimp if using, and pour half the batter on top.|Cook 3 to 4 minutes until the bottom is golden and crisp, then flip and cook 3 minutes more, pressing down.|Repeat with remaining ingredients.|Mix the soy sauce, vinegar, gochugaru and sesame seeds and serve alongside.","Korean"],
[3114,"Jeyuk Bokkeum (Spicy Pork Stir-Fry)","quick","🥓",35,"Easy",8.5,4,"Thin pork slices stir-fried in a fiery sweet gochujang sauce with onion and green onion.","1 1/2 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;3 tbsp|gochujang;1 tbsp|gochugaru;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|honey;1 tbsp|sesame oil;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;1|onion|sliced;1|jalapeno|sliced;3|green onion|cut in 2 inch pieces;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tbsp|sesame seeds","Mix the gochujang, gochugaru, soy sauce, sugar, honey, sesame oil, garlic and ginger.|Coat the pork in the sauce and marinate for at least 20 minutes.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over high heat.|Add the pork and onion and stir-fry 6 to 8 minutes until the pork is cooked and the edges caramelize.|Add the jalapeno and green onion and cook 1 more minute.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and serve with rice and lettuce.","Korean"],
[3115,"Kimbap","lunch","🍙",60,"Medium",8,4,"Korean seaweed rice rolls filled with seasoned vegetables, egg, pickled radish and beef or ham.","3 cup|rice|cooked short-grain, warm;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|sesame seeds;4|nori sheets|roasted;4|eggs|beaten;1|carrots|julienned;1|cucumber|cut in long strips;4|pickled radish strips|danmuji;4 oz|spinach|blanched and squeezed;1/4 lb|ground beef|cooked with 1 tbsp soy sauce and 1 tsp sugar;1 tbsp|vegetable oil","Season the warm rice with sesame oil, salt and sesame seeds.|Beat the eggs with a pinch of salt, cook as a thin omelet in a little oil, and cut into long strips.|Saute the carrot for 1 to 2 minutes with a pinch of salt.|Lay a nori sheet shiny side down on a bamboo mat and spread a thin layer of rice, leaving the top inch bare.|Arrange the egg, carrot, cucumber, radish, spinach and beef in a line across the lower third.|Roll tightly, seal with a few grains of rice, brush with sesame oil, and slice into 1 inch rounds.","Korean"],
[3116,"Gyeran-jjim (Korean Steamed Egg)","sides","🥚",15,"Very easy",7.5,2,"Fluffy, savory steamed eggs puffed up in a hot stone pot, a classic Korean side.","4|eggs;3/4 cup|water|or anchovy stock;1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|fish sauce|or soy sauce;2|green onion|finely sliced;1 tsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|sesame seeds","Beat the eggs with the salt, fish sauce and half the green onions until smooth.|Strain the eggs through a sieve for a silky texture and stir in the water.|Pour the mixture into a small heatproof or stone pot.|Cook over medium-low heat, stirring gently, until it begins to set at the bottom.|Cover and cook on the lowest heat 8 to 10 minutes until puffed and set.|Drizzle with sesame oil and top with remaining green onion and sesame seeds.","Korean"],
[3117,"Chicken Katsu","comfort","🍗",35,"Easy",9,4,"Crispy panko-breaded chicken cutlets served with shredded cabbage and tangy-sweet katsu sauce.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|sliced in half to make 4 cutlets;1/2 cup|flour;2|eggs|beaten;1 1/2 cup|panko;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/4 cup|ketchup;2 tbsp|worcestershire;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;2 cup|cabbage|finely shredded;|rice|cooked, for serving","Pound the chicken to an even 1/2 inch thickness and season with salt and pepper.|Dredge in the flour, dip in the egg, then press into the panko.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat to about 350°F.|Fry the cutlets 3 to 4 minutes per side until deep golden and cooked through to 165°F.|Whisk together the ketchup, worcestershire, soy sauce and sugar for the katsu sauce.|Slice the cutlets and serve with cabbage, rice and sauce.","Japanese"],
[3118,"Chicken Teriyaki","quick","🍗",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Seared chicken thighs glazed in a glossy homemade teriyaki sauce of soy, mirin and sugar.","2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, skin-on;1/4 cup|soy sauce;1/4 cup|mirin;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|sake|or water;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cornstarch|mixed with 1 tbsp water;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;2|green onion|sliced","Whisk the soy sauce, mirin, sugar, sake, ginger and garlic.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and cook the chicken skin side down for 6 to 7 minutes until deeply golden.|Flip and cook 5 minutes more, then pour off excess fat.|Pour in the sauce and simmer 3 to 4 minutes, spooning it over the chicken.|Stir in the slurry and cook 1 minute until thick and glossy and the chicken reaches 165°F.|Slice the chicken, spoon the sauce over, and top with sesame seeds and green onion.","Japanese"],
[3119,"Tonkotsu Ramen","soup","🍜",240,"Medium",9.5,4,"Rich, milky pork bone broth ramen with tender chashu pork, soft egg and green onion.","3 lb|pork bones|neck or trotters, blanched;1 lb|pork belly|rolled and tied;1|onion|halved;1 head|garlic|halved;3 slice|ginger;4|green onion|whites and greens separated;1/4 cup|soy sauce;2 tbsp|mirin;2 tbsp|sugar;4|eggs|soft-boiled 6 1/2 minutes;14 oz|ramen noodles|fresh;1 tbsp|sesame oil;2 tbsp|soy sauce|for tare;1 tsp|salt|for tare;|nori|for topping","Boil the pork bones 10 minutes, drain, and scrub clean to remove scum.|Return the bones to a pot with 4 quarts water, onion, garlic, ginger and green onion whites and boil hard for 3 hours, topping up water, until the broth turns milky.|Meanwhile simmer the pork belly in 1/4 cup soy sauce, mirin, sugar and 1 1/2 cups water, covered, for 1 1/2 hours, turning occasionally.|Marinate the peeled soft-boiled eggs in some of the pork braising liquid.|Strain the broth, season with the 2 tablespoons soy sauce and salt, and keep hot.|Cook the noodles per package, divide into bowls, ladle in broth, and top with sliced pork, egg, green onion and a drizzle of sesame oil.","Japanese"],
[3120,"Gyudon","quick","🍚",25,"Easy",8.5,2,"Thinly sliced beef and onion simmered in a sweet dashi-soy broth and served over rice.","3/4 lb|ribeye steak|sliced paper thin;1|onion|sliced thin;3/4 cup|water|or dashi;3 tbsp|soy sauce;3 tbsp|mirin;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tsp|ginger|grated;2 cup|rice|cooked, hot;2|eggs|optional, soft yolks;|pickled ginger|beni shoga, optional;1|green onion|sliced","Combine the water, soy sauce, mirin, sugar and ginger in a skillet and bring to a simmer.|Add the onion and cook 5 minutes until soft.|Add the beef in one layer and cook 2 to 3 minutes, skimming any foam.|Simmer 3 more minutes until the beef is tender and the sauce is slightly reduced.|Divide the rice into bowls and spoon beef, onion and sauce over each.|Top with an egg yolk, pickled ginger and green onion.","Japanese"],
[3121,"Oyakodon","quick","🍳",25,"Easy",8.5,2,"Chicken and softly set egg simmered in sweet dashi-soy sauce over steamed rice.","3/4 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, bite-size pieces;1|onion|sliced thin;3/4 cup|water|or dashi;3 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|mirin;1 tbsp|sugar;4|eggs|lightly beaten;2 cup|rice|cooked, hot;2|green onion|sliced;|nori|shredded, optional","Combine the water, soy sauce, mirin and sugar in a skillet and bring to a simmer.|Add the onion and chicken and cook 6 to 7 minutes until the chicken is cooked through.|Pour two-thirds of the beaten egg over the top in a circle and cover for 1 minute.|Pour the remaining egg over, cover, and turn off the heat for 30 to 60 seconds until just softly set.|Divide the rice into two bowls.|Slide the chicken and egg over the rice and top with green onion and nori.","Japanese"],
[3122,"Yakisoba","quick","🍝",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Japanese stir-fried noodles with pork, cabbage and carrots in a tangy sweet-savory sauce.","3 packet|yakisoba noodles|or ramen noodles, loosened;1/2 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 cup|cabbage|chopped;1|carrots|julienned;1|onion|sliced;3 tbsp|worcestershire;2 tbsp|ketchup;2 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|sugar;2|green onion|sliced;|pickled ginger|and bonito flakes, to top","Mix the worcestershire, ketchup, oyster sauce, soy sauce and sugar for the sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok or large skillet over high heat and cook the pork 3 minutes until browned.|Add the onion, carrot and cabbage and stir-fry 3 to 4 minutes.|Push the vegetables aside, add the remaining oil, and loosen the noodles with a splash of water in the pan.|Pour in the sauce and toss everything together for 2 to 3 minutes.|Top with green onion, pickled ginger and bonito flakes.","Japanese"],
[3123,"Miso Soup","soup","🍲",15,"Very easy",9.5,4,"Light dashi broth with savory miso paste, soft tofu and wakame seaweed.","4 cup|water;2 tsp|dashi powder|or one 4-inch piece kombu;3 tbsp|miso paste;8 oz|tofu|silken, cubed;1 tbsp|wakame|dried seaweed;2|green onion|sliced","Soak the wakame in warm water for 5 minutes, then drain.|Bring the water and dashi powder to a gentle simmer in a pot.|Add the tofu and wakame and warm for 2 minutes.|Reduce the heat to low and place the miso in a ladle or small sieve.|Dissolve the miso into the broth by stirring, without letting it boil.|Serve immediately topped with green onion.","Japanese"],
[3124,"Okonomiyaki","lunch","🥞",35,"Medium",8,4,"Savory Japanese cabbage pancakes topped with okonomi sauce, mayo and bonito flakes.","1 cup|flour;3/4 cup|water|or dashi;3|eggs;4 cup|cabbage|finely shredded;3|green onion|sliced;1/2 cup|tempura scraps|optional;4 slice|bacon|thin pork belly or bacon;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/4 cup|ketchup;2 tbsp|worcestershire;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;|bonito flakes|and nori, to top","Whisk the flour, water and 1 egg until smooth, then fold in the cabbage, green onion and tempura scraps.|Stir the ketchup, worcestershire, oyster sauce and sugar to make the okonomi sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a large skillet over medium heat and pour in half the batter, shaping a thick round pancake.|Lay 2 bacon slices on top and cook 5 minutes until the bottom is deep golden.|Flip carefully and cook 5 to 6 minutes more until cooked through.|Repeat, then top with the sauce, mayonnaise, bonito flakes and nori.","Japanese"],
[3125,"Yakitori","sides","🍢",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Skewered grilled chicken thighs glazed with a sweet, glossy soy tare.","2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, 1 inch pieces;6|green onion|cut in 1 inch pieces;1/2 cup|soy sauce;1/2 cup|mirin;1/4 cup|sake;3 tbsp|sugar;1 clove|garlic|smashed;1 slice|ginger;1 tsp|sesame seeds","Soak 12 bamboo skewers in water for 30 minutes.|Simmer the soy sauce, mirin, sake, sugar, garlic and ginger 10 to 12 minutes until syrupy, then strain.|Thread the chicken and green onion pieces alternately onto skewers.|Grill over medium-high heat or broil 4 minutes, turning once.|Brush with tare and keep grilling 5 to 6 minutes, turning and brushing until glossy and cooked through to 165°F.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and serve.","Japanese"],
[3126,"Tamagoyaki","sides","🍳",15,"Medium",7.5,2,"Japanese rolled omelet with layers of lightly sweet, savory egg, sliced into tender pinwheels.","4|eggs;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|mirin;1 tbsp|soy sauce;3 tbsp|water|or dashi;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;|daikon|grated, to serve","Whisk the eggs with the sugar, mirin, soy sauce and water until combined but not frothy.|Oil a small nonstick or rectangular pan lightly over medium-low heat.|Pour in a thin layer of egg and cook until almost set but still wet on top.|Roll the egg from one side to the other and push to the edge of the pan.|Oil the empty part, pour in another thin layer under the roll, and repeat rolling until the egg is used.|Rest 2 minutes, slice into thick pieces, and serve with grated daikon.","Japanese"],
[3127,"Pan-Seared Ribeye with Garlic Butter","comfort","🥩",30,"Medium",9,2,"A thick, deeply browned ribeye basted in garlic and thyme butter, the steakhouse way.","2|ribeye steaks|1 1/4 inch thick, about 12 oz each;2 tsp|coarse salt;1 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|butter;4 clove|garlic|smashed;4 sprig|fresh thyme","Pat the steaks very dry and let them sit at room temperature for 30 minutes. Season both sides generously with salt and pepper.|Heat a cast-iron skillet over high heat for 3 minutes until smoking hot, then add the oil.|Sear the steaks 3 to 4 minutes without moving until a dark crust forms. Flip and sear 2 minutes more.|Reduce heat to medium, add the butter, garlic and thyme. Tilt the pan and spoon the foaming butter over the steaks for 2 minutes.|Cook to 125°F internal for rare, 130°F for medium-rare, or 140°F for medium.|Rest the steaks on a board for 8 minutes, spoon over the pan butter, and slice against the grain.","American"],
[3128,"New York Strip Steak","comfort","🥩",25,"Easy",9,2,"A classic skillet-seared strip steak with a salty crust and a juicy pink center.","2|ny strip steaks|1 inch thick, about 10 oz each;2 tsp|coarse salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|butter;2 sprig|fresh thyme","Pat the steaks dry and season all over with salt and pepper. Let stand 20 minutes at room temperature.|Heat a heavy skillet over high heat until just smoking, then add the oil.|Sear the steaks 3 minutes per side for a dark crust. Render the fat cap by standing the steaks on their edge for 1 minute.|Lower the heat, add butter and thyme, and baste for 1 minute.|Cook to 130°F for medium-rare.|Rest 5 minutes before slicing.","American"],
[3129,"Filet Mignon","comfort","🥩",35,"Medium",9,2,"Tender beef filets seared in a skillet and finished in the oven with butter and herbs.","2|filet mignon steaks|1 1/2 inch thick, about 6 oz each;1 1/2 tsp|coarse salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|butter;2 clove|garlic|smashed;2 sprig|fresh thyme","Take the filets out of the fridge 30 minutes ahead, pat dry, and season with salt and pepper. Heat the oven to 425°F.|Heat an oven-safe skillet over high heat and add the oil.|Sear the filets 2 minutes per side until deeply browned, also searing the edges for 30 seconds.|Add butter, garlic and thyme and baste for 1 minute.|Transfer the skillet to the oven for 4 to 6 minutes until 125°F for rare or 130°F for medium-rare.|Rest 5 minutes, spoon the pan butter over, and serve.","American"],
[3130,"Steak au Poivre","comfort","🥩",35,"Medium",9,2,"Pepper-crusted steaks with a quick cognac cream pan sauce, a bistro favorite.","2|ny strip steaks|or filet mignon, 8 oz each;1 tbsp|black pepper|coarsely cracked;1 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|butter;1|shallot|minced;1/4 cup|cognac|or brandy;1/2 cup|beef broth;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 tsp|dijon mustard","Pat the steaks dry, season with salt, and press the cracked pepper firmly into both sides.|Heat the oil in a heavy skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the steaks 4 minutes per side for medium-rare (130°F). Move to a plate and tent with foil.|Pour off most of the fat, add the butter and shallot, and cook 1 minute.|Off the heat, add the cognac, return to heat carefully and let it reduce by half, about 1 minute.|Add the broth and simmer 3 minutes, then stir in the cream and mustard and simmer 2 minutes until it coats a spoon.|Serve the steaks with the sauce spooned over.","French"],
[3131,"Chimichurri Flank Steak","light","🥩",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Grilled flank steak sliced thin and topped with a bright, garlicky parsley chimichurri.","1 1/2 lb|flank steak;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|olive oil;1 cup|parsley|finely chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|red onion|minced;1/3 cup|olive oil;3 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1 tsp|oregano;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes","Mix the parsley, garlic, red onion, 1/3 cup olive oil, vinegar, oregano, red pepper flakes and 1/2 tsp salt. Let it sit 20 minutes.|Pat the steak dry, rub with 1 tbsp olive oil, and season with salt and pepper.|Heat a grill or cast-iron pan over high heat.|Cook the steak 4 to 5 minutes per side to 130°F for medium-rare.|Rest 10 minutes, then slice thinly against the grain.|Serve topped with the chimichurri.","American"],
[3132,"Steak Frites","comfort","🍟",50,"Medium",9,2,"Pan-seared steak with crisp golden fries and a garlic-herb butter, a French bistro classic.","1 1/2 lb|russet potatoes|cut into 1/4 inch sticks;4 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;2|ny strip steaks|1 inch thick;1 1/2 tsp|coarse salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|butter|softened;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 clove|garlic|grated;1 tsp|lemon juice","Soak the potato sticks in cold water 30 minutes, then drain and dry thoroughly. Mix the butter, parsley, garlic and lemon juice and chill.|Heat the oil to 325°F in a heavy pot. Fry the potatoes in batches 5 minutes until pale and tender, then drain.|Season the steaks with salt and pepper. Sear in a very hot skillet 3 to 4 minutes per side to 130°F, then rest 5 minutes.|Raise the oil to 375°F and fry the potatoes again 3 to 4 minutes until golden and crisp. Drain and salt immediately.|Slice the steak, top with the herb butter, and serve with the fries.","French"],
[3133,"Reverse-Sear Porterhouse Steak","comfort","🥩",75,"Medium",9,2,"A thick steak slowly warmed in the oven, then seared hot for an edge-to-edge pink center.","2 lb|porterhouse steak|about 1 1/2 inches thick;2 tsp|coarse salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|butter;2 clove|garlic|smashed;2 sprig|fresh thyme","Salt the steak all over and refrigerate uncovered on a rack for at least 1 hour. Heat the oven to 250°F.|Pat dry, season with pepper, and set on a rack over a baking sheet.|Roast 35 to 45 minutes until 110°F in the thickest part for medium-rare.|Heat the oil in a cast-iron skillet over high heat until smoking. Sear the steak 1 to 2 minutes per side.|Add butter, garlic and thyme and baste for 30 seconds. Final temperature should be about 130°F.|Rest 5 minutes, then slice the strip and filet from the bone.","American"],
[3134,"Steak Fajitas","quick","🌮",40,"Easy",8.5,4,"Marinated skirt steak seared with sizzling peppers and onions, served in warm tortillas.","1 1/2 lb|skirt steak|or flank steak;3 tbsp|olive oil;3 tbsp|lime juice;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|chili powder;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2|bell pepper|sliced;1|onion|sliced;8|flour tortillas|warmed;1/2 cup|sour cream;1/2 cup|salsa","Whisk 2 tbsp oil with lime juice, garlic, cumin, chili powder, paprika, salt and pepper. Marinate the steak 30 minutes to 2 hours.|Heat a large cast-iron skillet over high heat. Cook the steak 3 to 4 minutes per side to 130°F. Rest on a board.|In the same pan, add the remaining oil and cook the peppers and onion 5 to 6 minutes until charred at the edges.|Slice the steak thinly against the grain.|Serve with the vegetables, warm tortillas, sour cream and salsa.","Tex-Mex"],
[3135,"Salisbury Steak","comfort","🍖",45,"Easy",9,4,"Seasoned beef patties simmered in a rich onion and mushroom gravy.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1/3 cup|breadcrumbs;1|eggs;2 tbsp|worcestershire;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;8 oz|mushrooms|sliced;1|onion|sliced;2 tbsp|butter;2 tbsp|flour;1 1/2 cup|beef broth;1 tbsp|ketchup","Mix the beef, breadcrumbs, egg, 1 tbsp worcestershire, salt and pepper gently and shape into 4 oval patties.|Brown the patties in the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat, 3 minutes per side. Remove to a plate.|Add the butter, onion and mushrooms to the pan and cook 6 to 8 minutes until golden.|Stir in the flour for 1 minute, then whisk in the broth, ketchup and remaining worcestershire.|Return the patties to the gravy, cover, and simmer 12 to 15 minutes until cooked through (160°F).|Serve over mashed potatoes or egg noodles.","American"],
[3136,"Chicken Fried Steak with Gravy","comfort","🍳",50,"Medium",9,4,"Tenderized steak breaded, fried until crisp, and smothered in creamy pepper gravy.","4|cube steaks|about 6 oz each;1 1/2 cup|flour;2 tsp|salt;2 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;2|eggs;1/2 cup|milk;1 cup|vegetable oil;3 cup|milk|for gravy","Whisk the eggs with 1/2 cup milk. Mix the flour, salt, 1 tsp pepper, paprika and garlic powder in a shallow dish.|Dredge each steak in flour, dip in the egg mixture, then dredge in flour again, pressing firmly.|Heat the oil in a large skillet to 350°F. Fry the steaks 3 to 4 minutes per side until deep golden. Drain on a rack and keep warm.|Pour off all but 1/4 cup of the oil, leaving the browned bits.|Whisk in 1/4 cup of the seasoned flour and cook 1 minute, then slowly whisk in the 3 cups milk.|Simmer 5 minutes until thick, season with 1 tsp pepper and salt, and pour over the steaks.","Southern"],
[3137,"Garlic Butter Steak Tips","quick","🥩",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Juicy seared sirloin bites tossed in garlic butter, ready in about 25 minutes.","1 1/2 lb|sirloin steak|cut into 1 inch cubes;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;4 tbsp|butter;5 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tsp|worcestershire","Pat the steak dry and toss with salt, pepper and garlic powder.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over high heat until smoking.|Sear the steak in a single layer in two batches, 2 to 3 minutes total, turning once, until browned. Move to a plate.|Reduce the heat to medium, melt the butter, and cook the garlic 30 seconds.|Return the steak with the worcestershire and toss 1 minute.|Sprinkle with parsley and serve.","American"],
[3138,"Steak and Eggs","breakfast","🍳",25,"Easy",8.5,2,"A seared sirloin served with sunny-side-up eggs for a hearty diner-style breakfast.","12 oz|sirloin steak|about 1 inch thick;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|butter;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;4|eggs;2 slice|bread|toasted;1 tbsp|chives|chopped","Pat the steak dry and season with salt and pepper.|Heat the oil in a skillet over high heat. Sear the steak 3 to 4 minutes per side to 130°F. Rest 5 minutes.|Wipe the skillet, melt the butter over medium heat, and fry the eggs 3 minutes until the whites are set and yolks runny.|Slice the steak against the grain.|Serve with the eggs, toast and chives.","American"],
[3139,"Philly Cheesesteak","lunch","🥪",35,"Easy",8,4,"Thinly sliced ribeye piled on a roll with sauteed onions and melted provolone.","1 1/2 lb|ribeye steak|partially frozen, sliced paper thin;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2|onion|thinly sliced;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;8 slice|provolone;4|french bread|rolls, split","Freeze the steak 30 minutes, then slice as thin as possible.|Heat 1 tbsp oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onions with a pinch of salt for 12 to 15 minutes until soft and golden. Move aside.|Raise the heat to high, add the remaining oil, and cook the beef 2 to 3 minutes, chopping it with spatulas, seasoned with salt and pepper.|Mix in the onions and form 4 portions in the pan. Top each with 2 slices of provolone, cover 1 minute until melted.|Toast the rolls briefly and scoop each portion into a roll.","American"],
[3140,"Steak Salad with Blue Cheese","light","🥗",30,"Easy",7.5,2,"Sliced seared steak over crisp greens, tomatoes and red onion with a tangy vinaigrette.","12 oz|sirloin steak;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|olive oil;6 cup|lettuce|chopped;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1/4|red onion|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|blue cheese|crumbled;3 tbsp|olive oil|for dressing;1 tbsp|balsamic vinegar;1 tsp|dijon mustard","Season the steak with salt and pepper. Heat 1 tbsp oil in a skillet over high heat.|Sear 3 to 4 minutes per side to 130°F, then rest 8 minutes.|Whisk the dressing oil, vinegar and mustard with a pinch of salt.|Toss the lettuce, tomatoes and onion with half the dressing.|Slice the steak thinly against the grain and lay it on top.|Scatter the blue cheese and drizzle with the remaining dressing.","American"],
[3141,"Creamed Spinach","sides","🥬",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"The classic steakhouse side of spinach in a rich, nutmeg-scented cream sauce.","20 oz|frozen spinach|thawed and squeezed dry;2 tbsp|butter;1|shallot|minced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|flour;1 cup|milk;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt the butter in a saucepan over medium heat and cook the shallot 2 minutes. Add the garlic for 30 seconds.|Stir in the flour and cook 1 minute.|Slowly whisk in the milk and cream and simmer 3 to 4 minutes until thickened.|Stir in the parmesan and nutmeg until melted.|Add the spinach and cook 4 to 5 minutes until hot and creamy. Season with salt and pepper.","American"],
[3142,"Loaded Twice-Baked Potatoes","sides","🥔",100,"Easy",7.5,6,"Baked potato halves stuffed with a cheesy, bacony filling and baked again until golden.","3|russet potatoes|large;1 tbsp|olive oil;4 tbsp|butter;1/2 cup|sour cream;1/4 cup|milk;1 1/2 cup|cheddar|shredded, divided;6 slice|bacon|cooked and crumbled;3|green onion|sliced;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 400°F. Rub the potatoes with oil and salt and bake 60 minutes until tender.|Cool 10 minutes, halve lengthwise, and scoop out the flesh, leaving a 1/4 inch shell.|Mash the flesh with the butter, sour cream, milk, 1 cup cheddar, half the bacon, half the green onion, salt and pepper.|Spoon the filling back into the shells and top with the remaining cheddar.|Bake 20 minutes until golden. Top with remaining bacon and green onion.","American"],
[3143,"Smash Burgers","quick","🍔",20,"Easy",8.5,4,"Thin beef patties smashed on a hot skillet for crispy lacy edges, with melted cheese.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef|80/20, formed into 8 balls;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;8 slice|american cheese;4|burger buns|toasted;1/2|onion|thinly sliced;1/2 cup|pickles|sliced;3 tbsp|mayonnaise;1 tbsp|ketchup;1 tsp|mustard","Mix the mayonnaise, ketchup and mustard for the sauce. Toast the buns.|Heat a cast-iron skillet or griddle over high heat until very hot.|Place the beef balls on the skillet and smash firmly flat with a sturdy spatula. Season with salt and pepper.|Cook 2 minutes until the edges are crisp, scrape and flip, top with cheese, and cook 30 to 45 seconds.|Stack 2 patties per bun with the sauce, onion and pickles.","American"],
[3144,"Classic Meatloaf","comfort","🍖",85,"Easy",9,6,"A tender beef meatloaf with a sweet tangy ketchup glaze.","2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|finely diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;3/4 cup|breadcrumbs;1/2 cup|milk;2|eggs;2 tbsp|worcestershire;1 1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|ketchup;2 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|mustard","Heat the oven to 350°F. Soak the breadcrumbs in the milk for 5 minutes.|Mix the beef, onion, garlic, soaked breadcrumbs, eggs, worcestershire, salt and pepper gently with your hands.|Shape into a loaf on a lined baking sheet or pack into a loaf pan.|Stir the ketchup, brown sugar and mustard and spread half over the loaf.|Bake 50 minutes, brush on the remaining glaze, and bake 15 more minutes until 160°F.|Rest 10 minutes before slicing.","American"],
[3145,"Baby Back Ribs","comfort","🍖",195,"Medium",9,4,"Oven-roasted baby back ribs rubbed with spices and glazed in barbecue sauce, fall-off-the-bone tender.","2|pork ribs|racks baby back, about 2 lb each;3 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|paprika;2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|onion powder;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 cup|bbq sauce","Heat the oven to 275°F. Remove the membrane from the back of the ribs with a paper towel.|Mix the brown sugar, paprika, salt, pepper, garlic powder, onion powder and cayenne and rub all over the ribs.|Wrap each rack tightly in foil, meat side up, and set on a baking sheet.|Bake 2 1/2 hours until very tender.|Unwrap, brush with barbecue sauce, and broil or grill 5 to 8 minutes until sticky and caramelized.|Rest 10 minutes and cut between the bones.","American"],
[3146,"Buffalo Wings","lunch","🍗",60,"Easy",8,4,"Crispy baked chicken wings tossed in tangy buttery buffalo sauce.","3 lb|chicken wings|split, tips removed;1 tbsp|baking powder;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1/2 cup|buffalo sauce;4 tbsp|butter|melted;1/2 cup|ranch dressing;4 stalk|celery|cut in sticks","Heat the oven to 425°F. Pat the wings completely dry.|Toss with baking powder, salt and garlic powder and arrange on a rack over a foil-lined sheet.|Bake 25 minutes, flip, and bake 25 to 30 minutes more until deep golden and crisp.|Whisk the buffalo sauce with the melted butter.|Toss the hot wings in the sauce and serve with ranch and celery.","American"],
[3147,"Chicken and Waffles","breakfast","🧇",75,"Medium",8.5,4,"Crispy buttermilk-fried chicken stacked on fluffy waffles with warm maple syrup.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, cut in large pieces;1 cup|milk|with 1 tbsp lemon juice stirred in;1 1/2 cup|flour|for chicken;2 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;2 cup|flour|for waffles;2 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt|for waffles;2|eggs;1 3/4 cup|milk|for waffles;1/3 cup|butter|melted;1/2 cup|maple syrup|warmed","Marinate the chicken in the soured milk for at least 30 minutes.|Mix 1 1/2 cups flour with paprika, garlic powder, salt and pepper. Dredge the chicken, pressing to coat.|Heat the oil to 350°F in a deep skillet. Fry the chicken 6 to 8 minutes, turning, until golden and 165°F inside. Drain on a rack.|Whisk the waffle flour, sugar, baking powder and salt. Whisk in the eggs, milk and melted butter until just combined.|Cook the batter in a hot waffle iron until golden and crisp.|Top each waffle with chicken and drizzle with warm syrup.","Southern"],
[3148,"Skillet Cornbread","sides","🌽",35,"Easy",7.5,8,"Golden cornbread with a crunchy edge, baked in a hot buttered cast-iron skillet.","1 1/2 cup|cornmeal;1/2 cup|flour;1 tbsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|baking soda;1 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|sugar;1 1/4 cup|milk|with 1 tbsp lemon juice stirred in;2|eggs;4 tbsp|butter|melted, divided","Heat the oven to 425°F and place a 10-inch cast-iron skillet inside to heat 10 minutes.|Whisk the cornmeal, flour, baking powder, baking soda, salt and sugar.|Whisk the soured milk, eggs and 3 tbsp melted butter, then stir into the dry ingredients until just combined.|Add the remaining butter to the hot skillet, swirl, and pour in the batter.|Bake 18 to 22 minutes until golden and a toothpick comes out clean.|Cool 5 minutes before slicing.","Southern"],
[3149,"Creamy Coleslaw","sides","🥗",20,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Crisp shredded cabbage and carrot in a tangy creamy dressing.","1|coleslaw mix|14 oz bag;1/2 cup|mayonnaise;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1/2 tsp|celery seed|optional","Whisk the mayonnaise, sugar, vinegar, mustard, salt, pepper and celery seed until smooth.|Toss the coleslaw mix with the dressing.|Chill at least 30 minutes so the cabbage softens slightly.|Stir again and adjust seasoning before serving.","American"],
[3150,"Reuben Sandwich","lunch","🥪",20,"Easy",8,2,"Grilled rye with corned beef, sauerkraut, swiss and Russian dressing.","4 slice|rye bread;6 oz|corned beef|sliced deli;4 slice|swiss cheese;1/2 cup|sauerkraut|drained and squeezed dry;4 tbsp|mayonnaise;1 tbsp|ketchup;1 tbsp|pickles|finely chopped;2 tbsp|butter|softened","Mix the mayonnaise, ketchup and chopped pickles for the Russian dressing.|Spread dressing on one side of each bread slice.|Layer 2 slices with swiss, corned beef, sauerkraut and another swiss slice, then top with remaining bread, dressing side down.|Butter the outside of the sandwiches.|Cook in a skillet over medium heat 3 to 4 minutes per side until the bread is golden and the cheese melted.|Slice in half and serve hot.","American"],
[3151,"BLT Sandwich","quick","🥪",15,"Very easy",8.5,2,"Crisp bacon, ripe tomato and lettuce with mayo on toasted bread.","8 slice|bacon;4 slice|bread|toasted;3 tbsp|mayonnaise;1|tomatoes|large, sliced;4|lettuce|leaves;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Cook the bacon in a skillet over medium heat 8 to 10 minutes until crisp. Drain on paper towels.|Toast the bread and spread mayonnaise on each slice.|Season the tomato slices with salt and pepper.|Layer lettuce, tomato and bacon on 2 slices and top with remaining bread.|Cut in half and serve.","American"],
[3152,"Cobb Salad","light","🥗",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Chopped greens topped with rows of chicken, bacon, egg, avocado, tomato and blue cheese.","1 head|lettuce|chopped;2|chicken breast|cooked and diced;6 slice|bacon|cooked and crumbled;3|eggs|hard-boiled and chopped;2|avocado|diced;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1/2 cup|blue cheese|crumbled;2 tbsp|chives|chopped;1/4 cup|olive oil;2 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1 tsp|dijon mustard;|salt|to taste","Hard-boil the eggs for 11 minutes, cool in ice water, peel and chop.|Whisk the olive oil, vinegar, mustard and salt for the dressing.|Spread the lettuce on a large platter.|Arrange the chicken, bacon, egg, avocado, tomatoes and blue cheese in rows on top.|Sprinkle with chives and drizzle with dressing just before serving.","American"],
[3153,"Classic Grilled Cheese","quick","🧀",12,"Very easy",8.5,2,"Buttery golden toast with gooey melted cheddar.","4 slice|bread;4 slice|american cheese;1/2 cup|cheddar|shredded;2 tbsp|butter|softened","Butter one side of each bread slice.|Place 2 slices butter side down in a skillet over medium-low heat.|Layer the american cheese and cheddar on top and cover with the remaining bread, butter side up.|Cook 3 to 4 minutes until golden, flip, and cook 3 minutes more until the cheese is melted.|Slice and serve hot.","American"],
[3154,"Biscuits and Sausage Gravy","breakfast","🍳",35,"Easy",8.5,6,"Fluffy buttermilk-style biscuits smothered in peppery sausage cream gravy.","2 cup|flour;1 tbsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;6 tbsp|butter|cold, cubed;3/4 cup|milk;1 lb|breakfast sausage;1/4 cup|flour|for gravy;3 cup|milk|for gravy;1 tsp|black pepper;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 425°F. Whisk 2 cups flour, baking powder and salt, then cut in the cold butter until pea-sized crumbs form.|Stir in 3/4 cup milk just until a shaggy dough forms. Pat to 1 inch thick, cut 6 rounds, and place on a baking sheet.|Bake 12 to 15 minutes until golden.|Brown the sausage in a large skillet over medium heat 6 to 8 minutes, breaking it up.|Sprinkle in 1/4 cup flour and cook 1 minute, then slowly stir in 3 cups milk.|Simmer 5 to 6 minutes until thick, season with pepper and salt, and ladle over split biscuits.","Southern"],
[3155,"Fudgy Brownies","treats","🍫",50,"Easy",9,16,"Dense, fudgy chocolate brownies with a shiny crackly top.","1/2 cup|butter;1 cup|sugar;2|eggs;1 tsp|vanilla;1/3 cup|cocoa powder;1/2 cup|flour;1/4 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|baking powder;1/2 cup|chocolate chips","Heat the oven to 350°F and line an 8-inch square pan with parchment.|Melt the butter and stir in the sugar, then beat in the eggs and vanilla.|Sift in the cocoa, flour, salt and baking powder and stir until just combined. Fold in the chocolate chips.|Spread in the pan and bake 22 to 26 minutes, until a toothpick has a few moist crumbs.|Cool completely before cutting into squares.","American"],
[3156,"Chicken and Sausage Gumbo","comfort","🍲",120,"Medium",9,8,"A dark roux gumbo with chicken, smoked sausage and the holy trinity, served over rice.","1/2 cup|vegetable oil;1/2 cup|flour;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;3 stalk|celery|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;8 cup|chicken broth;1 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, bite-size;1 lb|smoked sausage|sliced;2|bay leaves;2 tsp|cajun seasoning;1 tsp|dried thyme;3 cup|rice|cooked;4|green onion|sliced","Whisk the oil and flour in a heavy pot over medium-low heat, stirring constantly 25 to 35 minutes until the roux is the color of dark chocolate.|Add the onion, bell pepper and celery and cook 5 minutes, then add the garlic for 1 minute.|Slowly whisk in the warm broth, then add bay leaves, cajun seasoning and thyme.|Add the sausage and simmer 30 minutes.|Add the chicken and simmer 30 more minutes until tender. Skim off any fat.|Remove the bay leaves, adjust salt and cayenne, and serve over rice with green onion.","Cajun"],
[3157,"Jambalaya","comfort","🍤",60,"Easy",9,6,"A one-pot rice dish with smoked sausage, chicken and shrimp in Cajun spices.","1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 lb|smoked sausage|sliced;1 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, diced;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14.5 oz;2 cup|rice|long-grain;3 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|cajun seasoning;1 tsp|dried thyme;1 lb|shrimp|peeled;3|green onion|sliced","Brown the sausage in the oil in a large Dutch oven over medium-high heat 4 minutes. Remove.|Brown the chicken 5 minutes, season with some cajun seasoning, and remove.|Cook the onion, pepper and celery in the drippings 5 minutes, then add the garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the tomatoes, rice, broth, remaining seasoning and thyme. Return the sausage and chicken.|Bring to a boil, cover, and cook on low 20 minutes without lifting the lid.|Lay the shrimp on top, cover, and cook 5 minutes until pink and the rice is tender. Fluff and add green onion.","Cajun"],
[3158,"Shrimp and Grits","comfort","🍤",45,"Easy",9,4,"Garlicky shrimp and bacon in a savory pan sauce over creamy cheddar grits.","1 cup|grits|stone-ground or old-fashioned;4 cup|chicken broth;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;2 tbsp|butter;1 1/2 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined;4 slice|bacon|chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 tsp|paprika;1 tbsp|lemon juice;3|green onion|sliced;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Bring the broth to a boil, whisk in the grits, then reduce to low, cover, and cook 25 to 30 minutes, stirring often, until creamy.|Stir in the cheddar and butter and season with salt and pepper.|Cook the bacon in a skillet until crisp, then remove, leaving 1 tbsp fat.|Season the shrimp with paprika, salt and pepper and cook in the fat 2 minutes per side until pink.|Add the garlic for 30 seconds, then the lemon juice and bacon.|Spoon the shrimp over the grits and top with green onion.","Southern"],
[3159,"Red Beans and Rice","comfort","🍛",180,"Easy",9,8,"Creamy New Orleans-style kidney beans slow-simmered with andouille and served over rice.","1 lb|kidney beans|dried, soaked overnight;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 lb|smoked sausage|andouille, sliced;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;3 stalk|celery|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;6 cup|chicken broth;2|bay leaves;2 tsp|cajun seasoning;1 tsp|dried thyme;3 cup|rice|cooked;|salt|to taste;3|green onion|sliced","Drain the soaked beans. Brown the sausage in the oil in a large pot 5 minutes.|Add the onion, bell pepper and celery and cook 6 minutes, then the garlic for 1 minute.|Add the beans, broth, bay leaves, cajun seasoning and thyme and bring to a boil.|Reduce to a low simmer, partly covered, and cook 2 to 2 1/2 hours until the beans are very tender, stirring occasionally.|Mash about a quarter of the beans against the pot to thicken, and season with salt.|Serve over rice topped with green onion.","Cajun"],
[3160,"Crawfish Etouffee","comfort","🦐",60,"Medium",9,6,"A blond-roux smothered stew of shrimp in Cajun trinity, served over rice.","6 tbsp|butter;1/3 cup|flour;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|chicken broth;1 can|diced tomatoes|14.5 oz;2 tsp|cajun seasoning;1 tsp|paprika;1 1/2 lb|shrimp|peeled, or crawfish tails;3|green onion|sliced;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;3 cup|rice|cooked","Melt the butter in a Dutch oven over medium heat, whisk in the flour, and cook 8 to 10 minutes to a peanut-butter colored roux.|Add the onion, bell pepper and celery and cook 6 minutes until soft. Add the garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the tomatoes, broth, cajun seasoning and paprika and simmer 20 minutes until thickened.|Add the shrimp and cook 4 to 5 minutes until pink.|Stir in the green onion and parsley and adjust seasoning.|Serve over rice.","Cajun"],
[3161,"Southern Collard Greens","sides","🥬",90,"Easy",7.5,6,"Tender collards simmered low and slow with smoky bacon and a splash of vinegar.","2 lb|collard greens|stemmed and chopped;6 slice|bacon|chopped;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;4 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1 tsp|sugar;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Wash the collards well and slice into 1 inch ribbons.|Cook the bacon in a large pot until crisp. Add the onion and cook 4 minutes, then the garlic for 1 minute.|Add the collards in batches, stirring until wilted.|Pour in the broth, vinegar, sugar and red pepper flakes and bring to a simmer.|Cover and cook on low 60 to 75 minutes until very tender.|Season with salt and pepper and serve with the pot liquor.","Southern"],
[3162,"Hush Puppies","sides","🧆",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"Crispy fried cornmeal fritters with sweet onion, perfect alongside fried fish.","1 cup|cornmeal;1/2 cup|flour;2 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|sugar;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|onion|finely minced;1|eggs;3/4 cup|milk;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Whisk the cornmeal, flour, baking powder, salt, sugar and pepper.|Stir in the onion, egg and milk to make a thick batter. Rest 5 minutes.|Heat the oil to 350°F in a heavy pot.|Drop the batter by tablespoons into the oil and fry 2 to 3 minutes, turning, until deep golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve warm.","Southern"],
[3163,"Fried Catfish","comfort","🐟",35,"Easy",9,4,"Cornmeal-crusted catfish fillets fried until crispy and golden.","4|catfish fillets|about 6 oz each;1 cup|buttermilk|or milk with 1 tsp lemon juice;1 cup|cornmeal;1/2 cup|flour;2 tsp|cajun seasoning;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 tsp|paprika;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1|lemon|cut in wedges","Soak the fillets in the buttermilk for 15 to 30 minutes.|Mix the cornmeal, flour, cajun seasoning, salt, pepper and paprika in a shallow dish.|Heat the oil to 350°F in a deep skillet.|Lift each fillet from the buttermilk, let it drip, and dredge in the cornmeal mix.|Fry 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden and the fish flakes at 145°F.|Drain on a rack and serve with lemon wedges.","Southern"],
[3164,"Shrimp Po' Boy","lunch","🥪",35,"Easy",8,4,"Crisp fried shrimp on a French roll with lettuce, tomato, pickles and spicy remoulade.","1 1/2 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined;1 cup|cornmeal;1/2 cup|flour;2 tsp|cajun seasoning;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|milk;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;4|french bread|rolls or 4 pieces of baguette;1/3 cup|mayonnaise;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 tsp|lemon juice;1/2 tsp|cajun seasoning|for sauce;2 cup|lettuce|shredded;2|tomatoes|sliced;1/2 cup|pickles","Stir the mayonnaise, mustard, lemon juice and 1/2 tsp cajun seasoning for the remoulade.|Mix the cornmeal, flour, 2 tsp cajun seasoning and salt. Dip the shrimp in milk, then dredge in the cornmeal mixture.|Heat the oil to 350°F and fry the shrimp in batches 2 to 3 minutes until golden. Drain.|Split and lightly toast the rolls and spread with the remoulade.|Fill with lettuce, tomato, pickles and the shrimp.","Cajun"],
[3165,"Peach Cobbler","treats","🍑",70,"Easy",9,8,"Juicy cinnamon peaches under a golden buttery biscuit-style crust.","6 cup|peaches|sliced, fresh or frozen;1/2 cup|sugar;1 tbsp|cornstarch;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|cinnamon;1 cup|flour;1/2 cup|sugar|for topping;1 1/2 tsp|baking powder;1/4 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|milk;6 tbsp|butter|melted","Heat the oven to 375°F. Toss the peaches with 1/2 cup sugar, cornstarch, lemon juice and cinnamon.|Pour into a 9x9-inch baking dish.|Whisk the flour, 1/2 cup sugar, baking powder and salt, then stir in the milk and melted butter until smooth.|Spoon the batter over the peaches in dollops.|Bake 40 to 45 minutes until golden and bubbling.|Cool 15 minutes and serve warm with vanilla ice cream.","Southern"],
[3166,"Banana Pudding","treats","🍌",50,"Easy",9,10,"Layers of vanilla custard, ripe bananas and vanilla wafers, chilled until soft.","3/4 cup|sugar;1/3 cup|flour;1/4 tsp|salt;3 cup|milk;4|eggs|yolks only;2 tbsp|butter;2 tsp|vanilla;4|banana|ripe, sliced;1|vanilla wafers|11 oz box;1 cup|heavy cream|whipped, for topping","Whisk the sugar, flour and salt in a saucepan, then whisk in the milk and egg yolks.|Cook over medium heat, stirring constantly, 8 to 10 minutes until thick.|Remove from the heat and stir in the butter and vanilla.|Layer wafers, banana slices and custard in a 2-quart dish, repeating twice.|Cover and chill at least 4 hours.|Top with whipped cream before serving.","Southern"],
[3167,"Nashville Hot Chicken","comfort","🌶️",90,"Medium",9,4,"Buttermilk-fried chicken brushed with a fiery cayenne oil and served on white bread with pickles.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;1 1/2 cup|buttermilk;2 tbsp|hot sauce;1 tbsp|salt;2 cup|flour;1 tbsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|black pepper;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|hot, for sauce;2 tbsp|cayenne;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;4 slice|bread;|pickles|to serve","Mix the buttermilk, hot sauce and 2 tsp salt. Marinate the chicken in it 4 hours or overnight.|Whisk the flour, 1 tbsp paprika, garlic powder, pepper and 1 tsp salt. Dredge the chicken, pressing, then dredge again.|Heat the frying oil to 325°F in a Dutch oven. Fry the chicken 14 to 18 minutes, turning, until 175°F. Drain on a rack.|Stir the cayenne, brown sugar, 1 tsp paprika and garlic powder into 1/2 cup hot frying oil.|Brush the hot sauce generously over the chicken.|Serve on bread with pickles.","Southern"],
[3168,"Pimento Cheese","sides","🧀",15,"Very easy",7.5,8,"The South's classic cheddar spread with sweet pimentos, great on crackers or in sandwiches.","2 cup|cheddar|sharp, freshly shredded;4 oz|cream cheese|softened;1/2 cup|mayonnaise;1 jar|pimentos|4 oz, drained;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1/4 tsp|cayenne;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Beat the cream cheese and mayonnaise until smooth.|Stir in the pimentos, garlic powder, cayenne and pepper.|Fold in the shredded cheddar.|Chill 1 hour before serving with crackers, celery or on bread.","Southern"],
[3169,"Deviled Eggs","sides","🥚",30,"Very easy",7.5,12,"Creamy mustard-mayo egg yolk filling piped into tender egg whites with paprika.","6|eggs;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 tsp|apple cider vinegar;|salt|to taste;|paprika|to garnish;1 tbsp|chives|chopped","Place the eggs in a pot, cover with cold water, bring to a boil, then cover off the heat for 12 minutes.|Cool in ice water 5 minutes, then peel and halve lengthwise.|Mash the yolks with the mayonnaise, mustard, vinegar and salt until smooth.|Spoon or pipe the filling into the whites.|Dust with paprika and chives and chill until serving.","Southern"],
[3170,"Sweet Potato Pie","treats","🥧",110,"Medium",9,8,"A silky spiced sweet potato custard in a flaky crust, a Southern holiday favorite.","2 lb|sweet potatoes;1|pie crust|9 inch, unbaked;1/2 cup|butter|softened;3/4 cup|brown sugar;2|eggs;1/2 cup|milk;1 tsp|vanilla;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|nutmeg;1/4 tsp|salt","Bake the sweet potatoes at 400°F for 50 to 60 minutes until very soft. Cool, peel, and mash until smooth (about 2 cups).|Lower the oven to 350°F and fit the crust into a 9-inch pie plate.|Beat the mashed sweet potato with the butter and brown sugar, then beat in the eggs, milk, vanilla, cinnamon, nutmeg and salt.|Pour into the crust.|Bake 50 to 55 minutes until the center is just set.|Cool completely before slicing.","Southern"],
[3171,"Palak Paneer","comfort","🥬",40,"Easy",9,4,"Cubes of soft paneer in a silky, spiced spinach sauce, finished with a swirl of cream.","1 lb|spinach|fresh or 10 oz frozen;14 oz|paneer|cubed;2 tbsp|butter;1|onion|chopped;4 clove|garlic|minced;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;2|tomatoes|chopped;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|garam masala;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1/4 cup|heavy cream;|salt|to taste","Blanch the spinach in boiling water for 1 minute, then move it to ice water, drain well and blend to a smooth puree.|Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat and fry the paneer cubes 2 to 3 minutes per side until lightly golden. Remove and set aside.|In the same pan, cook the onion for 6 to 8 minutes until soft and golden, then stir in the garlic and ginger for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, cumin, coriander, turmeric, cayenne and salt and cook 5 minutes until the tomatoes break down into a paste.|Pour in the spinach puree and 1/2 cup water, and simmer 5 minutes.|Stir in the cream and garam masala, add the paneer and simmer gently 3 minutes. Serve with rice or naan.","Indian"],
[3172,"Chana Masala","comfort","🍛",35,"Easy",9,4,"Chickpeas simmered in a tangy, deeply spiced tomato and onion gravy.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|finely chopped;4 clove|garlic|minced;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;1 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;2 can|chickpeas|15 oz each, drained;2 tsp|garam masala;1 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion 8 minutes until deep golden.|Add the garlic and ginger and cook 1 minute.|Stir in the cumin, coriander, turmeric, paprika and cayenne for 30 seconds until fragrant.|Add the tomatoes and salt and cook 8 minutes, mashing, until thick and the oil begins to separate.|Add the chickpeas and 1 cup water, and simmer 15 minutes, lightly crushing some chickpeas to thicken the sauce.|Stir in the garam masala and lemon juice, then top with cilantro. Serve with rice or naan.","Indian"],
[3173,"Chicken Biryani","comfort","🍚",90,"Medium",9,6,"Fragrant basmati layered with yogurt-marinated spiced chicken and fried onions, then steamed.","2 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in, skinless;1 cup|greek yogurt;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;6 clove|garlic|minced;2 tsp|garam masala;1 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|cayenne;2 cup|rice|basmati, rinsed;3|onion|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|vegetable oil;4|cardamom pods;1|cinnamon|stick;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/4 cup|mint|chopped;1/4 cup|milk|warmed, with a pinch of saffron;2 tbsp|butter;|salt|to taste","Mix the chicken with the yogurt, ginger, garlic, garam masala, turmeric, cayenne and 2 teaspoons salt. Marinate at least 1 hour.|Fry the onions in the oil over medium heat 20 to 25 minutes, stirring often, until deep brown and crisp. Remove half and set aside for topping.|Add the marinated chicken to the remaining onions in the pot and cook 10 minutes, then spread it in an even layer.|Boil the rice in plenty of salted water with the cardamom and cinnamon for 5 minutes until 70 percent cooked, then drain.|Layer the rice over the chicken, then top with the reserved onions, cilantro, mint, saffron milk and butter.|Cover tightly with foil and a lid, and cook over the lowest heat for 30 minutes.|Rest 10 minutes, then gently fluff and serve with raita.","Indian"],
[3174,"Aloo Gobi","sides","🥔",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Dry-style potatoes and cauliflower tossed with turmeric, cumin and ginger.","3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1|onion|chopped;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 lb|potatoes|1-inch cubes;1 head|cauliflower|cut into florets;1 tsp|turmeric;2 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1|tomatoes|chopped;1 tsp|garam masala;|salt|to taste;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat the oil in a large lidded skillet over medium heat and toast the cumin 30 seconds.|Add the onion and cook 6 minutes until golden, then add the ginger and garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the turmeric, coriander, cayenne and tomato and cook 3 minutes.|Add the potatoes, cauliflower, salt and 1/4 cup water. Cover and cook 15 minutes, stirring now and then.|Uncover and cook 5 to 8 minutes more until the vegetables are tender and lightly browned.|Sprinkle with garam masala and cilantro before serving.","Indian"],
[3175,"Samosas","treats","🥟",75,"Medium",9,8,"Crisp, flaky pastry triangles filled with spiced potatoes and peas.","2 cup|flour;1/4 cup|vegetable oil;1/2 tsp|salt;1 lb|potatoes|boiled and mashed coarsely;1/2 cup|frozen peas;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;1 tsp|coriander;1 tsp|garam masala;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 tbsp|lemon juice;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Mix the flour, 1/4 cup oil and salt, then add about 1/2 cup cold water to form a stiff dough. Knead 5 minutes, cover and rest 30 minutes.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a pan, toast the cumin and ginger 30 seconds, then add the spices and peas and cook 2 minutes.|Fold in the potatoes and lemon juice, season with salt and cool completely.|Divide the dough into 8 balls and roll each into an oval, then cut in half to make 16 half-circles.|Shape each half into a cone, fill with about 2 tablespoons filling, wet the edge and pinch to seal.|Heat the frying oil to 325°F and fry the samosas in batches for 8 to 10 minutes until deep golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve warm with chutney.","Indian"],
[3176,"Garlic Naan","sides","🫓",90,"Medium",7.5,6,"Soft, blistered skillet flatbread brushed with garlic butter.","1/2 cup|warm water;2 tsp|sugar;2 1/4 tsp|yeast|one packet;2 1/2 cup|flour;1/2 cup|greek yogurt;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|salt;4 tbsp|butter|melted;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped","Stir the warm water, sugar and yeast together and let sit 10 minutes until foamy.|Mix in the flour, yogurt, oil and salt, then knead 8 minutes until smooth and soft.|Cover and let rise in a warm place 1 hour until doubled.|Divide into 6 balls and roll each into a teardrop about 1/4 inch thick.|Heat a cast-iron skillet over high heat until very hot. Cook each naan 1 to 2 minutes per side until puffed and charred in spots.|Mix the melted butter with garlic and cilantro and brush over the hot naan.","Indian"],
[3177,"Chicken Korma","comfort","🍛",50,"Easy",9,4,"Tender chicken in a mild, creamy sauce of yogurt, onion and ground almonds.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, cut in chunks;1/2 cup|greek yogurt;2 tbsp|butter;2|onion|sliced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;2 tsp|coriander;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|garam masala;1/3 cup|almonds|ground;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 cup|chicken broth;|salt|to taste","Toss the chicken with yogurt and 1 teaspoon salt and marinate 30 minutes.|Melt the butter in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onions 10 minutes until soft and pale gold.|Add the garlic, ginger, coriander, cumin and turmeric and cook 1 minute.|Add the chicken with its marinade and brown lightly for 5 minutes.|Stir in the ground almonds and broth, cover and simmer 20 minutes until the chicken is cooked through.|Stir in the cream and garam masala and simmer 5 minutes. Serve with basmati rice.","Indian"],
[3178,"Chicken Vindaloo","comfort","🌶️",60,"Medium",9,4,"A fiery, tangy Goan-style curry of chicken in a vinegar and chile marinade.","2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, cut in chunks;1/4 cup|apple cider vinegar;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;6 clove|garlic|minced;2 tsp|cumin;1 tbsp|paprika;1 tsp|cayenne;1 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|mustard|ground seed or mustard powder;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;2|onion|finely chopped;2 tbsp|tomato paste;2|potatoes|cubed, optional;|salt|to taste","Mix the vinegar, ginger, half the garlic, cumin, paprika, cayenne, turmeric and mustard into a paste. Coat the chicken and marinate at least 1 hour.|Heat the oil in a heavy pot over medium heat and cook the onions 10 minutes until browned.|Add the remaining garlic and tomato paste and cook 2 minutes.|Add the chicken with marinade, salt and 1 cup water, and add the potatoes if using.|Cover and simmer 30 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the chicken and potatoes are tender and the sauce is thick.|Taste, adjust salt and serve with rice.","Indian"],
[3179,"Paneer Tikka","sides","🍢",45,"Easy",7.5,4,"Skewers of spiced yogurt-marinated paneer and peppers, charred until smoky.","14 oz|paneer|1 1/2-inch cubes;1/2 cup|greek yogurt;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|garam masala;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|bell pepper|cut in chunks;1|red onion|cut in chunks;|salt|to taste","Whisk the yogurt, ginger, garlic, spices, lemon juice, oil and salt.|Fold in the paneer, pepper and onion and marinate at least 30 minutes.|Thread onto skewers, alternating paneer and vegetables.|Heat the oven broiler to high, or a grill to 450°F.|Cook 4 to 5 minutes per side, turning, until charred at the edges.|Serve with lemon wedges and mint chutney.","Indian"],
[3180,"Cucumber Raita","sides","🥒",10,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Cooling yogurt with cucumber and toasted cumin, the perfect foil for spicy curries.","1 cup|greek yogurt;1|cucumber|grated and squeezed dry;1/2 tsp|cumin|toasted and ground;1 clove|garlic|grated;2 tbsp|mint|chopped;1/4 tsp|cayenne;|salt|to taste","Toast the cumin seeds in a dry skillet over medium heat 1 minute until fragrant, then grind.|Whisk the yogurt with 2 tablespoons water until smooth.|Stir in the cucumber, garlic, mint and cumin.|Season with salt, chill 15 minutes and dust with cayenne before serving.","Indian"],
[3181,"Gulab Jamun","treats","🍩",60,"Medium",9,8,"Soft milk-based dumplings fried golden and soaked in cardamom rose syrup.","1 cup|milk|powder, full fat;1/4 cup|flour;1/2 tsp|baking powder;2 tbsp|butter|melted;1/4 cup|milk|warm, plus more as needed;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 1/2 cup|sugar;1 1/2 cup|water;4|cardamom pods|crushed;1 tsp|lemon juice","Mix the milk powder, flour and baking powder, then work in the butter and enough warm milk to make a soft, smooth dough. Do not overknead.|Roll into 16 smooth, crack-free balls.|Simmer the sugar, water and cardamom for 8 minutes into a light syrup, add the lemon juice and keep warm.|Heat the oil to 275°F, a low temperature.|Fry the balls in batches 6 to 8 minutes, turning, until deep golden brown.|Drop the hot jamun into the warm syrup and soak at least 1 hour before serving.","Indian"],
[3182,"Chicken Jalfrezi","quick","🌶️",35,"Easy",8.5,4,"A bright stir-fried curry of chicken, peppers and onions in a spicy tomato sauce.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in strips;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|sliced;1|bell pepper|sliced;1|red pepper|sliced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;1 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|cayenne;1 can|crushed tomatoes|14 oz;1 tsp|garam masala;|salt|to taste;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a large skillet over high heat and sear the chicken 4 minutes until browned. Remove.|Add the remaining oil, onion and peppers and stir-fry 4 minutes until just tender-crisp. Remove half.|Add the garlic, ginger and spices to the pan for 1 minute.|Pour in the tomatoes and salt and simmer 8 minutes.|Return the chicken and all vegetables and cook 5 minutes until the chicken is cooked through.|Finish with garam masala and cilantro.","Indian"],
[3183,"Kheer","treats","🍚",60,"Easy",9,6,"Slow-simmered rice pudding scented with cardamom and studded with nuts.","1/2 cup|rice|basmati, rinsed;6 cup|milk;1/2 cup|sugar;4|cardamom pods|crushed;1/4 cup|almonds|sliced;1/4 cup|raisins;1 pinch|saffron","Bring the milk to a gentle simmer in a heavy pot over medium heat.|Add the rice and cardamom and simmer on low for 35 to 40 minutes, stirring often to prevent sticking.|Stir in the sugar, saffron, raisins and half the almonds and cook 10 minutes until thick and creamy.|Serve warm or chilled, topped with the remaining almonds.","Indian"],
[3184,"Vegetable Pakoras","sides","🧅",35,"Easy",7.5,6,"Crunchy chickpea-flour fritters of onion, potato and spinach.","1 cup|chickpea flour|besan;1/2 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 tsp|salt;2|onion|thinly sliced;1|potatoes|thinly sliced;1 cup|spinach|chopped;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Whisk the chickpea flour, baking powder, spices and salt with about 1/2 cup water into a thick batter.|Fold in the onion, potato and spinach so everything is coated.|Heat the oil to 350°F.|Drop spoonfuls of batter into the oil and fry in batches 4 to 5 minutes, turning, until deep golden and cooked through.|Drain on paper towels and serve hot with chutney.","Indian"],
[3185,"Rajma","comfort","🫘",50,"Easy",9,4,"Punjabi kidney beans in a thick, spiced tomato gravy, served over rice.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1|onion|finely chopped;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|crushed tomatoes|14 oz;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|cayenne;2 can|kidney beans|15 oz each, drained;1 tsp|garam masala;|salt|to taste;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat and toast the cumin 30 seconds.|Add the onion and cook 8 minutes until golden, then the ginger and garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the tomatoes, coriander, turmeric, paprika, cayenne and salt and cook 8 minutes until thick.|Add the beans and 1 1/2 cups water and simmer 25 minutes, mashing some beans to thicken.|Stir in the garam masala and cilantro and serve with rice.","Indian"],
[3186,"Keema Matar","comfort","🍛",40,"Easy",9,4,"Spiced minced meat simmered with peas and tomatoes, great with naan or rice.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|chopped;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 lb|ground beef;2|tomatoes|chopped;1 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 cup|frozen peas;1 tsp|garam masala;|salt|to taste;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onion 7 minutes until golden.|Add the ginger and garlic for 1 minute, then the beef and cook 8 minutes, breaking it up, until browned.|Stir in the cumin, coriander, turmeric, cayenne and salt and cook 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes and 1/2 cup water and simmer 10 minutes.|Add the peas and cook 5 minutes more.|Finish with garam masala and cilantro.","Indian"],
[3187,"Thai Red Curry","quick","🍛",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Chicken and vegetables in a creamy, spicy coconut red curry sauce.","1 can|coconut milk|14 oz;3 tbsp|red curry paste;1 lb|chicken breast|sliced thin;1 cup|chicken broth;1|bell pepper|sliced;1 cup|bamboo shoots|canned, drained;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1/2 cup|basil|Thai or regular;1|lime|juiced;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Scoop the thick cream from the top of the coconut milk into a pot over medium heat and fry the curry paste 2 minutes.|Add the chicken and cook 3 minutes, stirring.|Pour in the remaining coconut milk and broth and bring to a simmer.|Add the bell pepper, bamboo shoots, fish sauce and sugar and cook 8 to 10 minutes until the chicken is cooked through.|Stir in the basil and lime juice and serve over rice.","Thai"],
[3188,"Mango Sticky Rice","treats","🥭",60,"Easy",9,4,"Sweet coconut sticky rice served with ripe mango slices.","1 cup|rice|Thai glutinous sweet rice, soaked 4 hours;1 can|coconut milk|14 oz, divided;1/3 cup|sugar;1/2 tsp|salt;2|mango|ripe, peeled and sliced;1 tsp|cornstarch;1 tbsp|sesame seeds|toasted","Drain the soaked rice and steam over boiling water in a lined steamer for 25 minutes until tender and translucent.|Warm 3/4 cup coconut milk with the sugar and 1/4 teaspoon salt until dissolved.|Fold the hot rice into the sweetened coconut milk, cover and let sit 20 minutes to absorb.|Whisk the remaining coconut milk, cornstarch and remaining salt in a pot and heat until slightly thickened, about 3 minutes.|Serve the rice with mango slices, a drizzle of the sauce and sesame seeds.","Thai"],
[3189,"Chicken Satay","sides","🍢",50,"Easy",7.5,6,"Turmeric-coconut marinated chicken skewers with a rich peanut dipping sauce.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, sliced in strips;1/2 cup|coconut milk;1 tbsp|curry powder;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1/2 cup|peanut butter;1/2 cup|coconut milk;1 tbsp|red curry paste;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|lime juice;1 tbsp|brown sugar;|salt|to taste","Mix the 1/2 cup coconut milk, curry powder, soy sauce, sugar and fish sauce, add the chicken and marinate 30 minutes while soaking wooden skewers in water.|Thread the chicken onto the skewers.|Whisk the peanut butter, remaining coconut milk, curry paste, soy sauce, lime juice and sugar in a small pot and warm over low heat 5 minutes, thinning with water if needed.|Grill or broil the skewers at high heat 3 to 4 minutes per side until charred and cooked through.|Serve with the peanut sauce.","Thai"],
[3190,"Larb Gai","light","🥬",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Zesty Thai minced chicken salad with lime, fish sauce, herbs and toasted rice powder.","1 lb|ground chicken;2 tbsp|rice|uncooked, for rice powder;3 tbsp|lime juice;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;3|shallot|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced;1/2 cup|mint|torn;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1 head|butter lettuce|leaves separated","Toast the uncooked rice in a dry skillet over medium heat 5 minutes until golden, then grind into a coarse powder.|Cook the chicken in a skillet with 1/4 cup water over medium heat 6 to 8 minutes, breaking it up, until cooked through.|Take off the heat and stir in the lime juice, fish sauce, sugar and pepper flakes.|Fold in the shallots, green onion, mint, cilantro and rice powder.|Serve warm in lettuce leaves.","Thai"],
[3191,"Som Tam","light","🥗",20,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crunchy green papaya salad pounded with lime, chile, peanuts and tomatoes.","4 cup|green papaya|shredded, or carrot and cabbage;2 clove|garlic;2|chili|Thai, to taste;1 cup|green beans|cut in 1-inch pieces;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;3 tbsp|lime juice;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1/4 cup|peanuts|roasted","Pound the garlic and chiles in a large mortar, or mash them in a bowl, into a rough paste.|Add the green beans and bruise them lightly.|Add the lime juice, fish sauce and sugar and stir until the sugar dissolves.|Add the papaya and tomatoes and toss, lightly pounding to release their juices.|Top with the peanuts and serve right away.","Thai"],
[3192,"Khao Soi","soup","🍜",50,"Medium",9.5,4,"Northern Thai curry noodle soup with chicken, coconut milk and crispy noodles.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|red curry paste;1 tbsp|curry powder;1 tsp|turmeric;1 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, cut in chunks;1 can|coconut milk|14 oz;3 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|brown sugar;8 oz|egg noodles;1/2 cup|red onion|thinly sliced;2|lime|cut in wedges;1/4 cup|cilantro;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for crispy noodles","Fry a handful of the dry egg noodles in 1/2 cup hot oil 20 to 30 seconds until puffed and golden, then drain on paper towels.|Heat 2 tablespoons oil in a pot over medium heat and fry the curry paste, curry powder and turmeric 2 minutes.|Add the chicken and stir 3 minutes.|Add the coconut milk, broth, fish sauce and sugar and simmer 20 minutes.|Boil the remaining noodles according to the package and divide among bowls.|Ladle the curry over the noodles and top with crispy noodles, red onion, cilantro and lime wedges.","Thai"],
[3193,"Thai Yellow Curry","comfort","🍛",40,"Easy",9,4,"A mild, golden coconut curry with chicken and potatoes.","1 can|coconut milk|14 oz;3 tbsp|curry powder;1 tbsp|red curry paste;1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, cut in chunks;2|potatoes|cubed;1|onion|cut in wedges;1 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|lime juice;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Scoop the thick cream from the coconut milk into a pot over medium heat and fry with the curry powder and paste 2 minutes.|Add the chicken and onion and stir 3 minutes.|Add the remaining coconut milk, broth, potatoes, fish sauce and sugar.|Simmer 20 minutes until the potatoes and chicken are tender.|Finish with lime juice and serve over rice.","Thai"],
[3194,"Thai Cashew Chicken","quick","🥜",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Stir-fried chicken with cashews, peppers and a glossy savory-sweet sauce.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|bite-size pieces;1 tbsp|cornstarch;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1|bell pepper|diced;1/2|onion|cut in wedges;1/2 cup|cashews|roasted;3 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Toss the chicken with the cornstarch.|Heat the oil in a wok over high heat and stir-fry the chicken 4 to 5 minutes until browned and cooked. Remove.|Add the garlic, pepper and onion and stir-fry 2 minutes.|Mix the oyster sauce, soy sauce, fish sauce, sugar and 2 tablespoons water.|Return the chicken, add the sauce and cashews and toss 2 minutes until glossy.|Top with green onion and serve over rice.","Thai"],
[3195,"Thai Pineapple Fried Rice","quick","🍍",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Fried rice with sweet pineapple, cashews and curry powder, often served in a pineapple.","3 cup|rice|cooked and chilled;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/2|onion|diced;2|eggs|beaten;1 1/2 cup|pineapple|diced;1/2 cup|frozen peas;1 tsp|curry powder;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1/2 cup|cashews|roasted;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced","Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok over high heat and scramble the eggs 1 minute. Remove.|Add the remaining oil, garlic and onion and stir-fry 2 minutes.|Add the rice, breaking up clumps, and stir-fry 3 minutes.|Sprinkle in the curry powder, soy sauce and fish sauce and toss to coat.|Add the pineapple, peas, eggs and cashews and cook 3 minutes.|Top with green onion and serve.","Thai"],
[3196,"Pad Prik King","quick","🌶️",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"A dry stir-fry of pork and green beans in spicy red curry paste.","1 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|red curry paste;1 lb|green beans|cut in 2-inch lengths;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tsp|sugar;2|lime|leaves, optional;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Heat the oil in a wok over medium-high heat and fry the curry paste 1 minute.|Add the pork and stir-fry 3 minutes until no longer pink.|Add the green beans and stir-fry 5 minutes until crisp-tender.|Add the fish sauce, soy sauce, sugar and 2 tablespoons water and toss 2 minutes.|Serve over rice.","Thai"],
[3197,"Thai Garlic Pepper Pork","quick","🥩",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Fried pork slices in a punchy garlic and black pepper coating.","1 1/2 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;8 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|black pepper|coarsely ground;2 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tsp|sugar;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving;1|cucumber|sliced, for serving","Mix the garlic, pepper, oyster sauce, soy sauce, fish sauce and sugar, add the pork and marinate 15 minutes.|Heat the oil in a wide skillet over high heat.|Cook the pork in a single layer in batches 2 to 3 minutes per side until browned and cooked through.|Serve with rice and cucumber slices.","Thai"],
[3198,"Gai Yang","comfort","🍗",75,"Easy",9,4,"Thai grilled chicken marinated in lemongrass, garlic and cilantro root, with a sweet chili dip.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;4 clove|garlic;1/4 cup|cilantro|stems and leaves;2 tbsp|lemongrass|chopped;2 tbsp|fish sauce;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|honey;1 tbsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|sweet chili sauce|for dipping","Blend the garlic, cilantro, lemongrass, fish sauce, soy sauce, honey and pepper into a paste.|Coat the chicken and marinate at least 1 hour, or overnight.|Heat the oven to 425°F, or a grill to medium.|Roast on a rack-lined sheet pan 35 to 40 minutes until browned and 175°F inside, or grill about 30 minutes, turning.|Rest 5 minutes and serve with sweet chili sauce.","Thai"],
[3199,"Fresh Spring Rolls","light","🥬",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Rice paper rolls of shrimp, herbs and vermicelli with a peanut hoisin dip.","8|rice paper|8-inch rounds;12|shrimp|cooked, peeled and halved;2 oz|rice noodles|vermicelli, cooked;1 head|butter lettuce|leaves separated;1|carrots|julienned;1|cucumber|julienned;1/2 cup|mint;1/2 cup|cilantro;1/4 cup|hoisin sauce;2 tbsp|peanut butter;1 tsp|sriracha","Whisk the hoisin, peanut butter, sriracha and 2 tablespoons water into a dipping sauce.|Dip one rice paper into warm water for 10 seconds until just pliable and lay it on a damp board.|Arrange 3 shrimp halves in a row near the edge, then layer lettuce, noodles, carrot, cucumber and herbs.|Fold the bottom edge up over the filling, fold in the sides and roll tightly.|Repeat with the remaining wrappers and serve with the sauce.","Vietnamese"],
[3200,"Vietnamese Lemongrass Chicken","comfort","🍗",45,"Easy",9,4,"Chicken seared in a fragrant lemongrass, garlic and fish sauce marinade.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, sliced;3 stalk|lemongrass|minced, white part;4 clove|garlic|minced;2|shallot|minced;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Mix the lemongrass, garlic, shallots, fish sauce, sugar, soy sauce and pepper.|Add the chicken and marinate at least 30 minutes.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.|Cook the chicken in batches 5 to 6 minutes, turning, until browned and cooked through.|Sprinkle with pepper flakes and serve over rice.","Vietnamese"],
[3201,"Shaking Beef","quick","🥩",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Seared garlicky cubes of beef tossed in the wok, served on greens with lime-pepper dip (bo luc lac).","1 1/2 lb|sirloin steak|1-inch cubes;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|red onion|cut in wedges;2 tbsp|butter;4 cup|lettuce|for serving;2|tomatoes|sliced;2 tbsp|lime juice;|salt|to taste","Toss the beef with half the garlic, soy sauce, oyster sauce, sugar and 1 teaspoon pepper and marinate 20 minutes.|Mix the lime juice, 1 teaspoon pepper and 1/2 teaspoon salt for the dipping sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok over very high heat and sear half the beef 2 minutes, shaking the pan, until browned. Repeat with the rest.|Add the onion and remaining garlic and cook 1 minute, then add the butter and return all the beef.|Serve on a bed of lettuce and tomatoes with the dipping sauce.","Vietnamese"],
[3202,"Bun Cha","comfort","🍜",60,"Medium",9,4,"Hanoi grilled pork patties and slices in sweet-tangy broth with rice noodles and herbs.","1 lb|ground pork;1 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;3|shallot|minced;3 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|fish sauce;2 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|honey;1 tsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|fish sauce|for dipping broth;1/3 cup|sugar;1/4 cup|rice vinegar;1|carrots|julienned;8 oz|rice noodles|vermicelli;2 cup|lettuce|for serving;1/2 cup|mint;1/2 cup|cilantro","Mix the ground pork and sliced pork with the shallots, garlic, 3 tablespoons fish sauce, 2 tablespoons sugar, honey and pepper and marinate 30 minutes.|Stir the dipping fish sauce, 1/3 cup sugar, vinegar and 1 1/2 cups warm water until dissolved, and add the carrot.|Form the ground pork into small patties.|Grill or pan-sear the patties and pork slices over medium-high heat 4 minutes per side until charred and cooked through.|Cook the noodles per package and drain.|Serve the pork in the broth with noodles, lettuce and herbs on the side.","Vietnamese"],
[3203,"Cha Gio","sides","🥟",60,"Medium",7.5,6,"Crispy Vietnamese fried spring rolls filled with pork, shrimp and mushrooms.","1/2 lb|ground pork;1/4 lb|shrimp|minced;1 cup|mushrooms|finely chopped;1|carrots|grated;2 oz|rice noodles|vermicelli, soaked and chopped;3|shallot|minced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1|eggs;20|rice paper|8-inch rounds;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/4 cup|fish sauce|for dipping;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|lime juice","Mix the pork, shrimp, mushrooms, carrot, noodles, shallots, garlic, 1 tablespoon fish sauce, pepper and egg thoroughly.|Soften a rice paper in warm water for a few seconds and lay it flat.|Spoon 2 tablespoons filling near the bottom, fold the bottom over, fold in the sides and roll tight.|Heat the oil to 340°F and fry the rolls in batches 8 to 10 minutes until golden and crisp.|Drain on paper towels.|Stir the dipping fish sauce, sugar, lime juice and 1/4 cup water together and serve with the rolls.","Vietnamese"],
[3204,"Pho Ga","soup","🍜",90,"Medium",9.5,6,"Clear Vietnamese chicken noodle soup with charred ginger, onion and warm spices.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;1|onion|halved;1|ginger|4-inch piece, halved;3|star anise;1|cinnamon|stick;4|cloves;1 tbsp|coriander;3 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;14 oz|rice noodles|flat;2 cup|bean sprouts;1/2 cup|basil|Thai;1/2 cup|cilantro;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced;2|lime|cut in wedges;|salt|to taste","Char the onion and ginger directly over a flame or under the broiler 5 to 8 minutes until blackened in spots.|Toast the star anise, cinnamon, cloves and coriander in a dry pot 1 minute.|Add the chicken, onion, ginger and 3 quarts water, bring to a boil, then skim and simmer 40 minutes.|Remove the chicken, shred the meat and discard the bones and skin.|Strain the broth, season with the fish sauce, sugar and salt, and keep hot.|Cook the noodles per package and divide among bowls.|Add the chicken and ladle in the hot broth. Serve with sprouts, herbs and lime.","Vietnamese"],
[3205,"Bun Bo Xao","quick","🥩",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Lemongrass beef stir-fry over vermicelli, fresh herbs and peanuts.","1 lb|flank steak|sliced thin;2 stalk|lemongrass|minced;3 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;8 oz|rice noodles|vermicelli;1|cucumber|julienned;1|carrots|julienned;2 cup|lettuce|shredded;1/2 cup|mint;1/4 cup|peanuts|crushed;1/4 cup|fish sauce|for dressing;3 tbsp|lime juice;2 tbsp|sugar","Marinate the beef with the lemongrass, garlic, 2 tablespoons fish sauce and 1 tablespoon sugar for 15 minutes.|Stir the dressing fish sauce, lime juice, 2 tablespoons sugar and 3 tablespoons water.|Cook the noodles per package, rinse and drain.|Heat the oil in a wok over high heat and sear the beef 2 to 3 minutes until browned.|Divide the noodles, lettuce, cucumber, carrot and mint among bowls and top with beef and peanuts.|Drizzle with the dressing.","Vietnamese"],
[3206,"Com Ga","comfort","🍗",60,"Medium",9,4,"Vietnamese poached chicken over ginger-scented rice with a scallion dipping sauce.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;1|ginger|2-inch piece, sliced;1|onion|halved;2 cup|rice|jasmine, rinsed;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|lime juice;1 tsp|sugar;1|cucumber|sliced;|salt|to taste","Cover the chicken with water in a pot, add the ginger, onion and 1 tablespoon salt and bring to a boil.|Reduce the heat, cover and simmer 25 minutes until the chicken reaches 175°F.|Remove the chicken and keep warm, reserving the broth.|Sauté the garlic in 1 tablespoon oil 1 minute, add the rice and stir 1 minute, then add 3 cups strained broth and cook covered 18 minutes.|Heat the remaining oil and pour over the green onion with the fish sauce, lime juice and sugar to make a dipping sauce.|Chop the chicken and serve over the rice with cucumber and sauce.","Vietnamese"],
[3207,"Chicken Adobo","comfort","🍗",55,"Easy",9,4,"The Filipino national dish: chicken braised in soy sauce, vinegar and garlic.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;1/2 cup|soy sauce;1/2 cup|apple cider vinegar;1 head|garlic|cloves smashed;3|bay leaves;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Combine the chicken, soy sauce, vinegar, garlic, bay leaves and pepper and marinate 30 minutes.|Lift the chicken from the marinade and pat dry.|Heat the oil in a large pot over medium-high heat and brown the chicken 4 minutes per side.|Add the marinade and 1/2 cup water, bring to a boil, cover and simmer 30 minutes.|Uncover, add the sugar and simmer 8 to 10 minutes until the sauce reduces and thickens.|Serve over rice.","Filipino"],
[3208,"Lumpia Shanghai","sides","🥟",60,"Medium",7.5,8,"Thin, crisp Filipino spring rolls stuffed with seasoned pork and vegetables.","1 lb|ground pork;1|carrots|finely grated;1/2|onion|minced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced;1|eggs;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|salt;30|lumpia wrappers|spring roll wrappers;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/2 cup|sweet chili sauce|for dipping","Mix the pork, carrot, onion, garlic, green onion, egg, soy sauce, pepper and salt well.|Place about 1 tablespoon filling near the corner of a wrapper and roll up tightly, folding in the sides.|Seal the edge with a dab of water.|Heat the oil to 350°F.|Fry the rolls in batches 4 to 5 minutes, turning, until deep golden and cooked through.|Drain on paper towels and serve with sweet chili sauce.","Filipino"],
[3209,"Huli Huli Chicken","comfort","🍍",60,"Easy",9,6,"Hawaiian rotisserie-style chicken glazed with a sweet pineapple, ginger and soy sauce.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;3/4 cup|pineapple|juice;1/2 cup|soy sauce;1/2 cup|brown sugar;1/4 cup|ketchup;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Whisk the pineapple juice, soy sauce, sugar, ketchup, ginger, garlic, vinegar and pepper.|Reserve 1 cup of the sauce, and marinate the chicken in the rest for at least 4 hours.|Simmer the reserved sauce in a small pot 8 to 10 minutes until thickened to a glaze.|Heat a grill to medium or the oven to 400°F.|Cook the chicken 30 to 35 minutes, turning often, until 175°F inside.|Brush with the glaze during the last 10 minutes and serve.","Hawaiian"],
[3210,"Loco Moco","comfort","🍳",40,"Easy",9,4,"Hawaiian comfort plate: rice topped with a beef patty, fried egg and brown gravy.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1/4 cup|breadcrumbs;1|egg;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|butter;1/2|onion|sliced;3 tbsp|flour;2 cup|beef broth;1 tbsp|soy sauce;4|eggs|for frying;4 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Mix the beef, breadcrumbs, egg, salt and pepper and form 4 patties.|Cook the patties in a skillet over medium-high heat 4 to 5 minutes per side until cooked through. Remove.|In the same pan, melt the butter and cook the onion 4 minutes, then stir in the flour for 1 minute.|Whisk in the broth and soy sauce and simmer 5 minutes until the gravy thickens.|Fry the eggs sunny side up.|Layer rice, patty and egg on each plate and ladle on the gravy.","Hawaiian"],
[3211,"Chicken Parmesan","comfort","🍗",45,"Medium",9,4,"Crisp breaded chicken cutlets under marinara and melted mozzarella, served over spaghetti.","2|chicken breast|about 1 1/2 lb, sliced in half horizontally;1/2 cup|flour|;2|eggs|beaten;1 cup|panko|;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated, divided;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/2 cup|olive oil|for frying;1 1/2 cup|marinara sauce|;1 1/2 cup|mozzarella|shredded;8 oz|spaghetti|;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 425°F. Pound the chicken cutlets to an even 1/2 inch thickness and season with salt and pepper.|Set up three shallow dishes: flour, beaten eggs, and panko mixed with 1/4 cup parmesan and the Italian seasoning.|Dredge each cutlet in flour, dip in egg, then press into the panko mixture to coat well.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Fry the cutlets 3 minutes per side until golden, then move to a baking sheet.|Spoon marinara over each cutlet, top with mozzarella and the remaining parmesan, and bake 10 to 12 minutes until bubbly and the chicken reaches 165°F.|Meanwhile boil the spaghetti in salted water until al dente and drain.|Serve the chicken over the spaghetti with extra sauce and parsley.","Italian"],
[3212,"Chicken Piccata","quick","🍋",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Thin pan-seared chicken in a bright lemon, caper and butter sauce.","2|chicken breast|sliced in half horizontally into 4 cutlets;1/2 cup|flour|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;3 tbsp|olive oil|;4 tbsp|butter|divided;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|white wine|;1/2 cup|chicken broth|;3 tbsp|lemon juice|;3 tbsp|capers|drained;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Pound the cutlets to 1/2 inch thick, season with salt and pepper, and dredge in flour, shaking off the excess.|Heat the olive oil and 1 tablespoon butter in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the chicken 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden and cooked through. Move to a plate.|Lower the heat to medium, add the garlic, and cook 30 seconds.|Pour in the wine and scrape up the browned bits. Simmer 2 minutes, then add the broth and lemon juice and simmer 3 minutes until slightly reduced.|Whisk in the remaining 3 tablespoons butter and the capers.|Return the chicken to the pan and spoon the sauce over it for 1 minute. Sprinkle with parsley and serve.","Italian"],
[3213,"Chicken Marsala","comfort","🍄",35,"Easy",9,4,"Golden chicken cutlets and mushrooms simmered in a rich Marsala wine sauce.","2|chicken breast|sliced into 4 thin cutlets;1/2 cup|flour|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|olive oil|;3 tbsp|butter|divided;8 oz|mushrooms|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;3/4 cup|marsala wine|;3/4 cup|chicken broth|;1/4 cup|heavy cream|;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Pound the chicken to 1/2 inch thick, season, and dredge in flour.|Heat the olive oil and 1 tablespoon butter in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Brown the chicken 3 to 4 minutes per side and remove to a plate.|Add 1 tablespoon butter and the mushrooms. Cook 5 to 6 minutes until browned, then add the garlic for 30 seconds.|Pour in the Marsala and simmer 3 minutes, scraping the pan.|Add the broth and simmer 5 minutes until reduced by about a third. Stir in the cream and remaining butter.|Return the chicken to the pan and simmer 3 minutes until cooked through. Top with parsley.","Italian"],
[3214,"Shrimp Scampi","quick","🍤",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Garlicky shrimp in a lemon-butter white wine sauce tossed with linguine.","12 oz|linguine|;1 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|olive oil|;4 tbsp|butter|;5 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes|;1/2 cup|white wine|;2 tbsp|lemon juice|;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Boil the linguine in salted water until al dente. Save 1/2 cup of the pasta water, then drain.|Pat the shrimp dry and season with salt and pepper.|Heat the olive oil and 1 tablespoon butter in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the shrimp 1 to 2 minutes per side until just pink, then remove.|Lower the heat, add the remaining butter, garlic, and red pepper flakes, and cook 30 seconds.|Add the wine and lemon juice and simmer 3 minutes.|Toss in the linguine, shrimp, and a splash of pasta water until glossy. Finish with parsley.","Italian"],
[3215,"Spaghetti and Meatballs","comfort","🍝",60,"Medium",9,6,"Tender baked meatballs simmered in a simple tomato sauce over spaghetti.","1 lb|ground beef|;1/2 lb|ground pork|;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs|;1/4 cup|milk|;2|eggs|;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;3 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tsp|salt|;1/2 tsp|black pepper|;2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|finely diced;2 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz each;1 tsp|dried basil|;1 lb|spaghetti|","Heat the oven to 400°F. Soak the breadcrumbs in the milk for 5 minutes.|Mix the beef, pork, soaked crumbs, eggs, parmesan, half the garlic, parsley, salt, and pepper gently. Roll into about 24 meatballs.|Bake on a lined sheet pan 18 to 20 minutes until browned and cooked through.|Meanwhile heat the olive oil in a large pot and cook the onion 5 minutes. Add the remaining garlic for 30 seconds.|Stir in the crushed tomatoes, basil, and a pinch of salt. Add the meatballs and simmer 20 minutes.|Cook the spaghetti in salted water until al dente, drain, and serve topped with meatballs and sauce.","Italian"],
[3216,"Cacio e Pepe","quick","🧀",20,"Medium",8.5,4,"Roman pasta with just pecorino, black pepper and starchy pasta water.","1 lb|spaghetti|;2 tsp|black pepper|freshly cracked;2 cup|pecorino romano|finely grated;2 tbsp|butter|optional for richness;|salt|to taste","Boil the spaghetti in well-salted water, using less water than usual so it stays starchy. Cook until 1 minute shy of al dente.|Toast the pepper in a large dry skillet over medium heat for 1 minute.|Ladle in 1 cup of pasta water and the butter and bring to a simmer.|Use tongs to move the pasta into the skillet and cook 1 minute, tossing.|Take the pan off the heat, add the pecorino in handfuls, and toss hard, adding splashes of pasta water until the sauce is smooth and creamy.|Serve right away with extra pepper.","Italian"],
[3217,"Penne alla Vodka","comfort","🍝",30,"Easy",9,4,"Penne in a creamy blush tomato sauce with a splash of vodka and parmesan.","1 lb|penne|;2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|finely diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|tomato paste|;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes|;1/3 cup|vodka|;1 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz;3/4 cup|heavy cream|;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;2 tbsp|basil|torn;|salt|to taste","Boil the penne in salted water until al dente. Save 1 cup of pasta water and drain.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onion 5 minutes. Add the garlic and red pepper flakes for 1 minute.|Stir in the tomato paste and cook 2 minutes until it darkens.|Add the vodka and simmer 2 minutes until mostly evaporated.|Add the crushed tomatoes and simmer 10 minutes, then stir in the cream and salt.|Toss in the penne and parmesan, loosening with pasta water. Top with basil.","Italian"],
[3218,"Lasagna Bolognese","comfort","🍝",180,"Medium",9,10,"Layers of pasta, slow-simmered meat sauce, creamy bechamel and parmesan.","2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|finely diced;1|carrots|finely diced;1 stalk|celery|finely diced;1 lb|ground beef|;1/2 lb|ground pork|;1/2 cup|white wine|;1 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz;2 tbsp|tomato paste|;|salt|to taste;4 tbsp|butter|;1/3 cup|flour|;3 cup|milk|;1/4 tsp|nutmeg|ground;12|lasagna noodles|;1 1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1 cup|mozzarella|shredded","Heat the oil in a large pot and cook the onion, carrot, and celery 8 minutes. Add the beef and pork and brown 8 minutes, breaking it up.|Add the wine and cook 3 minutes, then stir in the tomatoes, paste, and salt. Simmer partly covered 1 hour, stirring occasionally.|For the bechamel, melt the butter, whisk in the flour for 1 minute, and slowly add the milk. Simmer 5 to 8 minutes until thick, then season with salt and nutmeg.|Boil the noodles 2 minutes short of the package time and drain. Heat the oven to 375°F.|In a 9x13 dish layer sauce, noodles, bechamel, and parmesan. Repeat to make 3 layers, finishing with bechamel, parmesan, and mozzarella.|Cover with foil and bake 30 minutes, then uncover and bake 20 minutes until golden. Rest 15 minutes before cutting.","Italian"],
[3219,"Tiramisu","treats","🍰",40,"Medium",9,9,"No-bake dessert of espresso-soaked ladyfingers layered with mascarpone cream and cocoa.","4|eggs|yolks only;2/3 cup|sugar|;16 oz|mascarpone|;1 cup|heavy cream|;1 1/2 cup|espresso|strong, cooled;3 tbsp|coffee liqueur|optional;24|ladyfingers|;2 tbsp|cocoa powder|unsweetened","Whisk the yolks and sugar in a heatproof bowl set over simmering water for 8 minutes until thick and pale and 160°F. Cool for 10 minutes.|Beat in the mascarpone until smooth.|Whip the cream to stiff peaks and fold it into the mascarpone mixture.|Mix the espresso and liqueur in a shallow dish. Dip each ladyfinger briefly, 1 to 2 seconds per side, and line the bottom of an 8x8 dish.|Spread half the cream over the ladyfingers, add a second dipped layer, then the remaining cream.|Chill at least 6 hours, then dust with cocoa before serving.","Italian"],
[3220,"Cannoli Dip","treats","🍨",15,"Very easy",9,10,"Sweet ricotta and mascarpone dip with mini chocolate chips, scooped up with cannoli shells or cookies.","15 oz|ricotta|well drained;8 oz|mascarpone|;1 cup|powdered sugar|;1 tsp|vanilla|;1/2 tsp|cinnamon|;3/4 cup|chocolate chips|mini;|waffle cookies|for dipping, to taste","Drain the ricotta in a fine strainer for 15 minutes, pressing out extra liquid.|Beat the ricotta, mascarpone, powdered sugar, vanilla, and cinnamon until smooth.|Fold in 1/2 cup of the chocolate chips.|Spoon into a bowl and top with the remaining chips.|Chill for 30 minutes, then serve with cannoli shells, waffle cookies, or graham crackers.","Italian"],
[3221,"Bruschetta","sides","🍅",20,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Toasted garlic bread topped with fresh tomato, basil and olive oil.","1|french bread|baguette, sliced 1/2 inch;4|tomatoes|ripe Roma, diced;1/4 cup|basil|thinly sliced;2 clove|garlic|1 minced, 1 halved;3 tbsp|olive oil|divided;1 tbsp|balsamic glaze|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 400°F. Brush the bread slices with 2 tablespoons olive oil and bake on a sheet pan 8 to 10 minutes until crisp and golden.|Mix the tomatoes, basil, minced garlic, remaining oil, salt, and pepper. Let sit 10 minutes.|Rub the toasted slices with the cut side of the halved garlic.|Spoon the tomato mixture on top, drizzle with balsamic glaze, and serve right away.","Italian"],
[3222,"Minestrone","soup","🥣",50,"Easy",9.5,8,"Hearty Italian vegetable soup with beans, small pasta and a parmesan finish.","2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;6 cup|vegetable broth|;1 can|kidney beans|15 oz, drained;1|zucchini|diced;1 cup|green beans|cut in 1 inch pieces;1 cup|pasta shells|small;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;2 cup|spinach|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated","Heat the olive oil in a large pot and cook the onion, carrot, and celery 7 minutes.|Add the garlic and Italian seasoning for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, broth, beans, zucchini, and green beans. Bring to a boil and simmer 15 minutes.|Stir in the pasta and cook 8 to 10 minutes until tender.|Add the spinach until wilted, then season with salt and pepper.|Ladle into bowls and top with parmesan.","Italian"],
[3223,"Caprese Salad","sides","🍅",10,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Ripe tomato, fresh mozzarella and basil with olive oil and balsamic.","4|tomatoes|large ripe, sliced;8 oz|fresh mozzarella|sliced;1/4 cup|basil|whole leaves;3 tbsp|olive oil|;1 tbsp|balsamic glaze|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Slice the tomatoes and mozzarella about 1/4 inch thick.|Arrange them on a platter in overlapping rows, tucking a basil leaf between slices.|Drizzle with olive oil and balsamic glaze.|Season with flaky salt and pepper and serve at room temperature.","Italian"],
[3224,"Panna Cotta","treats","🍮",20,"Easy",9,6,"Silky chilled vanilla cream dessert with berry sauce.","1 packet|gelatin|unflavored, 2 1/4 tsp;3 tbsp|milk|cold;2 cup|heavy cream|;1/3 cup|sugar|;1 tsp|vanilla|;1 cup|strawberries|sliced;1 tbsp|sugar|for the berries","Sprinkle the gelatin over the cold milk and let it bloom for 5 minutes.|Heat the cream and sugar in a saucepan until steaming and the sugar dissolves. Do not boil.|Remove from the heat, whisk in the gelatin until fully dissolved, then add the vanilla.|Pour into 6 ramekins or glasses and chill at least 4 hours until set.|Toss the strawberries with 1 tablespoon sugar and let them release their juices.|Spoon the berries over the panna cotta, or unmold onto plates.","Italian"],
[3225,"Spaghetti Aglio e Olio","quick","🍝",20,"Very easy",8.5,4,"Spaghetti tossed in garlic-infused olive oil with chili flakes and parsley.","1 lb|spaghetti|;1/3 cup|olive oil|;6 clove|garlic|thinly sliced;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes|;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated, optional;|salt|to taste","Boil the spaghetti in well-salted water until al dente. Save 1 cup of pasta water and drain.|Meanwhile warm the olive oil and garlic in a large skillet over medium-low heat 3 to 4 minutes until the garlic is pale gold. Do not let it brown.|Add the red pepper flakes for 30 seconds.|Add the spaghetti and 1/2 cup pasta water and toss over medium heat 1 minute until the sauce clings.|Off the heat stir in parsley, add more pasta water if needed, and serve with parmesan.","Italian"],
[3226,"Chicken Saltimbocca","quick","🍗",30,"Medium",8.5,4,"Chicken cutlets topped with prosciutto and sage, pan-seared in a white wine butter sauce.","2|chicken breast|sliced into 4 cutlets;8|sage|fresh leaves;4 slice|prosciutto|;1/4 cup|flour|;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|olive oil|;3 tbsp|butter|;1/2 cup|white wine|;1/2 cup|chicken broth|;1 tbsp|lemon juice|","Pound the cutlets to 1/2 inch, season with pepper, and lay 2 sage leaves on each, then wrap with a slice of prosciutto, pressing to stick.|Lightly dust the cutlets with flour on the chicken side only.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Place the cutlets prosciutto-side down and cook 3 minutes, then flip and cook 3 to 4 minutes until 165°F. Remove to a plate.|Add the wine to the pan and simmer 2 minutes, then add the broth and lemon juice and simmer 3 minutes.|Whisk in the butter, return the chicken, and spoon the sauce over.","Italian"],
[3227,"Chicken Souvlaki","light","🍢",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Lemon-oregano marinated chicken skewers grilled and served with pita and tzatziki.","2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless skinless, cut in 1 inch cubes;1/4 cup|olive oil|;1/4 cup|lemon juice|;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tsp|oregano|dried;1 tsp|salt|;1/2 tsp|black pepper|;1 tsp|paprika|;4|pita|;1 cup|greek yogurt|for serving;1|cucumber|sliced;1|tomatoes|sliced","Whisk the olive oil, lemon juice, garlic, oregano, salt, pepper, and paprika. Toss with the chicken and marinate 30 minutes to 4 hours in the fridge.|Soak 8 wooden skewers in water if using them, then thread the chicken on.|Grill over medium-high heat or cook in a grill pan 10 to 12 minutes, turning, until browned and 165°F.|Warm the pita briefly on the grill.|Serve the skewers in pita with yogurt or tzatziki, cucumber, and tomato.","Greek"],
[3228,"Chicken Gyro Bowl","light","🥙",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Spiced chicken over rice with cucumber, tomato, feta and tzatziki.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless skinless, sliced;3 tbsp|olive oil|;2 tbsp|lemon juice|;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|oregano|;1 tsp|cumin|;1 tsp|paprika|;|salt|to taste;2 cup|rice|cooked;1|cucumber|diced;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1/2 cup|feta|crumbled;1 cup|greek yogurt|;|olives|kalamata, to taste","Toss the chicken with 2 tablespoons olive oil, lemon juice, garlic, oregano, cumin, paprika, and salt. Marinate 15 minutes or up to overnight.|Heat the remaining oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and cook the chicken 8 to 10 minutes until browned and cooked through.|Mix the yogurt with a pinch of salt and a squeeze of lemon for a quick sauce, or use tzatziki.|Divide the rice among bowls and top with chicken, cucumber, tomatoes, onion, feta, and olives.|Drizzle with the yogurt sauce.","Greek"],
[3229,"Spanakopita","sides","🥬",75,"Medium",7.5,8,"Flaky phyllo pie filled with spinach, feta, dill and herbs.","2 lb|frozen spinach|thawed and squeezed very dry;2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|finely diced;4|green onion|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;8 oz|feta|crumbled;1 cup|ricotta|;3|eggs|beaten;1/4 cup|dill|chopped;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1/4 tsp|nutmeg|;|black pepper|to taste;1 lb|phyllo dough|thawed;3/4 cup|butter|melted","Heat the oven to 375°F. Cook the onion in the olive oil 5 minutes, then add the green onion and garlic for 2 minutes. Cool slightly.|Combine the spinach, onion mixture, feta, ricotta, eggs, dill, parsley, nutmeg, and pepper.|Brush a 9x13 dish with butter. Layer 10 sheets of phyllo, brushing each with butter, keeping the rest covered with a damp towel.|Spread the filling over the phyllo, then layer 10 more buttered sheets on top. Tuck in the edges.|Score the top into squares with a sharp knife, cutting through the top layers.|Bake 45 to 50 minutes until deep golden. Rest 10 minutes before cutting.","Greek"],
[3230,"Pastitsio","comfort","🍝",120,"Medium",9,10,"Greek baked pasta with cinnamon-spiced meat sauce and thick bechamel.","1 lb|penne|or ziti;1 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|diced;1 lb|ground beef|;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|tomato paste|;1 can|crushed tomatoes|15 oz;1/2 cup|red wine|optional, or use broth;1/2 tsp|cinnamon|;1 tsp|oregano|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;4 tbsp|butter|;1/2 cup|flour|;4 cup|milk|warm;1/4 tsp|nutmeg|;3|eggs|beaten;1 cup|parmesan|grated, divided","Boil the pasta 2 minutes short of al dente, drain, and toss with 1/2 cup parmesan.|Brown the onion and beef in the olive oil 8 minutes. Add the garlic, tomato paste, tomatoes, wine, cinnamon, oregano, salt, and pepper and simmer 25 minutes until thick.|For the bechamel melt the butter, whisk in the flour for 1 minute, then slowly whisk in the milk. Cook, stirring, 8 to 10 minutes until thick. Season with salt and nutmeg.|Cool the sauce 5 minutes, then whisk in the eggs and 1/4 cup parmesan.|Heat the oven to 350°F. Layer half the pasta in a 9x13 dish, then all of the meat sauce, then the remaining pasta.|Spread the bechamel on top, sprinkle with the remaining parmesan, and bake 40 to 45 minutes until golden. Rest 15 minutes before cutting.","Greek"],
[3231,"Avgolemono Soup","soup","🍋",40,"Medium",9.5,6,"Silky Greek chicken soup with rice, thickened with egg and lemon.","8 cup|chicken broth|;1/2 cup|rice|long grain;2 cup|chicken breast|cooked and shredded;3|eggs|;1/3 cup|lemon juice|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|dill|chopped","Bring the broth to a boil in a large pot, add the rice, and simmer 15 to 18 minutes until tender.|Add the shredded chicken and warm through. Turn the heat to low.|Whisk the eggs in a bowl until frothy, then whisk in the lemon juice.|Slowly ladle in 2 cups of hot broth, a little at a time, whisking constantly to temper the eggs.|Stir the egg mixture back into the pot and heat gently 3 to 5 minutes without boiling until slightly thickened.|Season with salt and pepper and serve with dill.","Greek"],
[3232,"Greek Salad","sides","🥗",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Chunky tomato, cucumber, red onion, olives and feta with oregano and olive oil.","4|tomatoes|cut in wedges;1|cucumber|sliced in half moons;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1|bell pepper|green, sliced;1/2 cup|olives|kalamata;6 oz|feta|a slab or crumbled;1/4 cup|olive oil|;1 tbsp|red wine vinegar|;1 tsp|oregano|dried;|salt|to taste","Combine the tomatoes, cucumber, onion, bell pepper, and olives in a large bowl.|Whisk the olive oil, vinegar, oregano, and salt and pour over the vegetables. Toss gently.|Top with the feta and a sprinkle of oregano.|Serve right away.","Greek"],
[3233,"Tzatziki","sides","🥒",15,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Cool Greek yogurt dip with grated cucumber, garlic, lemon and dill.","1|cucumber|grated and squeezed dry;2 cup|greek yogurt|;2 clove|garlic|finely minced;1 tbsp|olive oil|;1 tbsp|lemon juice|;1 tbsp|dill|chopped;|salt|to taste","Grate the cucumber, salt it lightly, and let it sit 10 minutes, then squeeze out all the liquid in a towel.|Stir the cucumber into the yogurt with the garlic, olive oil, lemon juice, and dill.|Season with salt and chill at least 30 minutes so the flavors blend.|Serve with pita, vegetables, or grilled meat.","Greek"],
[3234,"Baklava","treats","🍯",90,"Medium",9,24,"Crisp phyllo layered with spiced walnuts and soaked in honey syrup.","1 lb|walnuts|finely chopped;1/2 cup|sugar|for the filling;1 tsp|cinnamon|;1/4 tsp|cloves|ground;1 lb|phyllo dough|thawed;1 cup|butter|melted;1 cup|water|;1 cup|sugar|for the syrup;1/2 cup|honey|;1|lemon|a few strips of peel and 1 tbsp juice;1 tsp|vanilla|","Heat the oven to 350°F. Mix the walnuts, 1/2 cup sugar, cinnamon, and cloves.|Brush a 9x13 pan with butter. Layer 8 phyllo sheets, brushing each with butter, trimming to fit.|Spread with one third of the nut mix, then top with 4 buttered sheets. Repeat twice more, ending with 8 buttered sheets on top.|Cut into diamonds or squares all the way through before baking.|Bake 45 to 50 minutes until deep golden.|Meanwhile simmer 1 cup water, 1 cup sugar, honey, lemon peel, and juice for 10 minutes, then stir in the vanilla. Cool.|Pour the cooled syrup over the hot baklava and let it set for at least 4 hours before serving.","Greek"],
[3235,"Greek Lemon Potatoes","sides","🥔",75,"Easy",7.5,6,"Oven-roasted potatoes soaked in lemon, garlic, oregano and olive oil until golden and tender.","3 lb|potatoes|yukon gold, cut in wedges;1/3 cup|olive oil|;1/3 cup|lemon juice|;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|oregano|dried;1 cup|chicken broth|;1 tsp|salt|;1/2 tsp|black pepper|;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 400°F.|Put the potatoes in a large roasting pan and add the olive oil, lemon juice, garlic, oregano, salt, and pepper. Toss well.|Pour the broth around the potatoes and spread them in a single layer.|Roast 60 to 70 minutes, turning once or twice, until the potatoes are golden and the liquid has been absorbed.|Sprinkle with parsley and a squeeze of lemon.","Greek"],
[3236,"Keftedes (Greek Meatballs)","comfort","🧆",45,"Easy",9,6,"Herby beef and mint meatballs, pan-fried and served with tzatziki and pita.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef|;1|onion|grated;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs|;1|eggs|;2 tbsp|mint|fresh, chopped;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tsp|oregano|;1 tsp|salt|;1/2 tsp|black pepper|;1/4 cup|flour|for dusting;1/3 cup|olive oil|for frying;4|pita|;1 cup|greek yogurt|for serving","Mix the beef, onion, garlic, breadcrumbs, egg, mint, parsley, oregano, salt, and pepper until just combined.|Chill 15 minutes, then roll into about 24 balls and dust lightly with flour.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat.|Fry the meatballs in batches 8 to 10 minutes, turning, until browned and cooked through at 160°F.|Serve with warm pita and yogurt or tzatziki.","Greek"],
[3237,"Marry Me Chicken","comfort","💍",35,"Easy",9,4,"Seared chicken in a creamy sun-dried tomato and parmesan sauce.","2|chicken breast|sliced into 4 cutlets;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1 tsp|paprika|;2 tbsp|olive oil|;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|sun-dried tomatoes|chopped;3/4 cup|chicken broth|;3/4 cup|heavy cream|;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes|;2 tbsp|basil|chopped","Season the chicken with salt, pepper, and paprika.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Sear the chicken 4 minutes per side until golden. Remove to a plate.|Lower the heat to medium and cook the garlic and sun-dried tomatoes 1 minute.|Add the broth, cream, parmesan, Italian seasoning, and red pepper flakes. Simmer 4 to 5 minutes until slightly thickened.|Return the chicken to the sauce and simmer 5 minutes until cooked to 165°F.|Top with basil and serve with pasta, rice, or bread.","American"],
[3238,"Tuscan Chicken","comfort","🍗",35,"Easy",9,4,"Pan-seared chicken in a creamy garlic sauce with spinach and sun-dried tomatoes.","2|chicken breast|sliced into 4 cutlets;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|olive oil|;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|sun-dried tomatoes|chopped;1/2 cup|chicken broth|;1 cup|heavy cream|;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;3 cup|spinach|","Season the chicken with salt and pepper.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and cook the chicken 5 minutes per side until golden and 165°F. Remove to a plate.|Add the garlic and sun-dried tomatoes to the pan for 1 minute.|Pour in the broth and cream, add the parmesan and Italian seasoning, and simmer 4 to 5 minutes until thickened.|Stir in the spinach until wilted, about 2 minutes.|Return the chicken and spoon the sauce over it. Serve with pasta or mashed potatoes.","Italian"],
[3239,"Chicken Cordon Bleu","comfort","🧀",55,"Medium",9,4,"Chicken breast rolled around ham and Swiss, breaded and baked until crisp.","4|chicken breast|small, or 2 large halved;4 slice|deli ham|thin;4 slice|swiss cheese|;1/2 cup|flour|;2|eggs|beaten;1 cup|panko|;1/4 cup|parmesan|grated;1 tsp|garlic powder|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;3 tbsp|butter|melted;1 tbsp|dijon mustard|","Heat the oven to 400°F. Butterfly each chicken breast and pound to 1/4 inch thick. Season with salt and pepper.|Spread a little Dijon on each, lay ham and Swiss on top, roll up tightly, and secure with toothpicks.|Dredge in flour, dip in egg, and coat in panko mixed with parmesan and garlic powder.|Place seam-side down on a lined baking sheet and drizzle with the melted butter.|Bake 30 to 35 minutes until golden and 165°F inside. Rest 5 minutes and remove the toothpicks.","French"],
[3240,"Lemon Herb Roast Chicken","comfort","🍋",105,"Easy",9,6,"Whole roast chicken with crisp golden skin, lemon, garlic and herbs.","4 lb|whole chicken|patted very dry;4 tbsp|butter|softened;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|fresh thyme|chopped;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1|lemon|zested, then halved;1 1/2 tsp|salt|;1 tsp|black pepper|;1|onion|quartered;1 lb|baby potatoes|halved;3|carrots|cut in chunks","Heat the oven to 425°F. Mix the butter, garlic, thyme, parsley, lemon zest, salt, and pepper.|Loosen the skin over the breast and rub half the herb butter underneath. Rub the rest all over the outside.|Stuff the cavity with the lemon halves and onion. Tie the legs together.|Scatter the potatoes and carrots in a roasting pan and set the chicken on top, breast side up.|Roast 1 hour 10 minutes to 1 hour 25 minutes until the thickest part of the thigh reaches 165°F.|Rest 15 minutes before carving.","American"],
[3241,"Honey Mustard Chicken","quick","🍯",35,"Very easy",8.5,4,"Baked chicken thighs glazed with a tangy honey Dijon sauce.","2 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in skin-on;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/4 cup|honey|;1/4 cup|dijon mustard|;2 tbsp|mustard|whole grain;2 tbsp|olive oil|;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|paprika|;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 425°F. Pat the chicken dry and season with salt and pepper.|Whisk the honey, Dijon, whole grain mustard, olive oil, garlic, and paprika.|Toss the chicken in half of the sauce and place skin-side up in a baking dish.|Bake 25 to 30 minutes until 175°F, brushing with the remaining sauce for the last 5 minutes.|Garnish with parsley.","American"],
[3242,"Chicken Alfredo Bake","comfort","🧀",50,"Easy",9,6,"Penne and chicken in creamy Alfredo sauce, topped with melted mozzarella.","1 lb|penne|;2 tbsp|butter|;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|flour|;2 cup|heavy cream|;1 cup|milk|;1 1/2 cup|parmesan|grated, divided;3 cup|rotisserie chicken|shredded;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/4 tsp|nutmeg|;1 1/2 cup|mozzarella|shredded;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 375°F. Boil the penne 2 minutes short of al dente and drain.|Melt the butter in a large pot and cook the garlic 30 seconds. Whisk in the flour for 1 minute.|Slowly add the cream and milk, whisking, and simmer 4 minutes until thickened.|Stir in 1 cup parmesan, salt, pepper, and nutmeg until smooth.|Fold in the penne and chicken and transfer to a 9x13 dish.|Top with the mozzarella and remaining parmesan. Bake 20 to 25 minutes until bubbly and golden. Top with parsley.","Italian"],
[3243,"Bang Bang Chicken","quick","🌶️",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Crispy chicken bites tossed in a creamy, sweet and spicy bang bang sauce.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in 1 inch cubes;1/2 cup|cornstarch|;1 tsp|garlic powder|;1 tsp|paprika|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/3 cup|vegetable oil|;1/3 cup|mayonnaise|;1/3 cup|sweet chili sauce|;1 tbsp|sriracha|;1 tbsp|honey|;2|green onion|sliced;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Toss the chicken with the cornstarch, garlic powder, paprika, salt, and pepper until well coated.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Fry the chicken in batches 5 to 6 minutes until golden and crisp, then drain on paper towels.|Whisk the mayonnaise, sweet chili sauce, sriracha, and honey in a large bowl.|Toss the hot chicken in the sauce to coat.|Serve over rice topped with green onion.","American"],
[3244,"Chicken Tortellini Bake","comfort","🍝",40,"Very easy",9,6,"Cheese tortellini and chicken baked in marinara with plenty of melted mozzarella.","20 oz|tortellini|refrigerated cheese;2 cup|rotisserie chicken|shredded;2 cup|marinara sauce|;1/2 cup|heavy cream|;2 cup|spinach|;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 1/2 cup|mozzarella|shredded;1/4 cup|parmesan|grated;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 375°F. Boil the tortellini 2 minutes less than the package says and drain.|In a large bowl mix the marinara, cream, garlic, Italian seasoning, and salt.|Stir in the tortellini, chicken, and spinach and pour into a 9x13 dish.|Top with the mozzarella and parmesan.|Cover with foil and bake 15 minutes, then uncover and bake 10 minutes until bubbly and golden.","Italian"],
[3245,"Zuppa Toscana","soup","🥣",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"Creamy Italian sausage soup with potatoes, kale and bacon.","1 lb|italian sausage|mild or hot, casings removed;4 slice|bacon|chopped;1|onion|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes|;6 cup|chicken broth|;1 1/2 lb|russet potatoes|sliced 1/4 inch thick;1 bunch|kale|stemmed and chopped;1 cup|heavy cream|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the sausage in a large pot over medium-high heat, breaking it up, about 7 minutes. Move to a bowl.|Cook the bacon in the same pot until crisp. Remove, leaving about 2 tablespoons of fat.|Cook the onion 5 minutes, then add the garlic and red pepper flakes for 1 minute.|Add the broth and potatoes and simmer 15 minutes until tender.|Return the sausage and add the kale and cream. Simmer 5 minutes.|Season with salt and pepper and top with the bacon.","Italian"],
[3246,"Cabbage Roll Soup","soup","🥬",55,"Easy",9.5,8,"All the flavor of stuffed cabbage in a hearty tomato soup with beef and rice.","1 lb|ground beef|;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1|cabbage|small head, chopped about 6 cups;1 can|diced tomatoes|28 oz;1 can|tomato sauce|15 oz;4 cup|beef broth|;1 tbsp|worcestershire|;1 tsp|paprika|;1 tbsp|brown sugar|;1 cup|rice|cooked;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the beef and onion in a large pot over medium-high heat 8 minutes. Drain excess fat.|Add the garlic and cook 1 minute.|Add the cabbage, tomatoes, tomato sauce, broth, Worcestershire, paprika, and brown sugar.|Bring to a boil, then simmer 30 minutes until the cabbage is very tender.|Stir in the cooked rice and heat through. Season with salt and pepper.","American"],
[3247,"Beef Chili","soup","🌶️",75,"Easy",9.5,8,"Classic thick beef and bean chili with tomatoes and warm spices.","2 lb|ground beef|;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|chili powder|;2 tsp|cumin|;1 tsp|paprika|;1 tsp|oregano|;1 can|diced tomatoes|28 oz;1 can|tomato sauce|15 oz;2 tbsp|tomato paste|;1 can|kidney beans|15 oz, drained;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;1 cup|beef broth|;|salt|to taste;|sour cream|for serving, to taste;|cheddar|shredded, for serving, to taste","Brown the beef with the onion and bell pepper in a large pot over medium-high heat 8 to 10 minutes. Drain excess fat.|Add the garlic, chili powder, cumin, paprika, and oregano and stir 1 minute.|Stir in the tomato paste, diced tomatoes, tomato sauce, and broth.|Bring to a boil, then simmer partly covered 45 minutes, stirring now and then.|Add the beans and simmer 15 minutes more. Season with salt.|Serve topped with cheddar and sour cream.","American"],
[3248,"Pasta e Fagioli","soup","🥣",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"Rustic Italian soup of small pasta and white beans in a tomato broth.","2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;4 cup|chicken broth|;2 can|cannellini beans|15 oz each, drained;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;1 cup|pasta shells|small, or ditalini;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated","Heat the oil in a large pot and cook the onion, carrot, and celery 7 minutes.|Add the garlic and Italian seasoning for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, broth, and 1 can of beans. Mash the other can of beans and add it to thicken the soup.|Bring to a simmer, stir in the pasta, and cook 8 to 10 minutes until tender.|Season with salt and pepper and serve topped with parmesan.","Italian"],
[3249,"Stracciatella Soup","soup","🥣",25,"Easy",9.5,4,"Italian egg drop soup with parmesan and spinach in clear chicken broth.","6 cup|chicken broth|;3|eggs|;1/3 cup|parmesan|grated;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1/8 tsp|nutmeg|;3 cup|spinach|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Bring the broth to a gentle simmer in a medium pot.|Whisk the eggs with the parmesan, parsley, and nutmeg.|Add the spinach to the broth and cook 1 minute.|Slowly pour the egg mixture into the simmering broth while stirring in one direction so it forms thin ribbons.|Cook 1 to 2 minutes, season with salt and pepper, and serve with extra parmesan.","Italian"],
[3250,"Hamburger Soup","soup","🍲",45,"Very easy",9.5,6,"Easy ground beef and vegetable soup in a savory tomato broth.","1 lb|ground beef|;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|sliced;2 stalk|celery|sliced;3 clove|garlic|minced;2|potatoes|diced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;4 cup|beef broth|;1 tbsp|tomato paste|;1 tbsp|worcestershire|;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;1 cup|frozen peas|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the beef with the onion in a large pot over medium-high heat 6 to 8 minutes. Drain excess fat.|Add the carrots, celery, and garlic and cook 3 minutes.|Stir in the potatoes, tomatoes, broth, tomato paste, Worcestershire, and Italian seasoning.|Bring to a boil, cover, and simmer 20 minutes until the potatoes are tender.|Add the peas, cook 3 minutes, and season with salt and pepper.","American"],
[3251,"Chicken Pot Pie Soup","soup","🥧",40,"Easy",9.5,6,"Creamy chicken and vegetable soup with all the flavor of pot pie, topped with biscuit crumbs.","4 tbsp|butter|;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/3 cup|flour|;4 cup|chicken broth|;1 cup|milk|;1 lb|potatoes|diced small;3 cup|rotisserie chicken|shredded;1 cup|frozen peas|;1 tsp|dried thyme|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;4|refrigerated biscuits|baked and crumbled","Melt the butter in a large pot and cook the onion, carrot, and celery 6 minutes. Add the garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the flour and cook 1 minute.|Slowly whisk in the broth and milk. Add the potatoes and thyme and simmer 15 minutes until tender.|Add the chicken and peas and cook 5 minutes.|Season with salt and pepper and serve topped with crumbled biscuits.","American"],
[3252,"Cheeseburger Soup","soup","🍔",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"Creamy potato soup with ground beef and melted cheddar.","1 lb|ground beef|;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|butter|;3 tbsp|flour|;3 cup|beef broth|;1 lb|potatoes|diced small;2 cup|milk|;2 cup|cheddar|shredded;1 tbsp|worcestershire|;1 tbsp|ketchup|;1 tbsp|mustard|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;|pickles|chopped, for topping, to taste","Brown the beef and onion in a large pot 7 minutes. Drain excess fat and add the garlic for 1 minute.|Move the beef to a bowl. Melt the butter in the pot and whisk in the flour for 1 minute.|Slowly whisk in the broth, add the potatoes, and simmer 15 minutes until tender.|Add the milk, return the beef, and stir in the Worcestershire, ketchup, and mustard. Heat gently without boiling.|Stir in the cheddar a handful at a time until melted. Season and top with pickles.","American"]];
